{'job_title_name': '(NEW) Master Thesis: Identification and evaluation of Circular Economy KPIs for H2 engines', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'FEV Group GmbH', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Fev-Group-Gmbh?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhactghnjkv5800&fromjk=5ea97a5825de1cf5', 'city': 'Deutschland', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 3, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=5ea97a5825de1cf5&bb=8C0QK9jhA3fZuBJxrZJ4LUYBBoHjJA6FGH6KjBK7od9ChVtK-OSdwzKMuW_7gh8F&xkcb=SoCl67M3HqR8wN2YCJ0ObzkdCdPP&fccid=f16e2a68426e925d&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=20', 'job_description': 'Reference Number: CON-GER-STU-MA\n(NEW) Master Thesis: Identification and evaluation of Circular Economy KPIs for H2 engines\nLocation:\nGermany, Aachen; Germany, Cologne; Germany, Munich\nWorktime:\nFull-time\nWhat we do - And why!\nFEV Consulting is the FEV Group\'s technology-driven top management consultancy. We act as a guide between strategy development and product realization in today\'s global environment. We do not simply work for companies, but for our customers - people who want to move society forward. That\'s why we develop and optimize technical product concepts with our focus on customer benefit, feasibility, sustainability and profitability.\nWork together with us on challenging projects from different areas of the mobility, transportation and energy sectors.\nSample topics include: sustainable vehicle and mobility concepts, business transformations to maintain future viability, coupling the energy and transportation sectors, digital services, and business development for innovation.\nYOUR ROLE\nThe goal is to develop a Cost/ CO2 and circularity KPIs for a H2 engine (based on BOM). The evaluation should include research on the state of the art in science, industry and @ FEV on H2 engine manufacturing and rating of technologies by cost, CO2 and circularity. Develop an approach/ methodology to evaluate the differences conventional engines and H2 Engines considering multiple variables.\nYOUR PROFILE\nYou are completing your master\'s degree in industrial engineering, mechanical engineering, electrical engineering, computer science, business administration, economics or a comparable course of study at a leading university\nYou have exceptional academic performance and impress us with your personal profile\nYou ideally gained inital practical experience in consulting or a technical industry, favorable also with AI tools\nYou have very good analytical skills\nYou are a motivated and committed team player\nYou have very good knowledge of MS Office applications\nYou communicate very well in English, and you are ideally fluent in the local office language - both verbally and in writing\nWhat we offer\nBe part of a great team\nWe owe our success to our international and diverse team. Become a valuable member and foster strong cohesion!\nExpand your network\nJoin our Stammtisch company dinners - even as an alumnus or alumna! In addition, we inform our students about current customer projects and other internal company activities at our regular "Student Call"\nGet the best out of yourself\nFeedback is a reality at our company. Your personal mentor is at your side to promote your strengths! Continuously expand your horizons with our internal training opportunities. Our team of consultants will be happy to share their expertise and experience with you.\nDiverse career prospects\nWith us, anything is possible: gain practical experience in consulting alongside the theory in your studies. Do your internship with us. Write your thesis on an exciting project. Or go abroad with us! Plan your start at FEV Consulting, like many talented people before you.\nSina Aumann\nFEV Consulting GmbH\nPhone: +49 160 746 3685', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 38, 4, 710829), 'c