{'job_title_name': 'Customer Success Manager (f/m/d) - German-speaking, Berlin-based', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'NORNORM', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Nornorm?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhactjvqk6ot803&fromjk=fe0f0d212987fcb6', 'city': 'Berlin', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 3, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=fe0f0d212987fcb6&bb=JzSom5XrBcBwYMxu5yHgFJgbO-YQ6a0G-IZa8-ufT9jFfjE64-GnDWz5kMPjNwAa&xkcb=SoDz67M3HqR8wC2YCJ0IbzkdCdPP&fccid=cd8d7d6bd1227a91&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=20', 'job_description': 'Join us in revolutionising the office furniture industry!\nAt NORNORM, we have embarked on an incredible mission to reinvent workspaces with circularity at the core. Our vision is to integrate sustainable practices into the workplace of the future, showcasing the benefits it brings to individuals, design, business operations, and the environment.\nHow we\'ll make it happen:\nOur innovative and fully integrated service encompasses every aspect of workspace design, installation, layout adaptation, as well as the repair and replacement of our exceptional "better-than-new" pieces. We ensure that workspaces continuously maximise their impact without compromising the benefits they provide to people, businesses, or the planet.\nWho we are:\nNORNORM is not just any scale-up; we have the support of a major player in the furnishing industry and backing from growth equity investment firms. We are pioneering a sustainable, subscription-based solution for furnishing future workplaces and have already begun rolling out our services across Europe. With offices in Copenhagen, Amsterdam, Stockholm, Berlin, and London, we are expanding rapidly.\nWe are seeking:\nAmbitious and adaptable individuals who are eager to grow with us and unafraid to push the boundaries of their capabilities. In return, we offer a dynamic and fast-paced environment where taking initiative and embracing risks is not only encouraged but also supported. Join us on this exciting journey of growth and innovation!\nThe role\nWe are looking for a full-time Customer Success Manager (f/m/d) who can strengthen our CS team in Berlin. You will be a vital part of our global Customer Success team and the main point of contact for our customers in Germany!\nYour main responsibilities include:\nPrimary customer contact throughout the full customer lifetime cycle\nProactively solving problems and creating customer value\nBuilding relationships & nurturing NORNORM ambassadors\nEnsuring a smooth onboarding (explaining how NORNORM works)\nConducting customer check-ins, workshops and site visits\nProviding advice on and improving customers\' workspace experience\nMulti-level stakeholder management (office managers, sponsors, coworkers)\nManaging customer data on our CRM platform\nTracking and improving of customer health\nPreventing churn and driving upsell\nYou will also be expected to:\nManage several projects simultaneously and prioritise accordingly\nIdentify improvements in our ways of working\nTravel to our customers throughout Germany (~3 overnight stays per month)\nOccasional travels to our other locations (Netherlands, Denmark, Sweden)\nYou bring the following qualifications:\nWe imagine that you have about 2 years of relevant experience. You are willing to work in a startup with a fast-paced environment and use your problem-solving skills when facing challenges. In addition, we value the following qualifications and competencies:\nOutgoing personality with a customer-centric mindset\nProactiveness and ability to build meaningful relationships\nCommercial thinking and good business judgment\nNative or near-native level German speaker\n(mandatory)\n, fluent in English\nPrevious experience in the field of customer success\nBased in Berlin or willing to relocate\nA can-do mentality, persistence and a positive attitude\nA high moral compass and a strong sense of ownership\nExcellent communication skills\nPractical understanding of office space drawing and measurements\nInterest in office space design and circular business models is a plus\nExperience in the Real Estate sector is a plus\nWhat we offer you:\nAt NORNORM, we operate as a resourceful and innovative scale-up, prioritising a fulfilling and inspiring work environment. We are dedicated to providing a rewarding experience for our team. Here\'s what you can expect:\nEarly Responsibility: From day one, you\'ll have meaningful responsibilities, shaping our company\'s future and making a real impact.\nFlexible Working: We support work-life balance with flexible hours and hybrid work options to accommodate personal commitments.\nCollaborative Environment: Join a diverse team of serial entrepreneurs, furnishing industry experts, designers, logistics specialists and consultants, fostering continuous learning and growth.\nErgonomic Workspace: Your comfort is important to us. We provide ergonomic furniture for a healthy and productive work environment.\nCompetitive compensation: Your compensation package includes a free subscription to NORNORM home office furniture.\nOpen Communication: We value your ideas and encourage open collaboration among team members.\nPositive Culture: Our corporate values, "We care, we dare, we do, we make simple easy," shape our open and down-to-earth company culture.\nWork-Life Balance: Enjoy a reasonable amount of vacation days to recharge and spend quality time with loved ones.\nGrowth Opportunities: Join us on our growth journey, with abundant chances for personal and professional advancement.\nDon\'t miss out on the opportunity to be part of NORNORM\'s groundbreaking approach to office furniture, where sustainability and forward-thinking come together. Apply now and become a catalyst for change in the workplace of the future!\nDepartment\nCustomer Success & Fulfillment\nLocations\nBerlin\nContact Nikolas Hartlieb Customer Success Manager - Germany – Customer Success & Fulfillment\nBerlin', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 38, 8, 417810), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
