{'job_title_name': '(Senior) Sourcing Specialist (m/f/d) - Raw Materials', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'LyondellBasell Industries', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Lyondellbasell?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhactmtsikpf800&fromjk=a2a3b05e820093ae', 'city': '50389 Wesseling', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 4, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=a2a3b05e820093ae&bb=pgimYnTHDnAuUM-m9WrLzEm_E1g4i5AGfKcsKOq7iiAu-MUaQ1hJMECCNsNhDQ15&xkcb=SoDZ67M3HqR-JmgMiL0CbzkdCdPP&fccid=5938580c9c7de4d3&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=30', 'job_description': 'Location: Wesseling, Nrth Rhine Westfalia, DE, 50389\nReq ID: 84482\nFacility: Wesseling-501\nDepartment: EU Additives\nDivision: Olefins and Polyolefins and Global Procu\nAre you result oriented and willing to challenge the status quo? Welcome to LyondellBasell!\nFor our largest European production site in\nRotterdam or Wesseling near Cologne\n, we are looking for a\n(Senior) Sourcing Specialist (\nm/f/d) - Raw Materials\nResponsibilities & Accountabilities\nExecutes strategic sourcing following the agreed processes and sourcing strategy methodology for the assigned commodities with increasing complexity and high value\nUnderstands strategies for assigned segments or commodities and proactively drives initiatives to meet sourcing objectives\nDrives productivity opportunities with supply base to deliver value to the business\nEnsures high ethical and financial control compliance standards are met by the organization\nMaximizes revenue share and controls cost by responding to audits, surveys, or other information requests from internal and external sources\nAnswers inquiries requiring interpretation of policies and contributes to a strong governance culture by complying with appropriate governance policies and procedures\nWorks collaboratively with the Buyers in the implementation of strategic sourcing initiatives\nDevelops and composes bid specification in such a manner that internal customer needs are addressed\nDemonstrates courage and has the initiative to challenge inefficiencies, process deviations, and strategy deviations\nUnderstands strategies for assigned commodities and proactively drives initiatives to meet sourcing objectives\nAssesses supplier capabilities thru KPI analysis and makes recommendations on supplier acceptability\nIdentifies and qualifies new suppliers as required\nQualifications\nBachelors degree (Masters degree preferred) or equivalent combination of education and experience\n3+ years of chemical or related industry experience and knowledge related to purchasing and materials management is preferred.\nExperience in Business related positions required\nStrong communication skills and ability to work in a global team\nExcellent written and oral communication skills in English\nKnowledge in MS-Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and SAP and ARIBA-skills\nWhat makes us attractive\nAttractive remuneration with a thirteenth monthly salary\nGlobal bonus program\nVarious work schedules and mobile working\n30 days vacation and other free time options\nAdditional Long-term care insurance (CareFlex)\nEmployer-funded pension\nUrban Sports Club Membership\nCompany medical department including physio practice at the site\nOn-site canteen\nEmployee discounts\nInterested ?\nRegister your CV and apply via our online portal by clicking on the “apply” button. Please feel free to contact our Talent Acquisition Team at karriere@lyondellbasell.com for more details.\n#LI-HF1\nLyondellBasell\n(NYSE: LYB): As a leader in the global chemical industry, LyondellBasell strives every day to be the safest, best operated and most valued company in our industry. The company’s products, materials and technologies are advancing sustainable solutions for food safety, access to clean water, healthcare and fuel efficiency in more than 100 international markets. LyondellBasell places high priority on diversity, equity and inclusion and is\nAdvancing Good\nwith an emphasis on our planet, the communities where we operate and our future workforce. The company takes great pride in its world-class technology and customer focus. LyondellBasell has stepped up its circularity and climate ambitions and actions to address the global challenges of plastic waste and decarbonization. In 2022, LyondellBasell was named as one of FORTUNE Magazine\'s "World\'s Most Admired Companies" for the fifth consecutive year. For more information, please visit www.lyondellbasell.com or follow @LyondellBasell on LinkedIn.', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 38, 11, 280704), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
