{'job_title_name': 'PROJECT ENGINEER FOR SUSTAINABILITY CONSULTING & DESIGN FOR SUSTAINABILITY', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Forward Engineering GmbH', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Forward-Engineering-Gmbh?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhactnkpjksj800&fromjk=73fb4bc607fd061f', 'city': '80797 München', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 4, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=73fb4bc607fd061f&bb=pgimYnTHDnCro8IEDIjKvhzfllxGLtJVNN-LnK34KI1ZWX5g1_tuWM_IIFFHOIkz&xkcb=SoAZ67M3HqR-JmgMiL0PbzkdCdPP&fccid=ae01e8b4223414a7&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=30', 'job_description': 'Forward Engineering (FE) is a trusted partner for holistic and sustainable product development. The global FE team supports our client partners with comprehensive design, material and process know-how in the field of technical and fiber-reinforced polymers, functional lightweight construction and CAE-supported multi-material design optimization. Bringing together our global network of material manufacturers, technology providers and tier suppliers enables the resource efficient and cost-effective implementation of new and emerging technologies.\nTasks\nPlanning, support and implementation of development projects from the concept phase to series application in the areas of Design for Recycling, Design for Sustainability, Design for Circularity\nImplementation of sustainability assessments over several product life cycles to derive strategies in product and sustainability roadmap development\nGlobal material and technology scouting\nClose cooperation and coordination with internal and external project teams, technology partners, institutes and suppliers worldwide\nSustainability consulting and implementation of sustainable business transformations\nPresentation of the project results in the project team and at customer presentations\nRequirements\nSuccessfully completed degree programs (Dipl.-Ing., M. Sc., M. Eng.) in mechanical- or industrial engineering specializing in product development, plastics technology, sustainable resource management, vehicle design, aerospace or a comparable qualification.\nIndustrial experience in the areas of life cycle assessment (LCA), vehicle and/ or plastics technology is an advantage\nExcellent material know-how and its application in product development\nGoal- and solution-oriented with strong communication skills and know how to motivate your project team\nFluent in English and German\nFlexibility, willingness to travel and interested in international projects\nExperienced and comfortable with presenting to groups both at an introductory as well as deep dive technical expert level\nBenefits\nResponsible tasks in an innovative environment\nGreat conditions in an open-minded, collegial team\nA flat, project oriented and responsive organizational structure able to respond quickly to customer and market requirements\nIndividual, attractive opportunities for your development in a growing business\nWe are looking forward to your comprehensive application.', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 38, 12, 190515), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
