{'job_title_name': 'Technology & Innovation Manager (m/f/d)', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Tomra', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Tomra?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhactv64j30g800&fromjk=bc000282bcd8f0d1', 'city': ' 56218 Mülheim-Kärlich', 'remote': 'Zum Teil im Homeoffice', 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 24, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=bc000282bcd8f0d1&bb=H5xcOQ2MyjqFtYfzqKJW2LUyA9wyHJ2h_mHkepu40iVV0wBPepEkbgaHwnjVaGVHgIqUY1jT_6eZGNYbb7uSlDp3eI3HNKV4CFmnYRsX57M%3D&xkcb=SoDd67M3HqR-e2AwoD0ObzkdCdPP&fccid=94844d1fef46eb96&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=230', 'job_description': 'Company Description\nTOMRA has a fantastic story to tell. We are a world-leading technology company working with almost 5000 employees to expand the circular economy and contribute to a more sustainable future. Why is it worthwhile to start and stay at TOMRA? Quite simply, we are a steadily growing international company that has retained its family atmosphere. Our corporate culture is Norwegian, which means there is no hierarchical thinking. If you are interested in titles and hierarchy, you are at the wrong place here. We see a bright future in economic terms. Aside from that, it´s nice to know that our recycling machines are helping to make the world cleaner.\nOur customers have a wide variety of backgrounds and so do we. We like to hire people from all walks of life. It’s not just the right thing to do, but it also makes TOMRA stronger. And we’ll have to be strong to save the world.\nBelonging to the TOMRA Recycling division, the business model of our new start-up venture TOMRA Feedstock is to buy mixed plastic waste from incinerators and operate own plastic grading / sorting plants that turn the mixed plastic into a sellable feedstock stream for recyclers.\nJob Description\nWe are looking for a\nTechnology & Innovation Manager (m/f/d)\nwithin TOMRA Recycling / Feedstock who will ensure that our plastic grading / sorting plants are operated by cutting edge technology and innovates processes constantly.\nOur new\nTechnology & Innovation Manager (m/f/d)\nwill work together with the rest of the team, to frequently design new material processing concepts and commercialize the recycling of waste streams, that would otherwise go to incineration. A profound understanding of the specifics of plastic waste and its circularity is therefore crucial, along with feeling comfortable at waste processing plants and being in contact with technology partners to bring the concepts into life.\nThe Position requires readiness to travel of approximately 30%, having the ability to work remotely the rest of the time.\nResponsibilities of the Technology & Innovation Manager (m/f/d):\nDesigning & engineering of material processing concepts for pre-sorting & splitting plants\nDeveloping new potential recycling applications and making proposals for commercializing new streams\nTesting and evaluation of new equipment & technology solutions\nSuccessfully leading contract negotiations to secure best equipment at best price\nConsulting in- and externally with regards to technical expertise\nEvaluating processed materials incl. chemical analysis\nQualifications\n5+ years of working experience in a similar role in technical consulting, preferably in a sorting / grading plant\nProfound understanding of recycling processes and specifics of plastic waste\nStrong communication skills, being able to make complex technical processes understandable to non-technical stakeholders and adapting per target group, being fluent in English with German and / or another European language as a plus\nCreative and innovative personality, thinking outside of the box to develop new approaches to circularity\nEducational background\nA technical university degree, preferably in mechanical engineering, environmental engineering, process engineering or waste management\nAdditional business / commercial knowledge being a plus\nOther skills / abilities\nThinking along and completing assigned tasks independently\nSolution-oriented team player with intercultural competence\nHigh mobility, readiness to travel to plants and business partners on a frequent basis\nAdditional Information\nWhat else do we have to offer?\nA rewarding, unique and exciting position in a company focused on making a positive impact on the climate and making every resource count\nA high degree of personal responsibility and the opportunity to implement your own ideas\nIndividual personal development with many possibilities for growth within the different divisions and regions\nA great international and diverse team, who recognizes each individual and supports each other\nHybrid working & flexible working hours\nStaying healthy by using a job bike or joining Sport Clubs where we support the membership\nAre you interested?\nPlease send us\na motivation letter (indicating why you are a good match for this position),\nCV and\ndesired annual gross salary\nnotice Period (in weeks or months)\nCertificates from education and trainings\nPlease be aware that we only except digital applications – thank you!', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 38, 20, 366248), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
