{'job_title_name': 'Electrical Lead (gn) - Battery Design', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Voltfang GmbH', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Voltfang-Gmbh?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhacu07kikpf800&fromjk=8530ac1950b67601', 'city': ' 52062 Aachen', 'remote': 'Zum Teil im Homeoffice', 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 24, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=8530ac1950b67601&bb=H5xcOQ2MyjqFtYfzqKJW2EL4ZxQsWKSMYWzjydux6omMcpGeNEIdmrzY2xYarPmN8mJl1fxZgn5RTTHiGW4h1hAxu01TOwaYT4h2vyzysoE%3D&xkcb=SoDn67M3HqR-e2AwoD0IbzkdCdPP&fccid=84fbb82a8aa48f95&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=230', 'job_description': "Your mission\nAs Electrical Lead for the development of battery storage systems you have the opportunity to work on innovative projects and contribute to the advancement of clean energy technologies. We are looking for a sparring partner who can take responsibility for the future direction of our battery system. If you have a passion for electronic design, experience as a lead engineer and a drive to deliver high quality solutions for battery storage systems while ensuring compliance with certifications and functional safety, we invite you to apply:\nWith your expertise, you will lead your team in the design and development of battery storage systems, considering factors such as functionality, efficiency, industry standards, safety regulations, reliability, EMC / EMI requirements and best practices in electronic design for battery storage systems\nClose cooperation with the other departments to ensure seamless integration of electronic systems into battery storage solutions\nConduct feasibility studies and evaluate electronic component options to select the most suitable components and technologies for battery storage applications\nConcept and review of printed circuit boards (PCBs) ltium, taking into account design rules, signal integrity, thermal management and manufacturability for battery storage systems\nSelection of test methods for verification and validation of electronic designs for battery storage applications\nYour profile\nDegree in electrical engineering, electronics or a related field\nExperience as a lead engineer or team lead in electronics design, ideally in the battery environment\nExperience in circuit design, PCB layout and system design is an advantage\nKnowledge of electronic components, analog and digital circuits, battery management systems (BMS) and signal integrity principles\nFamiliarity with industry standards and regulations in the field of electronic design, such as safety standards (e.g. IEC62619, functional safety), EMC/EMI requirements\nFluency in German or English\nWhy us?\nActive contribution to\nclimate protection & the circular economy\nFree use of the\nVelocities (e-bikes)\nin Aachen\nCooperation with\nUrban Sports Club\nSubsidy for the\njob ticket\nOffice Dog\nFlexible working hours\nand\nhybrid working\npossible\nModern office spac\ne with shopping facilities nearby\nAbout us\nOur mission: The sustainable power storage system - Be part of it!\nWe are a fast growing company that develops and produces sustainable electricity storage systems from qualified electric car batteries. In this way, we help manufacturing businesses and industry to become more environmentally friendly and less dependent on conventional energy sources. In this way, we can make a significant contribution to climate protection and take a decisive step towards a green future.\nWe rely on an experienced and motivated team that contributes its knowledge and skills to achieve our goals. Our corporate culture is characterised by cooperation and team spirit. Different departments all pull together in order to be able to look forward to a positive future together.\nWe strive for constant further development, which is why we are looking for employees who can contribute and take on responsibility in order to grow with us individually. We are not just any team - we are the Voltfam. Creativity, enthusiasm and fun play a decisive role for us.\nThat's why we are looking for talented employees who want to achieve long-term success together with us. If you feel addressed and would like to be part of an ambitious team, then get in touch with us!\nWe are looking forward to meet you,\nYour Voltfam.\nEnable a future worth living!\nEqual opportunities for all: We welcome applications from people who are as diverse as we are and our tasks - regardless of gender, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, ethnic origin and nationality or social background.\nDo you have any further questions? Then feel free to contact us at\njobs@voltfang.de\n!", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 38, 21, 69198), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
