ll draw expertise from around the organisation and amongst external partners. As such we are looking for someone with experience of operating across a range of sectors with the ability to bring actors together from disparate groups to form alliances and deliver on creative solutions.\nPosition:\nPrimary Responsibilities\nTake leadership of Battery Pass, Europe’s leading consortium project to advance the implementation of the EU Battery Passport\nCo-develop Systemiq program for Digital Project Passports and resilient digital supply chains across Europe and beyond\nLead a team of other System Change Leaders and support them to thrive in their work\nCo-create approaches with our partners/clients to overcome the perceived trade-offs between economic viability, ecosystem regeneration, and social inclusion and wellbeing\nBring data together in a consistent way and perform analyses based on agreed questions for insights\nDevelop long-lasting and collaborative relationships with project partners and stakeholders\nProvide strategic insights and develop practical solutions for successful transformations\nSupport these partners in monitoring, evaluating and communicating their business model, vision and impact\nCo-create a regenerative culture and work environment within Systemiq where people feel well and thrive\nRequirements:\nAbout You\nYou’re a people person.\nYou have outstanding interpersonal skills and you are comfortable managing mutli-stakeholder relationships, sometimes with conflicting priorities. You can quickly establish rapport, build trust, and demonstrate credibility and authority. You are a collaborative team player.\nWords matter.\nYou have excellent communication skills, whether in-person, virtually, or by email, and you value listening and solving others’ challenges.\nYou’re solution-oriented.\nYou can clearly explain issues, contribute to their resolution, and effectively influence and negotiate to achieve consensus and successful outcomes. You can anticipate needs, make reasoned decisions, and communicate them effectively.\nYou delight in the details.\nYou have advanced problem-solving and analytical skills, and apply your detail-oriented project management skills to ensure your team has the knowledge and support they need to deliver the global projects, products, and services.\nYou are humble.\nNo task is too small for anyone. You’re all about the team, not the individual.\nYou get it done.\nYou have a methodical approach to your work with a strong focus on accuracy, attention to detail, consistency, and superb quality. You take the initiative and can operate autonomously.\nYou are creative.\nYou look at new ways of working, utilising systems thinking. You persevere and you’re pragmatic. You have an entrepreneurial spirit with the ability to identify opportunities and new initiatives and to turn them into reality.\nYou are curious.\nYou keep professional knowledge, capabilities, and skills up to date and an open and continuous learning mindset. You have an interest to quickly dive into new topics.\nEssential Qualifications / Experience\nMaster\'s degree/equivalent or higher\nProven excellent skills in high-pace multi-project management\nDemonstrable knowledge in the fields of electric vehicles, batteries, charging solutions, metals and mining and/or government policy relating to these topics would be enormously helpful\n5+ years of experience in a professional system change environment (thought leadership/research, start-ups, advisory/consulting, strategy, investment), preferably in an international environment,\nAdvanced problem-solving and analytical skills,\nSkills and experience of relationship management on a senior level,\nBusiness international level of German and English, both written and verbal is essential\nOther information:\nApplications from current residents in the following cities will be considered:\nMunich / Berlin (Germany)\nDisclaimer:\nPlease ensure you are legally eligible to work/live in your location when applying for this role. Visa sponsorship or relocation costs will not be provided.\nDiversity & Inclusion\nWe believe that diversity and inclusion are at the heart of system change and the mission we have set ourselves. So we commit ourselves to:\nEmbedding diverse and inclusive ways of working\nfrom day to day. This includes recruitment, performance management, and people processes and policies.\nProviding a supportive environment\n. We want people to be themselves and be at their best, regardless of their background, personality, gender, sexual orientation, race, mental health, religion, or other characteristics.\nEnabling a long-term, sustainable approach\nto work and life more generally. We want to support our people at all stages of their lives – as parents or caregivers, through changing life circumstances – and to accommodate personal priorities where they matter most.\nReward and Recognition\nRemuneration and benefits package will reflect the successful candidates\' experience and country where hired.', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 38, 52, 221873), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
