{'job_title_name': 'Senior Backend Engineer (div/w/m)', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'score4more GmbH', 'company_indeed_url': None, 'city': ' 10115 Berlin', 'remote': 'Zum Teil im Homeoffice', 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 34, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=29e2d0824450c044&bb=p4HogV91IXgMRFsuOtmcMcRbC2AhgDN58FlDEKdelYXce5HkXoK0RgNWhjWU5jcwt4tumjPEyzI6xCRs905vzBwtI2Rd2iQ4nC9wZIvIvSw%3D&xkcb=SoAv67M3HqR1nZwSDx0CbzkdCdPP&fccid=dd616958bd9ddc12&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=330', 'job_description': 'score4more - The B2B Sustainability Impact Startup\nscore4more - The B2B Sustainability Impact Startup\nscore4more is a platform to boost sustainability in companies and entire industries. Against this backdrop, we are building a B2B platform powered by AI/ML for change agents and companies. On this platform we interconnect three data areas:\nCOMPANIES: We engineer the sustainability data of companies in a company profile and provide data analytics comparison on an industry-specific basis.\nSOLUTIONS: We make sustainable innovations visible and data-accessible. By profiling sustainable solutions with decision-relevant data, we drive technology and knowledge transfer at a global level.\nPEOPLE: We connect and support the change agents - those committed to collaborate in order to create sustainable transformation across companies\nTogether with Europe’s leading sustainability recognition, the German Sustainability Award, we have already over 1,000 companies active on the platform with more than 50.000 sustainable actions and solutions, as well as 40 GT of greenhouse gas emissions as data available. The score4more platform and community continues to grow every day searching for the greatest levers for sustainable transformation:\nJoin our team and help make the score4more vision a reality: we are changing the industry toward a sustainable economy by leveraging the power of data and machine learning.\nHOW YOU CREATE IMPACT\nAt score4more, you contribute with your brainpower and technology skills to:\ndevelop the largest global impact platform in order to shape a sustainable transformation\ncreate new features to make it easy for companies to navigate transformation data, identify suitable sustainable actions and solutions to transform faster\nautomate our scoring and data analytics to give companies an assessment about their sustainability performance\nPOSITION KEY FACTS\nRole: Senior Backend Engineer\nScope of the position: full time\nWorking location: remote, hybrid and/or from our Berlin office,\nmain residency: germany (means you should have your main residency in germany, but you can work remotely)\nStarting date: January 2024 - permanent contract\nCompensation: we have a transparent team compensation and benefits system in which we classify you according to your professional experience - an adjustment/evaluation will take place after the 6-month probationary period\nVacation: 26 vacation days\nYOUR TASKS\nAs our first internal Backend Engineer you have the possibility to shape the score4more platform and work towards deploying the first Features. You will be involved in overall processes of the company, such as strategies and shaping the product in order to boost sustainability and therefore transform the economy towards a regenerative system.\nYour tasks as our first Backend Developer will be:\nBackend Development: Design, develop, and maintain robust, scalable, and high-performance backend systems using best practices and modern technologies.\nAPI Development: Create and maintain APIs that enable data flow between the front-end and backend systems, ensuring efficiency and security.\nDatabase Management: Design and optimize database schemas, implement data storage solutions, and ensure data integrity and security.\nCode Quality: Write clean, well-documented, and maintainable code, and participate in code reviews to maintain code quality standards.\nPerformance Optimization: Identify and address bottlenecks and performance issues in the backend systems to ensure a responsive and efficient user experience.\nSecurity: Implement and maintain security best practices to protect against common web application vulnerabilities.\nCollaboration: Work closely with teams to understand business requirements and translate them into technical solutions.\nTechnical Research: Stay updated on emerging technologies, industry trends, and best practices to ensure the continuous improvement of our backend systems.\nYOUR QUALIFICATIONS\nWhat you bring - "must have":\nMaster degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n7 years + proven experience as a Backend Engineer or similar role.\nInitial project leadership experiences, mentoring younger developers, managing projects, ambitions to coordinate tech roles\nStrong proficiency in one or more programming languages, Python is a must have\nExperience with database design and management (SQL, NoSQL).\nKnowledge of RESTful API design and development.\nFamiliarity with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, GCP).\nKnowledge of version control systems (e.g., Git).\nYou work collaboratively with your colleagues and consider what is best for the team. Diversity and inclusion are important to you.\nYou have start-up experience, preferably early stage, and have already built structures and developed strategies from scratch.\nThe following language skills are a prerequisite: excellent English.\nWhat you bring - "nice to have":\nExperiences in AI and machine learning model development\nUnderstanding of containerization and orchestration technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).\nYou are an impact-oriented person who wants to work with hand, heart and head for sustainable change.\nLeadership: Serving leadership and self-organization and their frameworks are familiar to you and you are keen to embark on this journey with us.\nWe encourage you to apply even if you do not meet all the requirements and have less experience than described. It is important to us that you are motivated, a quick learner and that you can work autonomously while familiarizing yourself with processes. We value a hands-on mentality, encourage continuous learning and help each other grow as a team every day.\nOUR TECH STACK\nWe are using latest technologies and an AI/ML-ready scalable tech stack:\nReact, TypeScript on the frontend\nCypress & Jest\nPython\nServerless architecture\nAWS Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB, Aurora (Postgresql), Cognito, S3\nGPT3 (Initial models)\nscore4more is a close partner of the Hasso-Plattner-Institute Potsdam as one of the leading technology institutes to collaborate on AI/ML.\nICING ON THE CAKE (BENEFITS)\nFlexibility in terms of working hours and location:\nHybrid Working from home, from our offices in Berlin and Potsdam or in other parts of Europe. We make sure that you are well equipped wherever you are.\nHome office: Equipment as required\nPersonal development:\nWith the help of peer reviews, we design your personal learning journey with you. Do you want to attend a conference or training? Go for it. Share the knowledge you\'ve learned with us.\nCultural events: Retreats, fun events, summer parties and hangouts.\nBenefits on top of your salary:\nGuud Card - We charge you €50 a month on a shopping card and you can use it to shop at sustainable retailers.\nContribution to a pension scheme - if you don\'t already have one, we\'ll be happy to suggest one for you.\nYou get virtual shares in score4more that increase in value every year - another way we help you become part of the company and provide for your future.\nOUR CULTURE\nOur six core values are the basis of our actions. We practice the share-commons principle with open and shared knowledge and work in a self-organized way.\nImpact & Integrity: We are honestly, sincerely and holistically committed to our vision and mission. Social impact is paramount and guides decision-making.\nTransparency & Trust: We build and maintain trusting relationships with each other. Our transparent work culture fosters trust. We value our contribution and the performance of those around us.\nFlow- & failure culture: We work according to the principle "better done than perfect" and dare to fail. Every day is a potential day for flow and ideas.\nWE FOSTER DIVERSITY\nscore4more recognizes the importance of diversity not only as a social obligation, but also as a valuable resource for our success. Diversity spans gender, ethnicity, culture, sexual orientation, age, skills and much more. It brings different perspectives, experiences and ways of thinking. By seeing diversity as a core value at score4more, we not only create a dynamic and innovative work environment, but also a positive impact on society. Every individual contributes to our collective success. Recognising and valuing differences leads to a positive change in the way we work and the way we see the world.\nAPPLY NOW\nApply now and become part of the score4more team. Send us your application documents (CV and motivation letter) via the application form. Please indicate your availability (start date and hours) in your application. Please refrain from submitting application photos and information on date of birth and marital status.\nAbout us\nWe want future generations to grow up in a sustainable world: climate neutral, circular, inclusive and fair with regenerated ecosystems. Join us to shape a future-proof planet together.', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 38, 59, 601655), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
