{'job_title_name': 'Analytics Director', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'SYSTEMIQ', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Systemiq?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhacvalk2bbt000&fromjk=17931329dab955d7', 'city': '81671 München', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 34, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=17931329dab955d7&bb=p4HogV91IXgMRFsuOtmcMQhf_zerbCmQAsij8DjEDK8WUGDar0Vg4EPNM7oH7z8F0rNdZ-dxyVr9FZ-BpzOVuiLWQL4nP0yQjS-WC_ooD3w%3D&xkcb=SoBI67M3HqR1nZwSDx0KbzkdCdPP&fccid=2d4f8512d54326dc&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=330', 'job_description': 'SYSTEMIQ was set up in 2016 to drive the implementation of the Paris Agreement and the UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) by transforming markets and business models in three key economic systems: land use, materials and energy. By addressing failures in these systems, SYSTEMIQ aims to unlock economic opportunities that benefit business, society and the environment.\nWe do this through five activities:\nConvene and support coalitions of leaders to shape policies and business strategies that will rapidly transform economic activity;\nWork with companies that want to be pioneers in and drivers of change towards more sustainable systems;\nCo-create and incubate the market solutions most likely to build regenerative economic systems\nInvest our own venture capital and expertise in opportunities with the biggest potential to drive rapid system change;\nDirect larger pools of capital into regenerative economic systems, enabling them to scale and multiply.\nSYSTEMIQ is an equal opportunities employer. SYSTEMIQ’s recruitment and selection policy ensures the best possible skill mix of colleagues and the highest quality candidates are appointed using objective job-related criteria.\nIn order to deliver in these areas, we recruit and develop distinctive and varied individuals who strive to achieve our mission, challenge the status quo and act as change leaders.\nPosition:\nWorld-class analytics is not sufficient to drive true system-level change, but it is a necessary ingredient. As we scale, SYSTEMIQ builds out a robust and distinctive analytical capability and offering.\nSYSTEMIQ has already had big successes in the area of analytics, as shown in our work in the Mission Possible Partnership, Breaking the Plastic Wave, Plastic IQ, PlastSimulator, among several others. We are now looking to scale and further professionalise these analytical capabilities into one central Analytics Hub.\nThe SYSTEMIQ Analytics Hub has four objectives:\nTo be a driving force and catalyst of SYSTEMIQ’s mission through powerful analytics and tools.\nTo make a significant contribution to SYSTEMIQ’s impact and economic success, while working collaboratively and supporting the objectives of other SYSTEMIQ platforms (energy, materials, nature) and impact vehicles. It is a revenue-centre, not a cost-centre.\nTo create consistency and excellence in our analytical work by being the professional authority of anything analytics within SYSTEMIQ, also enhancing our ability to attract talent – like you, in this space.\nTo strengthen and amplify our existing IP efforts by carrying over learnings, insights and data from project to project.\nWe are looking for another Director to join our Analytics Hub, preferably via one of our European hubs to help oversee SYSTEMIQ’s analytical work-programme. Primarily this will be about developing system models (most notably around country and decarbonization and energy transition modelling). The successful candidate will be responsible for developing analyses which answer some of the most complex and challenging questions on the road to a net-zero or net-positive economy, and for using these insights to help build consensus on critical actions for the next decade. The work includes all facets of the analytics process; techniques, organization, internal education and hiring.\nThis is an exciting opportunity to define the analytics platform at a growing and ambitious consultancy. The candidate will be one of SYSTEMIQ’s go-to expert on everything analytics, leading a central team of 5-10 specialists, working closely with all platforms.\nThe successful candidate will have an appetite to grip the big picture and the systems-implications of our work on decarbonization, material flows, nature and planetary boundaries, while also understanding the details underpinning analytical work and advanced modelling skills required. The candidate will be proactive and able to deliver autonomously, taking ownership for the set up of the team and its strategy, whilst progressively building out and linking up models and modules.\nThis role will initially report to two of our partners (Eveline Speelman, co-lead Energy Platform and Amsterdam Office Manager and Yoni Shiran, partner Materials Platform based out of London).\nRequirements:\nGeneral\nEnergy Transition and/or Decarbonisation modelling is strongly preferred\nExcellent analytical and problem-solving skills –confident leading high-quality quantitative and qualitative analytics on a range of different topics\nProactive and self-starter, appetite for working autonomously in a fast-paced environment\nProven track-record leading and managing an analytical / project team: Structuring and prioritising a complex, multiple-faceted work programme, including for other team members\nConfident working with assertive, analytical, diverse group of colleagues, and ability to work as part of the international team.\nAlignment with SYSTEMIQ values (creativity, challenge, collaborate, change and care), and be able to demonstrate how they have lived these values in a professional setting\nTechnical\nSkilled modeller, with strong computer skills in information technology and programming (DBMS, python, php, Javascript, and excel) and surrounding data ecosystem\nWorking experience with different types of modelling techniques, and an in depth understanding of good data and modelling practices. Experience in creating and developing modelling solutions that can help to answer complex questions will be particularly valuable.\nUnderstanding of geospatial data analysis (GIS) and data visualization toolkits such as Tableau\nKnowledge of and experience with designing relatively complex, interdependent IT-systems and data management systems\nExperience working with version control and open source software\nQualifications:\nProficiency in English (both conversation and writing).\nUniversity degree or equivalent combination of education and experience in programming, data analytics, data science or related technical fields.\nMinimum 10 years of experience in analytics, modelling, data science or data engineering, plus work in a leadership/oversight role as part of this experience.\nDesirable:\nFamiliarity with climate change mitigation, greenhouse gas emission accounting, and circular economy principles.\nExperience creating, working with and developing climate and energy system models, including optimisation models and power system dispatch models.\nExperience in fundraising, proposal and bid writing\nExperience in advisory / strategy consultancy\nKnowledge in QGIS, ArcGIS (desktop and server), Spatial Analysis and Image Processing Software (e.g. QGIS Semi-automatic Classification Plugin (SCP), The Sentinel Toolbox, Geographic Resources Analysis Support System (GRASS), ENVI, etc.) as well as data management\nOther information:\nWe are keen to receive applications from all parts of the community.\nPlease send your application via our website. Any questions on the application process please feel free to email Barry Edwards at Barry.Edwards@systemiq.earth.\nYou must have the Right to Work in the location for the position you are applying for – SYSTEMIQ usually cannot provide sponsorship.', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 39, 4, 408546), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
