{'job_title_name': 'Internal Communications Manager', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'SYSTEMIQ', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Systemiq?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhacvcfkjjip800&fromjk=889db71611bf6807', 'city': 'Berlin', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 30, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=889db71611bf6807&bb=X57XTztzBvXnoBfC4Sx6dewlb6aJE0ldjicUZHqhqXovNyp0CXzcAxVbZU2GJakPzulCN1b_Y7U_sB9dKuQe--Fm-T2IpYgCfZDXpweA7dc%3D&xkcb=SoCo67M3HqRyi_Q8A50GbzkdCdPP&fccid=2d4f8512d54326dc&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=290', 'job_description': "Internal Communications Manager – Amsterdam, Berlin, Munich or Paris\nSYSTEMIQ is a systems change company that partners with business, finance, policy-makers, and civil society to make economic systems truly sustainable. We combine high-level research with high-impact, on-the-ground work.\nOur purpose is to catalyse good disruptions in critical economic systems, with a current focus that includes low-carbon energy, materials and the circular economy, and regenerative oceans and land use. These disruptions are not only vital to the future of humanity and our planet, they also open up immense opportunities for the businesses that drive them.\nSYSTEMIQ connects the right people, ideas, technologies and capital to transform economic systems:\n1. We convene and support coalitions of leaders to shape policies and business strategies that will rapidly transform economic activity\n2. We work with pioneering companies that want to drive the change in their industry\n3. We co-create and incubate the market solutions most likely to build regenerative economic systems\n4. We invest our own venture capital and expertise to accelerate business innovation and drive system change\n5. We direct larger pools of capital so that they are invested for long-term sustainability, and we work to accelerate the transformation to a greener, more inclusive financial system.\nIn order to deliver in these areas, we recruit and develop distinctive and varied individuals who strive to achieve our mission, challenge the status quo and act as change leaders.\nPosition:\nThe talent we need\nYou will be part of a growing global communications and engagement team and will work closely with Systemiq’s leadership, the CCO and the wider team to build out the internal communications capabilities for Systemiq. This position is the first of its kind and will play a critical role in driving change within our organisation.\nMore specifically, your tasks will include:\nDevelop and implement a comprehensive internal communications strategy that supports Systemiq’s mission, vision and strategic objectives.\nBuild strong relationships with Systemiq’s leadership team, understanding their communication needs and helping them articulate and cascade key messages throughout the organisation.\nProvide expertise in change management, helping the organisation adapt to evolving strategies, initiatives and industry shifts.\nIn close collaboration with various stakeholders, e.g. knowledge management and the People team, create compelling and relevant content for internal communications, including for the Systemiq townhalls, intranet updates, presentations and announcements.\nManage and optimise various internal communication channels, ensuring information is accessible and engaging for employees around the world.\nEstablish key performance indicators (KPIs) to measure the effective of internal communications efforts, gathering feedback from employees using insights to continuously improve communications strategies.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure consistent messaging and alignment across different departments and geographies.\nYou will leverage your international experience to ensure that communication strategies are culturally sensitive and effective in diverse regions.\nRequirements:\nMindset & experience we expect\nSYSTEMIQ is looking for individuals with a record of excellence and achievement. You have proven that you are able to manage difficult tasks under pressure and are keen to work in an entrepreneurial company where you can get involved in a variety of work. You are passionate about SYSTEMIQ's mission. Specifically, you have\nProven experience in internal communications, working for a global organisation, covering different markets.\nExtensive experience working on internal communications strategies, while ensuring its implementation.\nExtensive experience in working with complex content across a multitude of subjects and themes, in a global context.\nStrong understanding of change management principles.\nAbility to navigate complex organisational structures and issues.\nStrategic thinker with the ability to translate organisational objectives into actionable communication plans.\nProficiency in using communication tools and platforms.\nPrevious experience in having worked as part of a broader team.\nExceptional written and verbal communication skills.\nFull fluency in English, (writing and speaking) and ideally fluence in French, German or Portuguese.\nHigh attention to detail along with excellent communication skills at all levels.\nA pro-active and organised mindset with an ability to multi-task and prioritise busy workloads efficiently.\nA team attitude - you pitch in when required.\nDemonstrated ability to work collaboratively and build strong relationships with leadership and colleagues.\nAn extremely flexible, collaborative work style with a desire to succeed.\nA calm and well organised nature that can deal with stress, ambiguity and changing circumstances.\nOther information:\nDisclaimer:\nPlease ensure you are legally eligible to work/live in your location when applying for this role. Visa sponsorship or relocation costs will not be provided.\nDiversity & Inclusion\nWe believe that diversity and inclusion are at the heart of system change and the mission we have set ourselves. So we commit ourselves to:\nEmbedding diverse and inclusive ways of working\nfrom day to day. This includes recruitment, performance management, and people processes and policies.\nProviding a supportive environment\n. We want people to be themselves and be at their best, regardless of their background, personality, gender, sexual orientation, race, mental health, religion, or other characteristics.\nEnabling a long-term, sustainable approach\nto work and life more generally. We want to support our people at all stages of their lives – as parents or caregivers, through changing life circumstances – and to accommodate personal priorities where they matter most", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 39, 6, 21550), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
