{'job_title_name': 'Dev Ops Engineer (All genders)', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Circunomics', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Circunomics?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhacvrmmjkuq800&fromjk=9df092938bba7dbc', 'city': '60311 Frankfurt am Main', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 28, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=9df092938bba7dbc&bb=Te2tRdv7piRkNf6n9FXw2pa-tqYITqC4twYwm3Ps90n-9_7ax1c8KIlb17ZVtZ0-&xkcb=SoB867M3HqRytqR8V50LbzkdCdPP&fccid=402bfc79b8bb7a33&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=270', 'job_description': 'Your mission\nSince it was founded in 2019, Circunomics has been pursuing a circular battery economy. Circunomics is the first IoT platform for reusing and recycling electric vehicles and energy storage batteries. We build circularity into every battery by creating digital lifecycle identities, running analytics, and enabling intelligent matching of used EV battery supply and second-life energy storage requirements via our Circular Marketplace for a genuinely green e-mobility and energy transition.\nYour profile\nYou will\nResponsible for our platform\'s quality, stability, security, and automatization\nActively participate in agile team\'s projects and focus on providing a highly available platform for our customers\nPlan, configuration, monitor, maintenance, and ongoing optimization of our CI/CD pipelines (GitHub Enterprise) and the associated tooling to integrate our external APIs and services. "You build it; you run it!"\nManage the application, infrastructure performance, and monitoring for continuous improvement\nIterate fast where needed with architect competently for long-term scalability\nTest coverage and enable continuous excellent delivery\nManage, write and maintain well-crafted documentation\nYou have\n3+ years of professional experience as a DevOps/Software Engineer\nExperience in software development projects in an agile environment, incl. service management, container orchestration (e.g., Kubernetes), and standard infrastructure-as-code tools, especially Terraform\nIn-depth knowledge of Microsoft Azure services, Azure Monitor & Policies, Linux, standard Unix tools, Ansible, or Salt stack\nWorking knowledge of monitoring, logging, alerting, and other aspects of application operations\nDesign continuous integration/delivery pipelines using GitHub actions, CircleCI or Jenkins\nExperience working as part of a remote team, sharing ideas, good communication skills, and presenting concepts effectively\nEnergetic and proactive attitude about improving the work with little supervision\nPublished software that enhances the user experience\nGood command of English and German is a plus\n\\_\\_Bonus points for\nAzure Certifications\nExperience with programming and scripting languages, especially PHP and Python\nUnderstanding of SQL database design and modeling\nWhy us?\nFlexible hours and 28 days of annual vacation\nWork-from-home options\nLow hierarchies and open feedback culture\nModern offices located in the center of Frankfurt City\nEnglish as company language and international working environment\nAttractive development perspectives with creative freedom for growth\nShape the future circular battery space and the green energy transition\nAbout Us\nWe are interested in hearing from you to learn more about your professional focus and personal projects. You will shape the circular battery space by creating an analytics and marketplace platform that powers an ecosystem of car manufacturers, energy storage, remanufacturers, and recyclers.\nTo know more about Circunomics, go to:\nhttps://www.circunomics.com/\nKfW Award Gründen 2021 Sieger\nSAP and Google Cloud Announce Finalists in the Circular Economy 2030 Competition\nAccelerated by SAP.iO Foundry Paris\nCircunomics closes second seed round\nGerman AI Startup Landscape 2021\nDr. Peter Mertens about Circunomics\\_\\_', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 39, 21, 897561), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
