{'job_title_name': 'PhD Researcher (f/m/x) - Electrochemical conversion of greenhouse gases from manure to valuable products', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Helmholtz-Zentrum für Umweltforschung UFZ', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Helmholtz--zentrum-F%C3%BCr-Umweltforschung-Ufz?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhacvt9p2gra001&fromjk=e23711ee9c3ad7e2', 'city': 'Leipzig', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 28, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=e23711ee9c3ad7e2&bb=zkFaOEXK9pFn4we8qxGaIyarVHteXxbWHBgdzF_qg7OzzZGw13Kuk6VSOomvY_0E&xkcb=SoA567M3HqRytrR8V50MbzkdCdPP&fccid=c69648529d489af8&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=270', 'job_description': 'Place of work\nLeipzig\nWorking time\n65 % (25,35 h / week)\nContract limitations\nlimited contract / 36 months\nSalary\nRemuneration according to the TVöD public-sector up to pay grade EG 13 including attractive public-sector social security benefits.\nContact\nYour contact for any questions you may have about the job:\nDr. Paniz Izadi\npaniz.izadi@ufz.de\nThe UFZ\nThe Helmholtz Centre for Environmental Research (UFZ) with its 1,100 employees has gained an excellent reputation as an international competence centre for environmental sciences. We are part of the largest scientific organisation in Germany, the Helmholtz association. Our mission: Our research seeks to find a balance between social development and the long-term protection of our natural resources.\nThe job\nThe UFZ offers four PhD positions in the framework of the PhD college “Coupling circular economy principles with environmental hazard management for liquid manure-based sustainable agriculture- SmartManure”. The aim of SmartManure is to address on-farm manure management from storage to land application, combining aspects of circular economy with sustainable agriculture, and develop technical solutions based on the joint research within the PhD college (see https://www.ufz.de/Smartmanure for more information).\nYour tasks\nLiquid manure produces significant amounts of the greenhouse gases CH4 and CO2 during storage on farms. Converting these into value-added chemicals will benefit the environment and contribute to circular economic goals. In this SmartManure subproject, we will develop an electrochemical system for the conversion of released CO2 to valuable chemicals and energy carriers particularly methanol.\nYour tasks include:\ndiscovering efficient catalysts for electrochemical conversion of CO2 to methanol,\nestablishing an electrochemical platform for reducing CO2 to allow on-farm liquid manure storage,\nexperimental validation and engineering of electrochemical CO2 reduction to methanol at biocompatible conditions,\nset-up, validation and conduction of methods and protocols needed for the development of process lines and integration,\ntransfer to technical lab scale and assessment of system parameters through early-stage life cycle assessment,\nmethod development and use of physical and chemical analysis, especially HPLC and GC,\nparticipate in the UFZ graduate school HIGRADE with options for targeted training\ncollaborate with all other PhD candidates of SmartManure\nproviding high quality scientific outputs in the form of journal publications and assisting technology transfer.\nWe offer\nExcellent technical facilities which are without parallel\nThe freedom you need to bridge the difficult gap between basic research and close to being ready for application\nWork in inter-disciplinary, multinational teams\nExcellent links with national and international research networks\nExcellent support and optimal subject-specific and general training with our HIGRADE graduate school\nYour profile\nMaster’s degree in Chemistry, Bioengineering, Chemical engineering, Environmental Sciences or related fields,\nExperience in process development is advantageous,\nReadiness for intensive material and process development,\nHigh motivation and team player skills are expected,\nExcellent communication skills (English required),\nAbility to work independently and motivated to work in an interdisciplinary team.\nAdditional skills are of added value:\nPreference will be given to people highly interested in electrochemistry,\nSkills in software and data evaluation,\nHigh degree of organisation and teamwork skills,\nKnowledge in basic laboratory analysis.\nApplication deadline: 31.01.2024\nDiversity and Inclusion\nThe UFZ has a strong commitment to\ndiversity\nand actively supports\nequal opportunities\nfor all employees regardless of their origin, religion, ideology, disability, age or sexual identity.\nWe look forward to applications from people who are open-minded and enjoy working in diverse teams.\nImportant\nPlease submit your application via our online portal with your cover letter, CV (please omit your\nphoto\n, age, or marital status) and relevant attachments.\nContact\nYour contact for any questions you may have about the job:\nDr. Paniz Izadi\npaniz.izadi@ufz.de\nMore information about jobs at the UFZ:\nwww.ufz.de/career', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 39, 23, 220489), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
