{'job_title_name': 'PhD Researcher (f/m/x) - Intercropping for mitigating manure-based hazards in agriculture', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Helmholtz-Zentrum für Umweltforschung UFZ', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Helmholtz--zentrum-F%C3%BCr-Umweltforschung-Ufz?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad01q92gra000&fromjk=a01139fb9532eca4', 'city': '06120 Halle (Saale)', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 29, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=a01139fb9532eca4&bb=2DYqV2cLi75OFhrbUZIwuSoKMDzMF5VAV6ZgwZYEbX7BCnlQ2ABc5C9d_0JioeFR&xkcb=SoC167M3HqRyujADBD0KbzkdCdPP&fccid=c69648529d489af8&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=280', 'job_description': 'Place of work\nHalle (Saale)\nWorking time\n65 % (25,35 h / week)\nContract limitations\nlimited contract / 36 months\nSalary\nRemuneration according to the TVöD public-sector up to pay grade EG 13 including attractive public-sector social security benefits.\nContact\nYour contact for any questions you may have about the job:\nDr. Thomas Reitz\nthomas.reitz@ufz.de\nThe UFZ\nThe Helmholtz Centre for Environmental Research (UFZ) with its 1,100 employees has gained an excellent reputation as an international competence centre for environmental sciences. We are part of the largest scientific organisation in Germany, the Helmholtz association. Our mission: Our research seeks to find a balance between social development and the long-term protection of our natural resources.\nThe job\nThe UFZ offers four PhD positions in the framework of the PhD college “Coupling circular economy principles with environmental hazard management for liquid manure-based sustainable agriculture- SmartManure”. The aim of SmartManure is to address on-farm manure management from storage to land application, combining aspects of circular economy with sustainable agriculture, and develop technical solutions based on the joint research within the PhD college (see https://www.ufz.de/Smartmanure\nfor more information).\nYour tasks\nGiven recent declines in agricultural output as a result of monocropping and climate change, agriculture is turning more towards manuring, polycropping and targeted use of cover crops. In this SmartManure subproject you will investigate whether benefits arising from the aforementioned management strategies go beyond nutrient management and extend to contaminant management.\nYour tasks are:\nto design and conduct pot and field trials\nto track antibiotics, antibiotic resistance genes and heavy metals in the rhizosphere of different varieties of corn, sunflower and clover\nto quantify antibiotics and heavy metal accumulation in plant tissues\nto determine root growth and development of corn/sunflower/clover - intercropping systems\nto assess crop yield, quality and nutrition status\nto analyze and statistically evaluate data\nto participate in the UFZ graduate school HIGRADE with options for targeted training\nto publish the results (peer-reviewed papers, national and international conferences)\nto collaborate with all other PhD candidates of SmartManure\nto interact with stakeholders such as farmers and agencies\nWe offer\nExcellent technical facilities which are without parallel\nThe freedom you need to bridge the difficult gap between basic research and close to being ready for application\nWork in inter-disciplinary, multinational teams\nExcellent links with national and international research networks\nExcellent support and optimal subject-specific and general training with our HIGRADE graduate school\nYour profile\nMaster’s degree in Biology, Soil Science, Chemistry, Environmental Sciences or related natural sciences,\nReadiness for intensive field work,\nHigh degree of organisation,\nHigh motivation and teamplayer skills are expected,\nExcellent communication skills (English required),\nAbility to work independently and motivated to work in an interdisciplinary team.\nAdditional skills are of added value:\nKnowledge in plant sciences is advantageous,\nA driver’s license to drive in Germany,\nSkills in IT and data evaluation,\nKnowledge in basic laboratory analysis.\nApplication deadline: 31.01.2024\nDiversity and Inclusion\nThe UFZ has a strong commitment to\ndiversity\nand actively supports\nequal opportunities\nfor all employees regardless of their origin, religion, ideology, disability, age or sexual identity.\nWe look forward to applications from people who are open-minded and enjoy working in diverse teams.\nImportant\nPlease submit your application via our online portal with your cover letter, CV (please omit your\nphoto\n, age, or marital status) and relevant attachments.\nContact\nYour contact for any questions you may have about the job:\nDr. Thomas Reitz\nthomas.reitz@ufz.de\nMore information about jobs at the UFZ:\nwww.ufz.de/career', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 39, 27, 932765), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
