{'job_title_name': 'Senior Frontend Developer (all genders)', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Circunomics', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Circunomics?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad033dipbb801&fromjk=a000a47d0c42ca00', 'city': '60311 Frankfurt am Main', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 29, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=a000a47d0c42ca00&bb=LlNT0-P3geuamoLHwnZZWFK5DGNwMDODqUAT40s697-HnRqlYAkskZDI60IRd5K7&xkcb=SoBx67M3HqRyuggDBD0JbzkdCdPP&fccid=402bfc79b8bb7a33&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=280', 'job_description': 'Your mission\nSince founded in 2019, Circunomics has been pursuing a circular battery economy. Circunomics is the first analytics-based marketplace for reusing and recycling electric vehicle batteries. We are driving the circularity of batteries by providing analytics, predicting the performance in various reuse applications, and facilitating secure trading of used EV battery supply that match specific second life energy storage requirements via our Circular Marketplace.\nWe are enabling circular batteries for a truly green e-mobility and energy transition.\nYour profile\nYou will\nDevelop our analytics-based marketplace using Angular\nContinuously maintain, develop and extend our existing component library (Storybook)\nWork in an agile interdisciplinary team with our product managers, UX designers, and backend developers\nDevelop and integrate E2E tests according to test definitions\nProvide a robust application with high-test coverage (unit tests)\nContinuously maintain and sustain technical documentation\nYou have\nDegree in computer science or a similar technical field\n5+ years of architecting and implementing scalable, multi-component User Interface experience\nProficiency in key web technologies: JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML, CSS\nSeveral years of experience with Angular, D3.js (or similar charting engine), JavaScript Unit Testing (Jasmine, Karma), CSS, and SASS.\nSolid understanding of RESTful API design and implementation\nGood communication and management skills\nExperience working as part of a remote team, sharing ideas, and presenting concepts effectively\nMotivated and proactive attitude about improving the work\nExperience with software releases\nGood command of English and German is a plus\n\\_\\_Bonus points for\nAzure Certifications\nExperience with backend technologies and IaaS\nAbility to implement UX analytics to analyze user activity on a website or app that provides insights into how its design can be adapted to meet the current or changing needs of end users\nWhy us?\nFlexible hours and 28 days of annual vacation\nWork-from-home options\nLow hierarchies and open feedback culture\nModern offices located in the center of Frankfurt City\nEnglish as company language and international working environment\nAttractive development perspectives with creative freedom for growth\nShape the future circular battery space and the green energy transition\nAbout Us\nWe are interested in hearing from you to learn more about your professional focus and personal projects. Please send your CV to jobs@circunomics.com.\nYou will shape the circular battery space by creating an analytics and marketplace platform that powers an ecosystem of car manufacturers, energy storage, remanufacturers, and recyclers.\nTo know more about Circunomics, go to:\nhttps://www.circunomics.com/\nKfW Award Gründen 2021 Sieger\nSAP and Google Cloud Announce Finalists in the Circular Economy 2030 Competition\nAccelerated by SAP.iO Foundry Paris\nCircunomics closes the second seed round\nGerman AI Startup Landscape 2021\nDr. Peter Mertens about Circunomics\\_\\_', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 39, 29, 118254), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
