{'job_title_name': 'PhD Researcher (f/m/x) - Managing soil microbiomes for sustainable agriculture', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Helmholtz-Zentrum für Umweltforschung UFZ', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Helmholtz--zentrum-F%C3%BCr-Umweltforschung-Ufz?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad07l5jqun804&fromjk=94d5ea9d45042826', 'city': 'Leipzig', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 30, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=94d5ea9d45042826&bb=X57XTztzBvXnoBfC4Sx6deu9TuG9DG_0dqu8lFzmbvN3C2TixuGzL9vkaAaH5e1JigDV0nIzJU2RIVla-e_eBtqgzEgSfc9LZpXh1NR6QBU%3D&xkcb=SoB767M3HqRyi_Q8A50PbzkdCdPP&fccid=c69648529d489af8&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=290', 'job_description': "Place of work\nLeipzig\nWorking time\n65 % (25,35 h / week)\nContract limitations\nlimited contract / 36 months\nSalary\nRemuneration according to the TVöD public-sector up to pay grade EG 13 including attractive public-sector social security benefits.\nContact\nYour contact for any questions you may have about the job:\nDr. Anja Worrich\nanja.worrich@ufz.de\nThe UFZ\nThe Helmholtz Centre for Environmental Research (UFZ) with its 1,100 employees has gained an excellent reputation as an international competence centre for environmental sciences. We are part of the largest scientific organisation in Germany, the Helmholtz association. Our mission: Our research seeks to find a balance between social development and the long-term protection of our natural resources.\nThe job\nThe UFZ offers four PhD positions in the framework of the PhD college “Coupling circular economy principles with environmental hazard management for liquid manure-based sustainable agriculture- SmartManure”. The aim of SmartManure is to address on-farm manure management from storage to land application, combining aspects of circular economy with sustainable agriculture, and develop technical solutions based on the joint research within the PhD college (see https://www.ufz.de/Smartmanure for more information).\nYour tasks\nIntensive crop production in agriculture contributes to a decline in soil microbial diversity, which is crucial for soil health and food safety as it acts as insurance against stressors. In this subproject of SmartManure you will identify suitable cover crops that stimulate the soil microbiome to become more resilient to manure-related hazards, while improving nutrient retention from applied manure.\nYour tasks will be to:\nDesign and conduct pot experiments and field trials with different cover crops.\nAnalyze shifts in microbial diversity and composition in the soils.\nTrack antibiotics, antibiotic resistance genes and heavy metals in the soils.\nDetermine nutrient retention from manure and changes in nitrate leaching and greenhouse gas emission.\nAnalyze and statistically evaluate data.\nParticipate in the UFZ graduate school HIGRADE with options for targeted training.\nPublish the results (peer-reviewed papers, national and international conferences).\nCollaborate with all other PhD candidates of SmartManure.\nInteract with stakeholders such as farmers and agencies.\nWe offer\nExcellent technical facilities which are without parallel\nThe freedom you need to bridge the difficult gap between basic research and close to being ready for application\nWork in inter-disciplinary, multinational teams\nExcellent links with national and international research networks\nExcellent support and optimal subject-specific and general training with our HIGRADE graduate school\nYour profile\nMaster's degree in Microbiology, Biochemistry, Biology, Environmental Science or a related field\nReadiness for intensive field work\nSkills in data evaluation (e.g. R)\nHigh motivation and teamplayer skills are expected\nExcellent communication skills (English required)\nAbility to work independently and motivated to work in an interdisciplinary team\nAdditional skills are of added value\nPreference will be given to people highly interested in soil microbiology and molecular biology\nDriving licence in Germany\nExperience in microbial community analysis\nKnowledge of plant-based research and conducting greenhouse and field trials\nApplication deadline: 31.01.2024\nDiversity and Inclusion\nThe UFZ has a strong commitment to\ndiversity\nand actively supports\nequal opportunities\nfor all employees regardless of their origin, religion, ideology, disability, age or sexual identity.\nWe look forward to applications from people who are open-minded and enjoy working in diverse teams.\nImportant\nPlease submit your application via our online portal with your cover letter, CV (please omit your\nphoto\n, age, or marital status) and relevant attachments.\nContact\nYour contact for any questions you may have about the job:\nDr. Anja Worrich\nanja.worrich@ufz.de\nMore information about jobs at the UFZ:\nwww.ufz.de/career", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 39, 33, 928570), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
