{'job_title_name': 'PhD Researcher (f/m/x) - Developing a bioelectrochemical process for degrading antibiotics and recovering heavy metals from manure', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Helmholtz-Zentrum für Umweltforschung UFZ', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Helmholtz--zentrum-F%C3%BCr-Umweltforschung-Ufz?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad08kfjkvk805&fromjk=6adb8d53048c636e', 'city': 'Leipzig', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 30, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=6adb8d53048c636e&bb=X57XTztzBvXnoBfC4Sx6dbX3x3b3978g8NRD5h1lJBJvit8DUxjzH7IK3YRr3S80Zs6p9YG9n74-rjA8Zb6mvakKDF7A3C4uKKiL5Zl_f6o%3D&xkcb=SoBo67M3HqRyi_Q8A50LbzkdCdPP&fccid=c69648529d489af8&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=290', 'job_description': 'Place of work\nLeipzig\nWorking time\n65 % (25,35 h / week)\nContract limitations\nlimited contract / 36 months\nSalary\nRemuneration according to the TVöD public-sector up to pay grade EG 13 including attractive public-sector social security benefits.\nContact\nYour contact for any questions you may have about the job:\nQiuguo Fu\nqiuguo.fu@ufz.de\nThe UFZ\nThe Helmholtz Centre for Environmental Research (UFZ) with its 1,100 employees has gained an excellent reputation as an international competence centre for environmental sciences. We are part of the largest scientific organisation in Germany, the Helmholtz association. Our mission: Our research seeks to find a balance between social development and the long-term protection of our natural resources.\nThe job\nThe UFZ offers four PhD positions in the framework of the PhD college “Coupling circular economy principles with environmental hazard management for liquid manure-based sustainable agriculture- SmartManure”. The aim of SmartManure is to address on-farm manure management from storage to land application, combining aspects of circular economy with sustainable agriculture, and develop technical solutions based on the joint research within the PhD college (see https://www.ufz.de/Smartmanure for more information).\nYour tasks\nThe intensive use of manure as fertilizer can lead to heavy metal and antibiotics accumulation in soils. Consequently, methods and processes need to be developed to selectively extract heavy metals and remove antibiotics from manure during its storage to obtain safe fertilizers. In this SmartManure subproject, a two-stage process will be devised that combines electrosorption and microbial electrochemistry for simultaneously recovering heavy metals and degrading antibiotics during on-site manure storage.\nYour tasks are:\nto devise a reactor that combines electrosorption and microbial electrochemistry,\nto benchmark the developed prototype with a synthetic medium,\nto adapt the reactor and process parameters to allow treatment of real manure,\nto develop analytical methods to quantify removal of heavy metals and antibiotics and further identify transformation byproducts of antibiotics,\nto analyze and statistically evaluate data,\nto participate in the UFZ graduate school HIGRADE with options for targeted training,\nto publish the results (peer-reviewed papers, national and international conferences),\nto collaborate with all other PhD candidates of SmartManure,\nto interact with stakeholders such as farmers and agencies.\nWe offer\nExcellent technical facilities which are without parallel\nThe freedom you need to bridge the difficult gap between basic research and close to being ready for application\nWork in inter-disciplinary, multinational teams\nExcellent links with national and international research networks\nExcellent support and optimal subject-specific and general training with our HIGRADE graduate school\nYour profile\nMaster degree or equivalent in biochemistry, biotechnology, electrochemistry, process engineering, or related natural sciences,\nKnowledge and laboratory skills in basic electrochemical methods and analytical chemistry are advantageous,\nExperimental creativity and hands-on problem-solving attitude is a prerequisite,\nStrong self-motivation for independent scientific work in an interdisciplinary project and high reliability and resilience are required,\nProficient in English speaking and writing,\nExcellent communication and teamwork skills\nAdditional skills are of added value:\nExperience with electrosorption and analytical methods (HPLC-HRMS/MS),\nSkills in bioreactor benchmarking.\nApplication deadline: 31.01.2024\nDiversity and Inclusion\nThe UFZ has a strong commitment to\ndiversity\nand actively supports\nequal opportunities\nfor all employees regardless of their origin, religion, ideology, disability, age or sexual identity.\nWe look forward to applications from people who are open-minded and enjoy working in diverse teams.\nImportant\nPlease submit your application via our online portal with your cover letter, CV (please omit your\nphoto\n, age, or marital status) and relevant attachments.\nContact\nYour contact for any questions you may have about the job:\nQiuguo Fu\nqiuguo.fu@ufz.de\nMore information about jobs at the UFZ:\nwww.ufz.de/career', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 39, 34, 880455), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
