{'job_title_name': 'Senior electrical engineer (gn) - Battery system development', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Voltfang GmbH', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Voltfang-Gmbh?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad0dtujksj800&fromjk=adf581c25adc89e4', 'city': ' 52062 Aachen', 'remote': 'Zum Teil im Homeoffice', 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 22, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=adf581c25adc89e4&bb=6uO9H_gxWCD-lPxaBY6YY9RtNFEKUCJI2sLtoU2uN_XajPMpZ_nSLReb-gewruw5&xkcb=SoCf67M3HqSOlN2eC50KbzkdCdPP&fccid=84fbb82a8aa48f95&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=210', 'job_description': "Your mission\nJoining our team as an Electronic Design Engineer for Battery Storage System Development offers an exciting opportunity to work on innovative projects and contribute to the advancement of clean energy technologies. If you have a passion for electronic design, a keen eye for detail, and a drive to deliver high-quality solutions in battery storage systems while ensuring certification and functional safety compliance, we invite you to apply and become a valued member of our team.\nDesign and develop systems for battery storage systems, considering factors such as functionality, efficiency, safety and reliability\nCollaborate closely with battery engineers, mechanical engineers and software engineers to ensure seamless integration of electronic systems into battery storage solutions\nConduct feasibility studies and evaluate electronic component options to select the most suitable components and technologies for battery storage applications\nDesign and layout of printed circuit boards (PCBs) with Altium, considering design rules, signal integrity, thermal management and manufacturability for battery storage systems\nSupport prototype builds, perform testing and troubleshooting and provide guidance to technicians during the development / validation phases of battery storage systems\nConduct design reviews and participate in the selection of test methodologies to verify and validate electronic designs for battery storage applications\nEnsure compliance with relevant industry standards, regulations and best practices in electronic design for battery storage systems, such as functional safety standards, EMC/EMI requirements\nYour profile\nDegree in electrical engineering, electronics or a related field\nExperience in electronic design, including circuit design, PCB layout and system design\nKnowledge of creating circuit diagrams and designing PCB layouts with CAD software (e.g. Altium Designer, Eagle) is an advantage\nKnowledge of electronic components, analog and digital circuits, battery management systems (BMS) and signal integrity principles\nFamiliarity with industry standards and regulations in electronic design such as safety standards (e.g. IEC62619, Functional Safety) and EMC/EMI requirements\nProficiency in using lab equipment for testing and debugging electronic circuits and systems\nWhy us?\nActive contribution to\nclimate protection & the circular economy\nFree use of the\nVelocities (e-bikes)\nin Aachen\nCooperation with\nUrban Sports Club\nSubsidy for the\njob ticket\nOffice Dog\nFlexible working hours\nand\nhybrid working\npossible\nModern office spac\ne with shopping facilities nearby\nAbout us\nOur mission: The sustainable power storage system - Be part of it!\nWe are a fast growing company that develops and produces sustainable electricity storage systems from qualified electric car batteries. In this way, we help manufacturing businesses and industry to become more environmentally friendly and less dependent on conventional energy sources. In this way, we can make a significant contribution to climate protection and take a decisive step towards a green future.\nWe rely on an experienced and motivated team that contributes its knowledge and skills to achieve our goals. Our corporate culture is characterised by cooperation and team spirit. Different departments all pull together in order to be able to look forward to a positive future together.\nWe strive for constant further development, which is why we are looking for employees who can contribute and take on responsibility in order to grow with us individually. We are not just any team - we are the Voltfam. Creativity, enthusiasm and fun play a decisive role for us.\nThat's why we are looking for talented employees who want to achieve long-term success together with us. If you feel addressed and would like to be part of an ambitious team, then get in touch with us!\nWe are looking forward to meet you,\nYour Voltfam.\nEnable a future worth living!\nEqual opportunities for all: We welcome applications from people who are as diverse as we are and our tasks - regardless of gender, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, ethnic origin and nationality or social background.\nDo you have any further questions? Then feel free to contact us at\njobs@voltfang.de\n!", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 39, 40, 342883), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
