{'job_title_name': 'Process and Market Expert*', 'job_type': 'Festanstellung', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Tomra', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Tomra?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad0k0vj30g801&fromjk=89f9dbe303d76c5d', 'city': ' 56218 Mülheim-Kärlich', 'remote': 'Zum Teil im Homeoffice', 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 23, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=89f9dbe303d76c5d&bb=hdNyq8ipDnXJjN4_UKOeQamrcdbNVzWA47mEJiIg_ZeogpCXU7X_gnw7Xunfh8Ua&xkcb=SoC767M3HqSO5vWQ5B0NbzkdCdPP&fccid=94844d1fef46eb96&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=220', 'job_description': 'Company Description\nFULL TIME\nGermany, Mülheim-Kärlich\nToday, we are not utilizing resources in a sustainable way. In fact, the world is only 9% circular, meaning much of the Earth’s precious resources are only used once, leaving huge untapped potential for more sustainable resource management.\nTOMRA\nprovides cutting-edge sorting solutions for optimal resource productivity within the recycling, mining and food industries and is therefore uniquely positioned to shape the Circular Economy, creating demand for this way of thinking in the world. At TOMRA we want to be a thought leader, encouraging a more sustainable way of thinking and inspiring active change around the world.\nWith our deep application knowledge, powerful machine learning software and a variety of in-house developed sensors we offer our customers state-of-the-art, high-performance sorting solutions for maximum purity and yield.\nJob Description\nThe Process and Market Expert is in charge to develop best possible sorting and recycling technologies mainly to ensure materials getting closed loop recycled which today are not recycled. This includes technical and market knowledge combined with an understanding of cost structures. The Business Development Manager has knowledge within the waste and recycling market and knows technologies being used. Good internal and external communication skills are necessary in this position.\nIn this position you will be responsible to develop specific material recycling segments and applications (Solutions for materials, mainly plastics, today being not recycled) within Waste Sector\nwill consult customers and colleagues and develop new solutions within Collection, sorting and recycling of materials.\nwill be responsible to develop and support with the extension of existing material recycling segments.\nThe job in specific:\nYou are responsible for the development of the specific segment within TOMRA\nYou are involved in strategy processes, technology development , both from the technical and commercial point of view\nAnother task is internal and external consulting, which means that you develop concepts and solutions for customers and our internal colleagues\nYou develop markets and segment as a pioneer for material sorting and recycling\nYou analyze the performance of existing and new installations, both from a technical point of view and a financial point of view.\nConducting training for colleagues in different departments (Sales, project Management etc.) is also part of your responsibilities\nDevelopment of new applications in close cooperation with customers and colleagues for various materials\nSupport and active participation in conferences, congresses and exhibitions\nQualifications\nMechanical, chemical or process engineering education with a min. of 3 years working experience in waste sorting or material recycling business.\nGood understanding of waste and recycling markets, also of environmental legislation is of advantage\nPragmatism with understanding of the business.\nGood communication skills with customers and colleagues and cross-cultural competence are needed\nCreative and innovative – willing and able to question the status quo and develop new ideas and solutions\nUsed to work in an international context across Europe, USA, Asia.\nBeing flexible in regards to timing, location, targets, organizations.\nFluent in German and English language.\nAdditional Information\n30 days annual leave;\nSupported company pension scheme;\nSupported group accident insurance;\nHybrid working principles, flexible working hours;\nOpportunity to purchase TOMRA shares;\nEmployee benefit discounts for TOMRA Online Shop;\nCompany (e-) bike leasing;\nGym membership coverage support;\nOffice comfort: free parking spaces, canteen, coffee machines;\nCoaching opportunities - Individual Development Programs;\nNorwegian corporate culture (\nno hierarchical thinking, transparent communication culture\n).', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 39, 46, 541274), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
