{'job_title_name': 'Field Service Engineer - Wood (m/w/d)', 'job_type': 'Festanstellung', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Tomra', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Tomra?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad10c7ipbk800&fromjk=8e256a915fe34320', 'city': '56218 Mülheim-Kärlich', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 26, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=8e256a915fe34320&bb=FQpNUE2_UOTGKpC4sWIGGLnuZDHntRrUdQR834PRBAarskgdoF0DUTCAS2qyUUH7&xkcb=SoBP67M3HqSOxYxcA50DbzkdCdPP&fccid=94844d1fef46eb96&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=250', 'job_description': 'Unternehmensbeschreibung\nToday, we are not utilizing resources in a sustainable way. In fact, the world is only 9% circular, meaning much of the Earth’s precious resources are only used once, leaving huge untapped potential for more sustainable resource management. TOMRA provides cutting-edge solutions for optimal resource productivity within the recycling, mining and food industries and is therefore uniquely positioned to shape the Circular Economy, creating demand for this way of thinking in the world. At TOMRA we want to be a thought leader, encouraging a more sustainable way of thinking and inspiring active change around the world.\nStellenbeschreibung\nInstalling, commissioning, optimize, performance tests, maintain and repair of sensor-based sorters in TOMRA’s Recycling install base\nDelivering exceptional customer experiences through top class communication and support using various mediums\nOptimizing of the sorting systems / process by sample accounting and testing\nIdentifying opportunities to add value to our customers businesses through the introduction of complementary TOMRA products, solutions and services\nAct as a conduit between our customer base and HQ by providing in market feedback so that we continuously look for opportunities to further delight our customers\nQualifikationen\nVocational education and training (VET) in electricity or electronics / computer science / or similar\n2-3 years work experience in industrial environment\nIn-depth knowledge of electrical systems and troubleshooting\nBeing self-motivated and having the proven capacity to fully complete tasks\nAdvanced IT and network skills\nAffinity for computer programs, healthy logical understanding to understand contexts\nA certain talent for communication when dealing with people - in our case these are customers\nSocially outgoing, ability to handle stressful tasks\nFluent in verbal and written English\nWilling to travel for at least 80 % of the time, based on a flexible schedule\nFull clean driving license essential\nKnowledge of recycling processes is a plus\nZusätzliche Informationen\nPlease send us...\na motivation letter, indicating why you are interested in this position (in\nEnglish\n)\nCV (in\nEnglish\n)\nCertificates (from university, trainings, testimonials, referrals, etc)\nContact: Sabine Petolowski', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 39, 59, 165558), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
