{'job_title_name': 'IT Systems Administrator', 'job_type': 'Festanstellung', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Tomra', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Tomra?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad129nk6po801&fromjk=12f7e12bf19bfa2e', 'city': '40764 Langenfeld', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 26, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=12f7e12bf19bfa2e&bb=FQpNUE2_UOQcW2xyxHWja0zy1_iL0tUZDmAl-GdIK08dcTv3qG__fwzLttWpL2zV&xkcb=SoA767M3HqSOxYxcA50PbzkdCdPP&fccid=94844d1fef46eb96&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=250', 'job_description': 'Company Description\nAbout us\nTOMRA was founded in 1972, based on the design, manufacturing and sale of reverse vending machines (RVMs) for automated collection of used beverage containers. Today TOMRA provides technology-led solutions for transforming how society and industries obtain, use and reuse the planet’s resources to enable a world without waste.\nThe company’s collection and sorting technology supports the transition to a circular economy, optimizes resource recovery and minimizes waste in the food, recycling, and mining industries. TOMRA turns complex challenges into valuable solutions and enables companies to transform into more profitable, sustainable businesses.\nTOMRA has approximately 100,000 installations in over 80 markets worldwide and had total revenues of ~12,2 billion NOK in 2022. The Group employs ~5000 globally and is publicly listed on the Oslo Stock Exchange. The company headquarters are in Asker, Norway.\nWe like to call it the "clean-loop recycling" and challenge all our employees to take part in the\nResource Revolution\n.\nJob Description\nAs an IT Systems Administrator you will work in the global IT Infrastructure and Support department focusing on regional IT administration, contributing to a secure, reliable, and scalable infrastructure.\nAs a member of the regional infrastructure team, you will be responsible for the lifecycle management of IT infrastructure in regional offices, data centers and management of Cloud resources. You will actively participate in the implementation of group initiatives and contribute to ensure state-of-the-art infrastructure is available to TOMRA employees. You will also support divisional systems as per our PaaS offering to internal customers.\nThe role is based at our office in Langenfeld, near Düsseldorf.\nIn this role, your responsibilities are - but not limited to:\nServer Administration\nImplementation and operation of internal systems.\nRegular updates and maintenance of different server operating systems (Windows and Linux).\nUpdate and general maintenance of the virtualization infrastructure (mainly VMware).\nConfiguration, monitoring and troubleshooting system backups, archiving, and disaster recovery.\nProviding expert support for on-prem and Cloud systems.\nExecution of disaster recovery drills.\nWork as part of the regional infrastructure team.\nNetwork Administration\nAdministration and maintenance of TOMRA network infrastructure (LAN, WAN).\nImplementation of network security according to provided guidelines.\nCloud Administration\nOn-prem to Cloud network connectivity administration.\nAdministration of Cloud resources according to security policies.\nAudits\nPrepare for and answer audit requests for systems you maintain\nConduct IT audits of other locations\nThird Party Communication\nCommunicate and work with external partners on infrastructure problems.\nOpen and manage tickets with external support.\nDocumentation\nKeep infrastructure documentation updated, especially as a part of change management.\nOn-prem and Cloud system documentation.\nReview and revise Standard Operating Procedures in collaboration with the global team of System Engineers.\nIssue documentation, incl. learnings and proposals from process adaptions.\nUser Support\nProvide expert support to the Helpdesk and help out with L1 requests during peaks.\nProvide L2 expert support for systems you maintain.\nTroubleshoot and escalate L2/L3 support cases.\nAsset Management\nManage server and application/service assets in a global CMDB.\nQualifications\nTechnical/Professional:\nUniversity degree in Computer Science (B.Sc.) or at least 3 years of experience in a similar position.\nGeneral:\nExperience with servers and storage systems (SAN, NAS)\nGood network technology and security knowledge (WAN, LAN, WLAN)\nWindows Server (2022/2019) and Linux administration\nExtensive knowledge in virtualization technologies (VMware, HyperV)\nExtensive knowledge in hybrid (Cloud + on-prem) environments with network and VM administration\nSkills in IT Service Management\nCustomer focused\nGood knowledge in Windows 11 and Office 365\nEnd user IT support experience\nExperience with administration of communication and collaboration systems (Exchange, Teams, O365)\nConfidence in using English and German as a work language - requesting B2 level or above.\nAdditional Information\nPlease ensure you...\nSubmit a\nshort\ncover letter telling us why you want this job and join TOMRA.\nSubmit an updated CV/resumé.\nApply no later than 6th October 2023\nThis is what we offer you:\nCompetitive salary (based on experience)\nCompetitive pension and insurance package\nGroup IT bonus system\nPossibility to develop and grow in a company that look after its employees.\nWe are looking forward to receiving your application including your cover letter and CV, and would like to onboard you as soon as possible and latest before the turn of the year.\nThe job is on-site\nfor the first period of your employment and at least until your onboarding is completed and you are up-and-running. After we have verified you are sufficiently independent, you\nmay\nagree with your manager to work hybrid.\nTOMRA is an equal opportunity employer, where we recognise and celebrate the diversity of our workforce and community – be it on the basis of gender, age, culture, religion, language or personal circumstances. TOMRA is also committed to building on the perspectives, experience, knowledge and skills that this diversity brings to our organisation.', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 40, 1, 304844), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
