{'job_title_name': 'Circular Economy Engineering Program Manager (m/f/d)', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Landbell Group', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Landbell-Group?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad1vfjj4ri800&fromjk=274f710df83c176d', 'city': 'Mainz', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 20, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=274f710df83c176d&bb=cd8IYeAQmq8Knzw8ejqgNRPH72yGeaPig8qpEvKuvZteziKGMjApk4IjvcTPeK2v&xkcb=SoC567M3HqSLuJxTsp0LbzkdCdPP&fccid=63f01a5c22fae995&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=190', 'job_description': 'Located by Agreement\nImmediately | Full time | Travel availability for around 20% of the time\nAs a\nCircular Economy Engineering Program/Project Manager\n, you will lead and support the design, develop and delivery of global circular economy engineering solutions\nin the scope of end-of-life products/accessories and packaging take-back programs, for worldwide producers\n, focussing on WEEE, Batteries and Packaging.\nThe position is an excellent opportunity for an experienced waste management professional in a growing team with an international client portfolio. The ideal candidates will excel at interacting with multi-national clients in a technical, client relationship management and product focused capacity. You will be supporting a few key clients and will work as part of a small team on several different projects at a time.\nThe company has an ethos of trust, accountability and absolute discretion derived from senior experience within blue chip organizations.\nYour responsibilities\nReviewing complex customer requirements and design take-back programs that comply with those requirements, with aptitude for risk mitigation and by applying project management principles.\nAct as a catalyst for designing bespoke consulting product lines, related to global take-back.\nManaging contractual networks for global take-back, within the group and with external suppliers.\nSet-up and Improve operational workflows. Ensure continual service deliver improvement.\nMonitoring service/operational performance and profitability by analysing data and producing technical reports and customers charters.\nAct as the customer operational/technical single point of contact.\nYour qualifications\nEngineering degree or equivalent.\n5 years as a minimum of working experience and 3 years in a similar role (desirable)\nProficiency in English (level C as a minimum). Proficiency in other languages is welcome.\nIT Proficiency (Office 365 suite as a minimum). Excel expert proficiency (desirable).\nWaste operations management experience (3 years)\nWaste management legislation knowledge (handling, transport, and treatment)\nExperience in sustainability matters (desirable)\nCommunication and Relationship Building\nCross Cultural Awareness\nCross-functional team leadership and collaboration\nAnalytical and attention to detail\nPlanning/organisation\nProblem Resolution\nCustomer Orientation (internal and external)\nFlexibility, Adaptability, Resilience and Self-motivated\nWe offer you\nMulticultural environment\nFlat hierarchies with short decision-making paths\nCompetitive salary\nGreat working atmosphere in a motivated team\nApply now\nInterested in joining our team? Send your CV and cover letter to Ursula Hayes u.hayes@h2compliance.com', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 40, 31, 306397), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
