{'job_title_name': 'Senior Accountant', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Avient', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Avient-2?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad22vpj30g803&fromjk=fdfd84fe519e351a', 'city': 'Rastatt', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 20, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=fdfd84fe519e351a&bb=m-utibcWiMIdRUUUznmuhWgvPJewupe0y2jHou9r4k2k5Edx5Z6bnNtjpPXWBVZ7&xkcb=SoAm67M3HqSLuORTsp0JbzkdCdPP&fccid=62e846a13660317d&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=190', 'job_description': "Avient Corporation (NYSE: AVNT) provides specialized and sustainable material solutions that transform customer challenges into opportunities, bringing new products to life for a better world. Examples include:\nDyneema®, the world's strongest fiber™, enables unmatched levels of performance and protection for end-use applications, including ballistic personal protection, marine and sustainable infrastructure and outdoor sports\nUnique technologies that improve the recyclability of products and enable recycled content to be incorporated, thus advancing a more circular economy\nLight-weighting solutions that replace heavier traditional materials like metal, glass and wood, which can improve fuel efficiency in all modes of transportation and reduce carbon footprint\nSustainable infrastructure solutions that increase energy efficiency, renewable energy, natural resource conservation and fiber optic / 5G network accessibility\nAvient is certified ACC Responsible Care®, a founding member of the Alliance to End Plastic Waste and certified Great Place to Work®. For more information, visit www.avient.com/. To access Avient's news library online, please visit www.avient.com/news.\nJob Summary\nThe Senior Accountant plays a key role on the level of German legal entity, is part of European finance team, leads month-end close process, reconciliation reporting, month end variance analysis, audits and other adhoc tasks. This position reports directly to European Lead Regional Controller, collaboration with corporate functions like treasury, tax and legal is essential.\nEssential Functions\nAccountabilities\nEnsuring the consistent integrity of information, in a timely manner.\nCompliance with internal and external accounting policies, procedures and legislation.\nResponsibilities\nPrepares and files annual financial statements under German GAAP (HGB)\nLeads external and internal audits to include providing detailed documentation for audit requests\nWorks with external consultants on annual income tax return preparation\nMonthly income tax calculation, quarterly income tax provision – current and deferred taxes – internal tax reporting\nResponsible for the month end close process (accounting part)\nCompletion of monthly VAT returns and intrastat reports\nCompletion of national statistics reports\nPrepares and posts recurring and standard manual journals\nMonthly review of cost centres with the business unit finance manager to ensure accuracy of financial data\nReconciliation of intercompany balances\nCompletion of balance sheet reconciliations in line with prescribed templates and frequencies\nOwnership of the fixed asset process and being the main point of contact. To include capitalisation and ensure CIP is monitored in a timely manner\nManaging the liquidity flow for German legal entity, collaborating with Corporate Treasury\nPrepares monthly cash flows to agreed deadlines\nOther projects and general office duties as required\nQualifications & Experience\nEssential\nGerman language knowledge on professional level\nBachelor – Accounting, Finance or equivalent\nAt least 3 years’ experience working within industry as Senior Accountant (Bilanzbuchhalter), 7 years in accounting in total\nStrong team player\nAbility to work to deadlines and efficiently\nAbility to build relationships with stakeholders in a virtual environment\nSelf-reliant and self-motivated\nExcellent communication skills\nStrong Excel skills\nStrong SAP knowledge\nDesired\nSOX compliance\nIFRS\nCompetencies\nCustomer Focus\nAction Orientated\nInstils Trust\nDemonstrates Self-Awareness\nCollaborates\nCommunicates Effectively\nBeing Resilient\nSituational Adaptability\nWHY AVIENT:\nAt Avient, we strive for a culture of trust and engagement. Our associates are leading company initiatives such as Lead by Women, HYPE (Harnessing Young Professionals), Pride at Avient and Embrace to advance diversity in professional and personal development. We also provide our associates with robust development programs such as Avient Academy, Lean Six Sigma, and various leadership workshops to allow for career growth in a variety of ways. With workplace flexibility, health and wellness programs, and paid time off for community service, we are committed to building upon our positive momentum.\nAt Avient, we believe diversity of ideas and backgrounds gives us the creativity to be successful in a rapidly changing world. In support of this, we stress equality of opportunity for all qualified individuals in accordance with applicable laws. Decisions in hiring, promotion, development, compensation and advancement are based upon non-discriminatory factors such as, for example, qualifications, abilities, experience, and performance\nAvient Corporation is a drug free workplace. Avient is an equal opportunity employer. We maintain a policy of non-discrimination in providing equal employment to all qualified employees and candidates regardless of race, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, color, religion, national origin, disability, genetic information, protected veteran’s status, or other legally protected classification in accordance with applicable federal, state and local law.", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 40, 34, 753553), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
