{'job_title_name': 'Electrical engineer (gn) - Battery system development', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Voltfang', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Voltfang?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad272nk78s800&fromjk=d8d81908afebe2f0', 'city': ' Aachen', 'remote': 'Zum Teil im Homeoffice', 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 21, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=d8d81908afebe2f0&bb=CJiPVUdvWGtAXf2h2UZEA6hkaBEWsyefVb2OpGf97eDPldNdwj-vaDYPAU-G8HyiO0qZWtWNaXtL0uAUBXKvdWSccnWmWEiFM4Ic6xEegzU%3D&xkcb=SoDr67M3HqSLi7Q3lR0MbzkdCdPP&fccid=eee86c8aa0f91fa5&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=200', 'job_description': "Voltfang - The sustainable power storage system\nWe are a fast growing company that develops and produces sustainable electricity storage systems from qualified electric car batteries. In this way, we help anufacturing businesses and industry to become more environmentally friendly and less dependent on conventional energy sources. In this way, we can make a significant contribution to climate protection and take a decisive step towards a green future.\nWe rely on an experienced and motivated team that contributes its knowledge and skills to achieve our goals. Our corporate culture is characterised by cooperation and team spirit. Different departments all pull together in order to be able to look forward to a positive future together.\nWe strive for constant further development, which is why we are looking for employees who can contribute and take on responsibility in order to grow with us individually. We are not just any team - we are the Voltfam. Creativity, enthusiasm and fun play a decisive role for us.\nThat's why we are looking for talented employees who want to achieve long-term success together with us. If you feel addressed and would like to be part of an ambitious team, then get in touch with us!\nTasks\nJoining our team as an Electronic Design Engineer for Battery Storage System Development offers an exciting opportunity to work on innovative projects and contribute to the advancement of clean energy technologies. If you have a passion for electronic design, a keen eye for detail, and a drive to deliver high-quality solutions in battery storage systems while ensuring certification and functional safety compliance, we invite you to apply and become a valued member of our team.\nDesign and develop electronic circuits and systems for battery storage\nsystems, considering factors such as functionality, efficiency, safety,\nand reliability\nCollaborate closely with battery engineers, mechanical engineers, and software engineers to ensure seamless integration of electronic systems into battery storage solutions\nConduct feasibility studies and evaluate electronic component options to select\nthe most suitable components and technologies for battery storage applications.\nDesign and lay out printed circuit boards (PCBs) using Altium, considering design rules, signal integrity, thermal management, and manufacturability for battery storage systems\nSupport prototype builds, perform testing and troubleshooting, and provide\nguidance to technicians during the development and validation phases of\nbattery storage systems\nConduct design reviews and participate in the selection of test methodologies to verify and validate electronic designs for battery storage applications\nEnsure compliance with relevant industry standards, regulations, and best practices in electronic design for battery storage systems, such as functional safety standards, EMC/EMI requirements\nRequirements\nBachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering, Electronics, or a related field. A master's degree is preferred\nProven experience (at least 3-5 years) in electronic design, including circuit\ndesign, PCB layout, and system integration for battery storage systems.\nProficiency in schematic capture and PCB layout design using CAD software (e.g.,\nAltium Designer, Eagle) for battery applications\nStrong knowledge of electronic components, analog and digital circuits, battery\nmanagement systems (BMS), and signal integrity principles relevant to\nbattery storage systems\nFamiliarity with industry standards and regulations in electronic design for battery storage, such as safety standards (e.g. IEC62619, Functional Safety), EMC/EMI requirements\nProficiency in using lab equipment for testing and debugging electronic circuits and systems\nBenefits\nActive contribution to climate protection & the circular economy\nFree use of the Velocities (e-bikes) in Aachen\nCooperation with Urban Sports Club\nSubsidy for the job ticket\nOffice Dog\nFlexible working hours and hybrid working possible\nModern office space with shopping facilities nearby", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 40, 38, 776173), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
