{'job_title_name': 'NGO Event Manager', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Circular Berlin', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Circular-Berlin?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad27q9j4ri800&fromjk=ae7da023b9194073', 'city': '10407 Berlin', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 21, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=ae7da023b9194073&bb=CJiPVUdvWGtAXf2h2UZEA04szeS4_7JPy9sfi_iV1ZoyMABy3OPka4pgfHVsOI9NgzE4KRhvS_mi5b2WttpUb0fU-iwXOeBvKMPdsGeFeWc%3D&xkcb=SoDC67M3HqSLi7Q3lR0ObzkdCdPP&fccid=388395e22ee53457&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=200', 'job_description': 'Are you looking for an opportunity to support the circular economy transformation through the ideation and realization of inspiring events and learning moments? Circular Berlin is looking for you!\nCircular Berlin is a non-profit accelerating Berlin transition towards a circular city, envisioning it as a resilient, citizen-oriented region. We develop knowledge on the circular economy and apply it through practical projects, community building and education. Everything we learn in Berlin is made openly available to implement in other corners of the world.\nCircular Berlin is looking for an event manager with experience in the ideation and realization of different event formats for its community of individuals and its ecosystem of organizations, to join its team 2 days/week from January 2024.\nIn this role, you will be responsible for the creation of inspiring and engaging events (online and offline) to bring together our community whilst disseminating Circular Economy knowledge. You are the person orchestrating all the different activities and involved people for a smooth realization of the planned events.\n40% position:\nFor this role, it is expected to be engaged 16 hrs/week.\nTasks\nYour Responsibilities in this role:\nGeneral coordination & execution: Responsible for planning, organizing, and executing internal and external event formats.\nEvent Planning: Planning of the upcoming formats for the year as well as defining concepts, objectives, timelines, and budgets.\nEvent organization: Finding and booking locations and speakers as well as sponsors and partners.\nEvent promotion & communication: Writing engaging invitation texts and cooperation with the communication team for the scheduling and promotion.\nEvent execution and on-site management: Overseeing on-site logistics during events, coordination of speakers.\nCooperating with the Project Managers supporting them with the events’ dissemination work of their specific projects.\nMonitoring the effectiveness of the events in reaching the organization\'s goals through periodic analysis of data and KPIs.\nParticipate in regular meetings with the organizational board and project teams.\nRequirements\nRequirements for this position:\nAt least 2 years of professional experience in organizing events.\nYou are interested in creating inspiring formats for our community & ecosystem and use all your creativity to invent innovative formats.\nYou are not afraid to communicate and to reach out to possible speakers, sponsors, event venues.\nExperience in setting up basic technical equipment for online events (zoom) as well as for offline events (e.g: setting up monitor, beamer, microphones, etc...).\nA good knowledge of the topic of Circular Economy and a strong network of organizations, individuals & companies active in this field in Berlin will be considered as strong assets for this position.\nInterest and experience in moderating events are a plus.\nFluent written and spoken German and English.\nBenefits\nWhat we offer in a nutshell:\nA long-term position\nFlexible timing;\nWork remotely or from our office;\nAccess to our community, internal circular economy resources & slack channel\nA monthly salary of about € 1.300,- (gross)\nTo apply, please send your CV and a short cover letter outlining your relevant experience and interest in the role. Please include "Application as Event Manager" in\nthe subject line.\nFor more information about Circular Berlin and our work, please visit our website.\nWe look forward to receiving your application!', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 40, 39, 580556), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
