{'job_title_name': 'Project Manager Budget-To-Report (f/m/d)', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Heidelberg Materials AG', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Heidelberg-Materials?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad2dcq2bbt002&fromjk=05de63e1a3b5fcbe', 'city': 'Heidelberg', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 10, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=05de63e1a3b5fcbe&bb=EAjDq30HM7IHygWgZ48qZ828Fu3KItqDjW3RltpH_aEdEFiVSF5w0d4w_pzJOguclbXSgQwj83HaUClnBXSuQ2VOBXTgkh609fXKuuFyzZU%3D&xkcb=SoCU67M3HqSGu9WQ6Z0GbzkdCdPP&fccid=305a803957776ce6&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=90', 'job_description': "At the center of our actions lies the responsibility for the environment. As the forerunner on the path to carbon neutrality and circular economy in the building materials industry, we are working on sustainable building materials and solutions for the future. We enable new opportunities for our customers through digitalization.\nFor our Group Shared Service Center Department we are seeking to recruit a Project Manager Budget-To-Report (f/m/d).\nAs a B2R Project Manager, you will be responsible for the identification of gaps between existing processes and the global business processes defined by the Global Process Owner (GPO) as well as for launching and monitoring of process improvement initiatives.\nIn this role you will support the GSSC GPOs during the SAP S/4HANA project, to ensure that the entire GSSC business processes are fully converted into SAP S/4HANA. You will also support to develop process-based solution proposals with the target to achieve the highest possible added value from the SAP S/4HANA conversion and thus a high level of end user satisfaction within the SSC community and other business departments involved.\nYou will report to the Director Group Shared Service Center and you will be located in Heidelberg.\nYour next challenge\nClose collaboration with the Global Process Owners\nProactive cooperation with the entire Group SSC Team to share information, get guidance and document results\nDevelop and maintain business policies which drive our processes\nEnsure compliance, standardization and harmonized processes across business lines\nUnderstand business user needs and processes to suggest efficient end-to-end enhancements in close alignment with the GPO, Group Departments and Digital\nImprove existing processes wherever possible with SAP S/4HANA to reach highly efficient performance indicators\nLaunching projects to identify best practices and to transfer the best-in-class solutions to the SSCs\nCommunicate and facilitate discussions with all involved parties, prepare and hold presentations to drive solutions on proposed features and functionalities\nWork with IT teams to ensure good fit to existing Infrastructure technologies and applications (where applicable), to obtain project budgets\nEnsure the delivery of high-quality transaction processes\nWillingness to travel to business offices as appropriate and as necessary\nDeliver process related trainings\nRollout / support of process related software tools\nYour profile\nEducation/Qualification\nUniversity degree\nSAP Junior experts in the areas of accounting and controlling\nHigh IT affinity and skills required, especially SAP ECC and ideally in SAP S/4HANA\n3 years’ consulting experience in business process improvement initiatives, accounting, controlling, consolidation and/or shared service center processes\nBusiness Competence\nStrong leadership skills\nSubstantial accounting experience; IFRS knowledge\nExcellent process knowledge in Budget to Report\nVery good verbal and written communication skills in English\nStrong analytical and technical skills\nSoft Skills\nInterpersonal & communication skills\nExperience in an international working environment\nStrong presentation skills\nManagement Skills\nEnergetic “hands on” approach with good organization skills and the ability to prioritize\nConcentration on results, control and process efficiency\nFast and consistent implementation of decisions\nSelf-driven, organized and detailed-oriented personality\nLeadership Skills\nInternal & external motivation\nGoal orientation\nCommunication\nOur offer\nWe are convinced that only those who successfully realize their personal goals can also fully contribute professionally. That's why we offer you attractive benefits, such as:\nFlexible working time models with up to 50% remote working within Germany\n30 vacation days plus additional special vacation days\nAttractive compensation with profit share/bonus, Christmas and vacation payment\nMultiple learning & development options: support of job-related further training, E-campus, various technical and leadership development programs\nJobTicket, JobBike and further special conditions and discounts for e.g. gyms\nCompany fitness room, various sports classes, health and prevention campaigns\nIndividual onboarding with buddy program as well as various networking initiatives (Network of Women, International Network etc.)\nModern headquarters next to the river Neckar with ergonomic workplaces and height-adjustable desks\nCanteen with discounted and healthy meals\nBicycle and underground parking with charging stations - for e-bike and car\n...and much more.\nJob description\nProfessional\nEntry level\nHeidelberg, Germany\nLocation\nFull time\nContract\nFinance\nCategory", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 40, 45, 244260), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
