{'job_title_name': 'Campus Internship - Digital Innovation – Cross-functional in Germany', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Dow', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Dow?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad2eu7jjip800&fromjk=0f5e7381aa504cd4', 'city': 'Wiesbaden', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 10, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=0f5e7381aa504cd4&bb=EAjDq30HM7IHygWgZ48qZyy64VujNYrOkWsvz9Mm1iB7RNJCRAXiv3H8x6XlAFayq6Q2ELL5qAflcF4s_ruE72h6ydPTYoklGQWGdMEJHAw%3D&xkcb=SoCH67M3HqSGu9WQ6Z0CbzkdCdPP&fccid=b3a3d9b7840e20cb&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=90', 'job_description': "At Dow, we believe in putting people first and we’re passionate about delivering integrity, respect and safety to our customers, our employees and the planet.\nOur people are at the heart of our solutions. They reflect the communities we live in and the world where we do business. Their diversity is our strength. We’re a community of relentless problem solvers that offers the daily opportunity to contribute with your perspective, transform industries and shape the future. Our purpose is simple - to deliver a sustainable future for the world through science and collaboration. If you’re looking for a challenge and meaningful role, you’re in the right place.\nAbout you and this role\nDo you want to join Dow's digital innovation journey? We are seeking master's / Ph.D. students interested to complement their primary expertise with Digital Internship in one of its European sites in Wiesbaden or Ahlen (Germany). You will be integrated in one of Dow’s key functions - Research and Development. You will work with a cross-functional team whose high-level goal is to accelerate the digital evolution of a global leader in the materials industry. You will bring your skills and experience to work with a group of domain experts to accelerate delivery of high priority projects. Goals of the project(s) could include delivering breakthrough sustainable chemistry innovations; advancing on a circular economy; producing better and safer materials; optimizing products and processes to reduce carbon footprint; optimizing planning, scheduling, and value chain to a greener chemistry; and other areas to help Dow reaching ambitious sustainability goals.\nDepending on your suitability and agreement, you will be selected for one of the following project proposals:\nTitle: Silicone Polymer production data analysis\nDescription: Dow Performance Silicones has been a global leader in silicone-based technology for more than seventy years with >7000 silicone products in the market. Dow SylgardTM silicone dielectric gels are among the most well-known products offered by Dow Performance Silicones. By possessing properties such as high elongation and low hardness, these gels are widely used for coating, encapsulating, potting, and sealing electronic devices. Quality control on key raw materials used for the gel production is critical to ensure these gel’s consistent high performance. Over the years, there has been a large data library comprising several process steps and their quality test results for the production of these key raw materials. It is envisioned that an in-depth data analysis of this library would be highly beneficial in providing valuable information for both good product quality control and future continuous production improvement. We are looking for a digital intern with outstanding skills with Excel or any other data and statistical analysis programs, general programming skills and hand-on experience to work with large numerical data set\nSkills: Prior work experience in data analysis and production. Passion for material and digital sciences. Knowledge of German is a plus.\nLocation: Wiesbaden, Germany\nTitle: Develop a Model for predicting non-pneumatic PU wheel performance\nDescription: Polyurethane elastomers, due to its unique properties such as high abrasion resistance, tear strength, excellent chemical resistance, are gaining increasing interest used as tyre materials for non-pneumatic wheels and rollers. However, PU materials generally exhibit considerable internal heat generation and Insufficient high-temperature resistance, which leads to premature failures when they undergo high load and high speed applications. Due to a cost/time constrain on intensive wheel testing, a model that is able to predict wheel performance (Such as Max. load capacity, failure strain/temperature, failure modes) would be extremely useful tool for new product development. The scope of this project is to improve the existing model, by implement new dynamic mechanical data generated from larger deformation scale, to improve its precision on predicting wheel performance.\nSkills: Prior work experience in Matlab coding. Passion for studying relationship of PU chemistry – Physics – Performance.\nLocation: Ahlen, Germany\nQualifications\nCurrently enrolled in a MSc. Or Ph.D. degree program in Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Material Science, Polymer Science, Computer Science, Mathematics, Physics, Operations Research, Data Science, or other related disciplines\nLegally entitled by EU citizenship or by a valid VISA to work in the project country\nProficient in English\nKey Traits\nExperienced in chemical, polymer, and/or material properties; manufacture and/or customer experience of materials; supply chains around manufacturing; and/or the computing/IT systems needed to accomplish the above\nPrimary expertise in chemical engineering, materials science, chemistry, polymer science, theoretical modeling, operations management, or other industrial engineering\nEducated with data science techniques such, machine learning, its applicability to industry, and potential for value creation\nDemonstrate competency in computer science, data analytics, and/or machine learning\nAble to work independently but also in teams\nGreat time-management skills and ability to work under tight deadlines\nEffective communicator, organized and responsive\nAble to quickly assimilate and understand technology, out-of-box thinker\nAdditional notes\nPreferable duration is 6 months, but other duration could be arranged. This internship could be part, but not necessary, of a graduating school assignment. Working hours will be the local and legal equivalent of a full-time employee.\nAbout Dow\nDow (NYSE: DOW) combines global breadth; asset integration and scale; focused innovation and materials science expertise; leading business positions; and environmental, social and governance leadership to achieve profitable growth and help deliver a sustainable future. The Company's ambition is to become the most innovative, customer centric, inclusive and sustainable materials science company in the world. Dow's portfolio of plastics, industrial intermediates, coatings and silicones businesses delivers a broad range of differentiated, science-based products and solutions for its customers in high-growth market segments, such as packaging, infrastructure, mobility and consumer applications. Dow operates manufacturing sites in 31 countries and employs approximately 37,800 people. Dow delivered sales of approximately $57 billion in 2022. References to Dow or the Company mean Dow Inc. and its subsidiaries. For more information, please visit\nwww.dow.com\nor follow\n@DowNewsroom\non Twitter.\nAs part of our dedication to the diversity of our workforce, Dow is committed to equal opportunities in employment. We encourage every employee to bring their whole self to work each day to not only deliver more value, but also have a more fulfilling career. Further information regarding Dow's equal opportunities is available on\nwww.dow.com\n.", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 40, 47, 25062), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
