{'job_title_name': 'Senior Engineer (m/w/d) RD&E', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Ecolab', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Ecolab?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad2jie2gra002&fromjk=dbcdaf55851c4321', 'city': '40789 Monheim am Rhein', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 11, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=dbcdaf55851c4321&bb=CreZbCrejfakBLvupu0rgreXe09GaAzpHZtOWNgaqTJJLZ84vt9ODAtnh-3FCp3b2h7yqdJqOicR3aLxPd6TozZbc62ttCXgTT5oAlgC1YQ%3D&xkcb=SoCs67M3HqSGgxgwoD0HbzkdCdPP&fccid=b8df555617879658&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=100', 'job_description': "Ecolab is the global leader in planet health. At the heart of our mission is our goal to help our industrial customers improve their water sustainability.\nWith more than $13 billion in sales, an aggressive growth agenda and 48,000 global associates, this is a chance to help impact some of the world’s biggest challenges. Come join a company making a difference in more than 170 countries around the world.\nWe are looking for a\nSenior Engineer\n(f/m/d) to join our international team in\nMonheim am Rhein, Germany\n. This position reports to Senior Program Leader RD&E Life Science Europe & Asia Pacific.\nIn your role, you are responsible for\nleading cross-divisional innovation pipeline projects to develop safe, sustainable, and easy-to-use Packaging, Equipment and Application solutions\n. You will interact closely with research development & engineering, marketing, supply chain, regulatory affairs, sales, customers, and industry partners to identify and successfully implement game-changing concepts for Pharmaceutical customers. Your positive and energetic attitude to lead and drive projects with your peer technical staff, as well as your collaborative interaction with the sales team is key to your success.\nWhat You Will Do:\nLead the development of mid/ long-term strategy\nfor packaging and equipment solutions incorporating customer input, corporate ambitions, and regulatory requirements.\nLead large/complex projects to completion\naccording to time, compliance, quality and cost targets as well as in consideration of Ecolab´s sustainability metrics.\nCommunicate project\nstatus to stakeholders across the organization.\nThe assigned packaging/equipment development work activities include packaging laboratory testing, bench scale experimentation, scale up work, plant test protocol, packaging transfer manual, test reports, specification development and regulatory agency certification/compliance.\nManage required resources and partnerships\nwith Ecolab vendors & copackers.\nDevelop and sustain industry network\nto enable early access to state-of-the-art sustainable packaging / application technology.\nSupport knowledge gaps\nfor customers and Ecolab associates and create materials to inform and educate.\nWhat skills will set you apart:\nExperienced Project Manager\nfor packaging and equipment development.\nAgility to align input from\nmultiple stakeholders\nto define priorities.\nGood communication & collaboration skills\n, excellent analytical skills and ability to work in a diverse and global team.\nKnow-how to work in regulated markets with the\nhighest quality standards\n, ideally in sterile products.\nWhat you'll need:\nUniversity degree either in packaging engineering, chemical or mechanical engineering or natural sciences\nand work experience (up to 5yrs) in an international environment, preferably in packaging or equipment development.\nPrior\nexperience\nin Pharmaceutical business and/or other regulated markets.\nPrior experience with\nsustainability and circular economy\nFluent in English\nwith good verbal and written communication skills.\nA second European language besides English is preferred, fluency in German is also beneficial.\nOur recruiter are looking forward to your application.\n#li-eu\nOur Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion\nAt Ecolab, we believe the best teams are diverse and inclusive, and we are on a journey to create a workplace where every associate can grow and achieve their best. We are committed to fair and equal treatment of associates and applicants. We recruit, hire, promote, transfer and provide opportunities for advancement on the basis of individual qualifications and job performance. In all matters affecting employment, compensation, benefits, working conditions, and opportunities for advancement, we will not discriminate against any associate or applicant for employment because of race, religion, color, creed, national origin, citizenship status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and expressions, genetic information, marital status, age, disability, or status as a covered veteran.\nIn addition, we are committed to furthering the principles of Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) through Affirmative Action (AA). Our goal is to fully utilize minority, female, disabled and covered veteran individuals at all levels of the workforce. Ecolab is a place where you can grow your career, own your future and impact what matters.", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 40, 51, 555732), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
