{'job_title_name': 'Research Assistent/Postdoc (m/w/d) process technology', 'job_type': 'Teilzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Zentrum für Sonnenenergie- und...', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Zentrum-F%C3%BCr-Sonnenenergie---Und-Wasserstoff--forschung-Baden-W%C3%BCrttemberg-(zsw)?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad2lr3jqun800&fromjk=f850fef6327199f5', 'city': '89081 Ulm', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 11, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=f850fef6327199f5&bb=CreZbCrejfakBLvupu0rgnrL-kBCRhzdYNRRVWqbbSE3qUYbmDs73BjhApl3dQT56qU6eDGl8MZMBf6eccDXdzeRG-HSz-yNTPDmuADNfAk%3D&xkcb=SoB_67M3HqSGgxgwoD0ObzkdCdPP&fccid=369a352d824b093d&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=100', 'job_description': '// Zentrum für Sonnenenergie- und Wasserstoff-Forschung Baden-Württemberg (ZSW)\nWir suchen aktuell: Research Assistent/Postdoc (m/w/d) process technology in Ulm\n// Energy with a future\nThe Centre for Solar Energy and Hydrogen Research Baden-Württemberg (ZSW) is one of the leading institutes for applied research into the major issues relating to the energy transition which include photovoltaics, wind energy, battery technology, fuel cells, electrolysis, e-fuels, circular economy, policy advice, and the use of AI for process and system optimisation. We work in tandem with industry to pave the way to market for new technologies. The challenge falls to more than 300 employees and around 100 research and student assistants at the ZSW bases in Stuttgart and Ulm. The ZSW also operates a test site for wind energy and another test site for PV systems. The ZSW is a member of the Innovationsallianz Baden-Württemberg (innBW), an alliance of ten applied research institutions.\nFor the department\nAccumulators Materials Research\nat the Ulm site, we are seeking as soon as possible a\nResearch Assistent (Post Doc) (m/f/d) process technology\nYour areas of responsibility:\nManagement and processing of research projects on the development of lithium-ion electrodes and cells\nFurther development of formulations and processes for electrode production, elaboration of technological progress\nAssessment of the electrochemical performance of electrodes in prototype cells\nInstruction of technical staff\nCommunication with customers and offer preparation\nPresentation of project results at project meetings and conferences\nWriting of project reports\nYour profile:\nAbove-average university degree in C\nhemistry, Electrochemistry, Anorganic Chemistry\nor comparable qualification\nProfound knowledge and experience in the field of electrochemistry and Li-ion electrodes production\nVery good skills in processing data and in scientific evaluation\nVery good German and English language skills and high expressiveness in spoken and written language\nExcellent communication and teamwork skills\nSurpassing commitment, an eye for the most important aspects and structured and goal-oriented work approach\nOur offer to you:\nExcellent research meets direct application: We research for and directly with industry and design the energy supply of tomorrow today - scientifically excellent but always application-oriented\nCreative working atmosphere: We live an open corporate culture with flat hierarchies, plenty of freedom for creative development, shaping research content and innovation\nUse flexibility: Flexitime model with flexible working hours and the possibility to work hybrid as well as flexible part-time models to support the compatibility of family and career\nSustainable mobility: DeutschlandTicket as a subsidised job ticket, free charging at the institute\'s own charging stations, bicycle parking with service area\nNetworking and career: Cross-institute cooperation, national and international research projects, as well as a wide range of individually customisable training.\nModern institute buildings with first-class infrastructure offer an appealing working environment, company health management with numerous sports and health courses, mostly employer-funded company pension scheme\nThe employment contract is limited to 2 years, has a volume of employment of 100% and is classified according to the TV-L regulations of the civil service in Baden-Württemberg. If you are interested in this position, please apply exclusively using "Jetzt online bewerben" button in the job advertisement. Should you have any technical questions, please feel free to call Dr. Alice Hoffmann +49 731 9530-558. Further information is available at www. zsw-bw.de.\nWould you also like to advance applied energy research? We are looking forward to receiving your application!', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 40, 54, 22699), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
