{'job_title_name': 'Senior Specialist Packaging Engineering (m/f/d)', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'CYBEX', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Cybex?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad2ot7k78q800&fromjk=0b3f54c8c93288da', 'city': '95448 Bayreuth', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 12, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=0b3f54c8c93288da&bb=7nbWtxUJE5dmqZMZMIKRAVNCG8fh4aQKg_7qRvBt6VgP84SiwwjwBfoeAmS5a05lJ2m_6QK6YbAfRDdDquMIfftyni2iCxg9hPuaBCn0a5o%3D&xkcb=SoAt67M3HqSG5IQSDx0DbzkdCdPP&fccid=208031f912d98323&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=110', 'job_description': "Bayreuth, DE\nCYBEX is a company that puts tomorrow’s people at the heart of its brand. Always questioning the status quo and not afraid of challenging the establishment, CYBEX has become not just a leader in child safety but is seen as an innovative lifestyle and fashion brand for parents. We offer car seats, baby carriers, kids furniture and strollers enabling parents to keep their little ones safe in style. After growing rapidly in the last few years, we look for ambitious talent to contribute to CYBEX’s success story.\nYour areas of responsibilities:\nManage and develop packaging solutions for new and existing products, ensuring they meet functional, cost, and sustainability requirements\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams such as R&D, Quality, Procurement, and Marketing to ensure packaging solutions meet product and customer needs\nConduct packaging assessments to identify opportunities for improvement in cost, sustainability, and performance\nStay up-to-date with industry trends and emerging packaging technologies, and make recommendations for their application to the company's products\nDevelop and maintain packaging specifications, standards, and best practices\nSupport regulatory compliance efforts by ensuring packaging meets applicable regulations and standards\nProvide technical support and training to internal and external stakeholders on packaging-related topics\nYour profile of qualification:\nBachelor's degree in Packaging Engineering, or a related field\nExperience in packaging engineering, with a focus on consumer goods\nStrong technical knowledge of packaging materials, manufacturing processes, paper technology, and testing methods\nExperience in project management, including managing timelines, budgets, and stakeholders\nExperience with sustainable packaging design and circular economy principles\nProfound knowledge of Artios CAD, Cape Pack (or similar) programs\nExcellent communication, collaboration, and problem-solving skills\nStrong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple priorities\nFluent in English, German is a plus\nCYBEX operates globally and has employees from over 29 nations. If you are keen to leave your footprint in a swiftly growing business that offers plenty of opportunities to grow both on a professional and individual level, you’ve come to the right place. As part of Goodbaby International Holdings Ltd., CYBEX is dedicated to creating an inclusive working environment that encompasses diversity and equal opportunities. In addition to a competitive salary, attractive annual leave, and discounts on our products you’ll have the chance to develop your personal profile in an international environment.", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 40, 57, 53598), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
