{'job_title_name': '(Senior) Consultant/Manager (all genders) Environmental Sustainability', 'job_type': 'Teilzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': 'Montag bis Freitag', 'company_name': 'Porsche Consulting GmbH', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Porsche-Consulting-Gmbh?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad2s3f2gtd000&fromjk=b16783589fc6732e', 'city': 'Stuttgart', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 12, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=b16783589fc6732e&bb=7nbWtxUJE5dmqZMZMIKRAaROjzKUBW3oCQ82KbhETk1I4N4296Xhh1y5EPtq1kVo_YmPzU8iStXVWXm-wQ03qnR2OLeI0XiuIC0fPpVorro%3D&xkcb=SoAE67M3HqSG5IQSDx0BbzkdCdPP&fccid=2144c20dbeb7cbb8&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=110', 'job_description': '(Senior) Consultant/Manager (all genders) Environmental Sustainability\nCode number:\nJ000002021\nEntry level:\nProfessionals\nLocation:\nBerlin, Frankfurt am Main, Hamburg, München, Stuttgart\nOrganization:\nPorsche Consulting GmbH\nTasks\nTasks\nTasks\nWe’re open to new ideas, and we welcome people who contribute and think for themselves. The more perspectives we draw on, the more innovative our work can be.\nWe need people who think strategically and act pragmatically, who want to help shape the future, who identify with our values and outlook, and who are committed to our goals.\nPeople are our priority! We will challenge you and encourage your individual strengths. We offer an appreciative working environment with development opportunities and a wide range of responsibilities. Let’s set new standards together—send in your application today.\nDevelopment, implementation and evaluation of cross-company sustainability strategies and business models\nDevelopment, design and implementation of measures focusing on decarbonization, zero impact factory, circular economy or sustainable supply chains, taking into account social and economic aspects\nManagement and steering of company-wide programs in sustainability transformation for the development, implementation and evaluation of strategies and business models in the fields of environment, climate and resources\nDevelopment and establishment of concepts and measures to anchor sustainability in the organization and in business processes, accompanied by individual change management, communication and qualification measures, as well as coaching of managers in the transformation process\nEvaluation and management as well as reporting on sustainability measures and results\nSupport in the acquisition of consulting projects, continuous further development of our consulting methods, maintenance of our client network as well as publication of topic-specific studies to strengthen external perception.\nQualifications\nQualifications\nQualifications\nSuccessfully completed university degree, ideally in a business/engineering subject (e.g. chemistry, physics, biology) with a focus on the environment and sustainability.\nSeveral years of professional experience in strategic management consulting with a focus on sustainability, practical experience in the manufacturing industry or with service providers as well as with innovative, leading start-ups with a focus on the design and implementation of sustainable solutions in the company, products and processes\nProfound knowledge in the areas of recycling, materials, renewable materials as well as life cycle analysis including the associated databases as well as in environmental, resource and energy management (ISO14001; 50001; 14040/44)\nPractical experience in holistic project management in a sustainability environment - from goal definition, staffing, task differentiation and team leadership to successful project completion\nStrong consulting skills such as strategic thinking, hands-on mentality and customer-centric communication\nVery good analytical skills as well as conceptual thinking and high result orientation to avoid entrepreneurial risks and ensure the future viability of companies and products\nDistinct independent, structured and professional way of working\nAn open, communicative, team-oriented and empathic personality\nVery good expression in German and English\nAt a Glance\nAt a Glance\nAt a Glance\nThere are many great reasons for a career at Porsche Consulting.\nWith more than 800 employees around the globe, Porsche Consulting is one of the world’s leading management consultancies. Founded in 1994, we now have 13 offices in six countries.\nOur international and dynamic field of work offers superb opportunities to build networks and forge professional contacts. Interesting tasks and challenging projects await you, as well as highly motivated and committed colleagues in the automotive, energy, financial services, industrial and consumer goods, aviation, pharmaceutical and medical technology, and transportation sectors.\nFor more information, visit: www.porsche-consulting.com\nExclusive look behind the scenes\nExclusive look behind the scenes\nExclusive look behind the scenes\nCorporate culture:\nWe are diverse and multinational with a strong team spirit and flat hierarchies—we use “du” with each other in German. We place a premium on transparency and short decisional paths. Team- and site-based events plus an alumni program foster a friendly ambience.\nWay of working:\nWe stand for strategic visions and smart implementation. With us you can take responsibility and set things in motion. Feedback is important to us, because people are our priority.\nWork environment:\nFlexibility is an integral part of our culture, with your choice of office location and an honor system for working hours. Our modern offices are attractively located, but we naturally also offer mobile work and part-time options as well as sabbaticals.\nEntry:\nAll new employees go through a three-week warm-up to prepare for their positions. You’ll experience the Porsche spirit at first hand, with special events to help you meet the team and the brand—and drive it, too. Our mentoring program offers individual guidance to all new employees for six months.\nDevelopment:\nLearning is key. You’ll go on learning together with your colleagues at two set weeks of training every year. Further opportunities include e-learning, internal expertise-based communities, potential support for doctoral and MBA programs, and annual employee review and coaching options.\nBenefits:\nA sports and fitness program, an attractive and sustainable mobility option, leasing offers, JobRad, on-site snacks and drinks, and comprehensive professional mobile work equipment are all a matter of course.\nSustainability:\nWe are proud signatories of the Diversity Charter. We actively promote diversity, reduce resource consumption wherever possible, and compensate for unavoidable emissions. We want our work to help make the world more efficient, livable, and sustainable.\nHow to apply?\nHow to apply?\nHow to apply?\nSend your application here – we look forward to meeting you.\nPlease fill out our online application form completely. Your documents should include a cover letter, full résumé, employment references, and transcripts. A photograph is not needed.\nPorsche Consulting is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will be considered regardless of ethnic or social origin, age, gender, sexual identity, religion, worldview, or disability.\nSee our website for more information about joining Porsche Consulting: www.porsche-consulting.com.\nContact\nContact\nContact\nDo you have any questions regarding your application at Porsche Consulting? Our recruiting center will be happy to answer them for you from Monday to Friday between 3 p.m. and 7 p.m. by calling 0711 / 911 - 1 21 57. You can also use our FAQ section.\nWould you like to receive even more exciting information and get to know us better? Then take advantage of our numerous recruiting events and career fairs.\nFeel free to connect with us via LinkedIn:\nApply online now: ?ac=application&jobad_id=2021', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 41, 0, 771353), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
