{'job_title_name': 'Manager- Sustainability Policy Global DEU', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'First Solar', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/First-Solar-1?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad30odk6rc800&fromjk=7abc950b8f9b91ce', 'city': 'Deutschland', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 13, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=7abc950b8f9b91ce&bb=n1nIdf7XFVTzm_sLZO-GXNcG63SvonWxcqceKrgkD97E_-z5-Ge78ZR26pyFbHv7&xkcb=SoBq67M3HqSG4qA0D70MbzkdCdPP&fccid=1f66b9db983df9f4&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=120', 'job_description': 'First Solar reserves the right to offer you a role most applicable to your experience and skillset.\nBasic Job Functions:\nDesign and implement government affairs strategies to manage regulatory risk which could impact First Solar operations or its products in key markets.\nTrack, monitor and influence global sustainability legislative and regulatory developments affecting PV, focusing on waste, recycling and chemical policy, Ecolabel/Ecodesign, sustainable finance/sustainability reporting and environmental and human rights due diligence, in collaboration with U.S. and India GA.\nDevelop and manage internal and external positioning of the company on sustainability policy issues and form effective alliances to lever company position and sustainability differentiation.\nSupport the implementation of global sustainability advocacy strategies in collaboration with U.S. and India GA.\nEstablish and maintain relationships with key stakeholders involved in the drafting and amendment of dossiers in the regulatory process in the European Commission, European Parliament and the European Council as well as with scientific and policy advisors of the political groups and functions.\nEstablish and maintain relationships with opinion leaders in the regulatory discussions, including non-governmental organizations and societal stakeholders.\nTrack, monitor and effectively influence positioning of relevant industry, societal and environmental organizations and associations in the context of relevant sustainability policy discussions.\nParticipate and contribute to PV relevant sustainability positioning of EU and U.S. based industry trade associations.\nExperience:\n7+ years of relevant work experience in a public affairs or sustainability policy role in a multinational company, EU institution, consultancy or EU trade association required.\nExperience in sustainability issues (e.g. circular economy, recycling, waste and chemical policy, ecolabels, environmental and human rights due diligence) required.\nEstablished network within the EU institutions (Parliament, Commission) and EU community (industry associations, NGOs etc.)\nExcellent understanding of the regulatory processes within the EU institutions and the EU Member States.\nSuccessful track record of working on European affairs and working internationally.\nEducation:\nMasters degree (EU affairs, Environmental affairs, Sustainability policy, Natural Sciences, Political Science, Law)\nRequired Skills/Competencies:\nAbility to interact with and influence people at all levels inside, across groups and external to the company\nAbility to identify problems, develop and implement solutions, work independently and in collaboration with others, and build support for new programs and systems\nStrategic thinker who can manage long and short term projects\nAbility to work independently, manage multiple tasks and set priorities\nExcellent communication, writing and presentation skills\nAbility to exercise sound judgment\nWillingness to travel: Expected travel time up to 20%\nFluent in English and an additional EU language (French a plus)\nEssential Responsibilities:\nProactively develop targeted technology and sustainability messaging to promote company position among stakeholders\nDevelop and support compliance and advocacy strategies on global sustainability policy issues and influence key EU and national legislation relating to energy, waste, chemicals, CO2, human rights and sustainability reporting\nEngage with key stakeholders and stakeholder groups through EU and international forums, trade associations and working groups\nPrepare executive briefing documents for both internal and external audiences.\nReporting Relationships:\nReports to Global ESG & Sustainability Director\nNo direct reports\nTravel:\nInternational travel expected\nPhysical Requirements:\nOffice Physical Requirements:\nAll positions in our office require interaction with people and technology while either standing or sitting. In order to best service our customers, internal and external, all associates must be able to communicate face-to-face and on the phone with or without reasonable accommodation. First Solar is committed to compliance with its obligations under all applicable state and federal laws prohibiting employment discrimination. In keeping with this commitment, it attempts to reasonably accommodate applicants and employees in accordance with the requirements of the disability discrimination laws. It also invites individuals with disabilities to participate in a good faith, interactive process to identify reasonable accommodations that can be made without imposing an undue hardship.\nPotential candidates will meet the education and experience requirements provided on the above job description and excel in completing the listed responsibilities for this role.\nEqual Opportunity Employer Statement: First Solar is an Equal Opportunity Employer that values and respects the importance of a diverse and inclusive workforce. It is the policy of the company to recruit, hire, train and promote persons in all job titles without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, veteran status, disability, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We recognize that diversity and inclusion is a driving force in the success of our company.', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 41, 5, 151518), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
