{'job_title_name': 'Expert (m/f/d) for Life Cycle Assessment and Sustainability', 'job_type': 'Festanstellung', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'DENSO', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Denso?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad3rlu2gtd000&fromjk=344a04fef5bbd0ed', 'city': '85386 Eching', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 6, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=344a04fef5bbd0ed&bb=Uwn5OJhcTXXh-d6pe6vDN_kZOd5fjRg9njtL7LHQ1ebeEuphZV1ST_dzNqFDDtYE_gLXAXLWkIvEDgt34UeLjjRdixcgDvxKo_djxUoI_HY%3D&xkcb=SoDF67M3HqSB4KwSDx0NbzkdCdPP&fccid=dae59249f7edc321&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=50', 'job_description': 'Company Description\nAs an automotive supplier, DENSO is leading in developing and providing components and systems for heating, air conditioning, motor cooling, exhaust gas aftertreatment, automotive electrics and electronics and instrumentation.\nJob Description\nWe are looking for an\nExpert (m/f/d) for Life Cycle Assessment and Sustainability,\nlocated in Eching near Munich. As an expert for LCA and Sustainability reporting within DENSO International Europe, you will primarily be responsible for the Life Cycle Analysis of our products and processes. You will be working cross functional with different departments and manufacturing plants for the identification of hotspots within DENSO’s scope 1, 2 and 3.\nModelling and calculation of Product carbon footprints\nIdentification of hot spots within scope 1,2 and 3 by Life Cycle Assessment\nLead the creation of LCA reports towards internal and external stakeholders\nSupport our scope 1,2 related certification process with external companies\nCreate strategies and best practices for primary and secondary data use / analysis\nKeep up to date to latest guidelines and standards by participation in EU-wide workshops and represent DENSO as a company (Catena-X, CLEPA, etc.)\nCollection and interpretation of governmental regulations in regards to Sustainability, Circular Economy and Carbon Neutrality (CBAM, ELV directive, etc.)\nSupport the verification of PCF calculation methodologies with external partners\nSupport CO2 reduction initiatives based on fact-based LCIA results for circular economy and implementation of new technologies\nSupport with refining the DENSO sustainability strategy for scope 1,2 and 3 based on LCA results and market trends\nEnhance organizational capabilities for LCA calculations and a sustainable mindset by development and holding workshops and trainings\nSetting up IT-solutions for automized calculation\nQualifications\nBachelor’s or master’s degree with technical and/or sustainability background\nWorking experience of >2years is preferred, however we would like to give the chance to employees with less experience\nExperience and education in the area of LCA and sustainability reporting\nExperience with IT-tools (Umberto), Product Sustainability Platform, IMDS / IPCA, Python (not mandatory)\nExperience with databases and their usage\nPreferred: Knowledge in the area of materials and its production (Aluminum, Polymer, Steel, Copper)\nVery good English skills and good German skills (our business language is English)\nFast learner, proactive, flexible mindset, team player\nAdditional Information\nInternational company with various development opportunities\nOpen and diverse corporate culture\nWide range of trainings and education opportunities\n13 monthly salaries and optional allowances\n30 days of vacation and a flextime model for flexible working hours\nOpportunity for home office\nGenerous daily allowance for business trips\nModern offices, canteen onsite and free parking for employees\nFree coffee, tea and water\nEmployee benefits, such as attractive leasing offers, net salary optimization, additional private health insurance, free employee advice assistance hotline and much more.\nCompany events\nIt has come to our attention that various individuals have contacted people offering false employment opportunities with DENSO. Such scams are fraudulent and intended to steal from the victims.\nBy making you aware of this, we hope to avoid and ultimately stop victims from falling for this scam. Please do not provide any personal or financial information and do not send any money to anyone you suspect of recruitment fraud.\nIf you are contacted by someone whom you suspect may not be appropriately representing DENSO, please email: EU_DIEU_TALENTACQUISITION@eu.denso.com. Please forward the original email that you received that includes the original subject line and complete header information.\nDo not send CVs or vacancy applications to that email address as it will not be reviewed or considered. If you wish to apply for a job, please submit your application for an open position to https://careers.smartrecruiters.com/DENSOINTERNATIONALEUROPE', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 41, 32, 761360), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
