{'job_title_name': 'Manager Newsroom (f/m/d)', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Heidelberg Materials AG', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Heidelberg-Materials?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad3svij4ri800&fromjk=6f2f4d862edd89aa', 'city': 'Heidelberg', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 6, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=6f2f4d862edd89aa&bb=Uwn5OJhcTXXh-d6pe6vDN-oTrTP3d3aCVw1XC0xaA0gNhQHbyTWplOzRZRp1Gph7nTit2J_TaboG0SRKmm6LxrpKf1MA7rNa2eGXlj8hhOY%3D&xkcb=SoBi67M3HqSB4KwSDx0IbzkdCdPP&fccid=305a803957776ce6&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=50', 'job_description': "Job description\nProfessional\nEntry level\nHeidelberg, Germany\nLocation\nFull time\nContract\nMarketing & Communication\nCategory\nApply now\nAny Questions?\nLara Janna Pasaric\nTalent Acquisition Lead\nRecruitingGHR.DEUShared@heidelbergcement.com\nManager Newsroom (f/m/d)\nAre you a passionate communicator and networker with a strong instinct for great stories? If you are keen to engage people around our ambitious decarbonization journey and position Heidelberg Materials as a leader in the building materials industry, join us!\nWe are seeking a Manager Newsroom (f/m/d) for our Group Communication & Investor Relations Department. In this role, you will be part of the Corporate Communication team and drive editorial planning, channel coordination and day-to-day operations in our global newsroom.\nGroup Communication and Investor Relations play a crucial role in enhancing Heidelberg Materials' reputation and value among investors, policymakers, the public, employees, and customers as the frontrunner on the path to carbon neutrality and circular economy in the building materials industry.\nAs our new Newsroom Manager, you will report to the Head of Corporate Communications and be located in our headquarters in Heidelberg, Germany.\nYour next challenge\nYou will play a decisive role in proactively driving our content strategy and editorial planning process working closely with the Corporate Communication team and network of communicators around the world\nYou will further develop our global newsroom and manage all related processes (ownership of planning software, host all newsroom meetings)\nYou collaborate extensively with content and channel owners to identify relevant themes stories and communication activities\nYou develop and implement the right measures to increase relevance and reach of our content\nYour profile\nAt least 5 years of professional experience as a newsroom manager, editor-in-chief, in public relations or corporate communication in a large corporation or communication agency\nA degree in journalism/communication management/media relations\nProfound knowledge of corporate communication processes and channels as well as editorial planning\nAn intrinsic understanding of what makes a great story and excellent content creating skills for a variety of formats\nExceptional writing and expression skills in both German and English (being an English native speaker is a plus)\nInterested in current economic, social, and geopolitical issues\nOutstanding project and stakeholder management skills as well as strong analytical and conceptual skills\nTeam player with a strong sense of ownership, well organized, focused on high quality, creative, and able to multi-task\nOur offer\nWe are convinced that only those who successfully realize their personal goals can also fully contribute professionally. That's why we offer you attractive benefits, such as:\nFlexible working time models with up to 50% remote working within Germany\n30 vacation days plus additional special vacation days\nAttractive compensation with profit share/bonus, Christmas and vacation payment\nMultiple learning & development options: support of job-related further training, E-campus, various technical and leadership development programs\nJobTicket, JobBike and further special conditions and discounts for e.g. gyms\nCompany fitness room, various sports classes, health and prevention campaigns\nIndividual onboarding with buddy program as well as various networking initiatives (Network of Women, International Network etc.)\nModern headquarters next to the river Neckar with ergonomic workplaces and height-adjustable desks\nCanteen with discounted and healthy meals\nBicycle and underground parking with charging stations - for e-bike and car\n...and much more.\nWe look forward to receiving your online application!\nApply now", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 41, 34, 131191), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
