{'job_title_name': 'Intern (m/f/d) Global Business Entity Controlling', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Covestro', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Covestro?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad44dqipai801&fromjk=77e381f4429d1c40', 'city': '51373 Leverkusen', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 8, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=77e381f4429d1c40&bb=REbZEDoxKpQuhqk7WzQBnJS6i-8yjsyaWjidJfWCnksrvOOHMTpSQH7QBZ2855toODdtHi3Ynf6je2GP4AMlOM7cq54YEt9-jCUKvFfaz38%3D&xkcb=SoCG67M3HqSBwP2Q8p0BbzkdCdPP&fccid=a204805f388c4ee8&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=70', 'job_description': "We are Covestro. We are curious. We are courageous. We are colorful. We refine chemical material solutions with game-changing products. Let us empower you to push boundaries. Join us and our 18.150 colleagues now and together we will make the world a brighter place.\nWHAT WE OFFER\nOur Controlling team collaborates with a broad range of departments and functions at Covestro to generate relevant business insights. Our work enables the Covestro management to fully understand relevant information, take the right decisions and implement action plans through tailored business partnering. We constantly develop and refine our tools and processes to reflect state-of-the-art standards in data analytics, reporting, forecasting, planning and business steering, which include statistical, machine learning and BI applications. Furthermore our Controlling department plays an essential role in one of our currently most important projects – making Covestro fully circular in the future. During your internship you will work in Performance Materials Controlling, a department in the CFO area that supports Covestro's largest business entity.\nYour tasks and responsibilities:\nSupport financial planning and forecasting processes, as well as subsequently track and analyse forecast deviations in order to help the management to efficiently run the operative business\nHelp to prepare strategy conferences and take part in strategic projects which help Covestro to achieve its sustainability goals\nPerform detailed profitability analyses for different product groups and regions with the help of statistical models\nReview and analyze marketing, sales and manufacturing costs in order to help Covestro meet its cost targets\nPreparing presentations and reports for Covestro's high level management team\nContribute and support in ad hoc analysis of relevant business data and project related tasks, e.g. circular economy and energy-efficiency projects\nConceptual work, including the optimization of existing tools, applications and processes\nWHAT YOU OFFER\nYou are a Bachelor or Master student (m/f/d) in Controlling, Accounting, Finance or a comparable course of study\nIdeally, you have already gained some practical experience in Controlling, Accounting or Finance\nYou have good user skills in MS Office (especially Excel and PowerPoint), high command of digitalization and automation skills desirable (e.g. R, Python, VBA)\nYou have an analytical mindset and enjoy communicating concepts and ideas with stakeholders on a global level\nYou are able to multi-task and achieve a high quality standard at the same time\nExcellent English skills are required, German is desirable\nPlease note, the duration of the internship is 4 to preferably 6 months. After the first training sessions in Leverkusen office, mobile working within Germany will be definitely possible.\nPlease also let us know your possible starting date as well as the duration and apply with your complete documents (cover letter, CV, certificates, enrollment certificate, examination/study regulations).\nIf you have any questions regarding the application process, please do not hesitate to contact our Recruiting Team (recruiting@covestro.com).\nYOUR APPLICATION\nAre you curious, courageous and colorful as we are? If so, we can offer you exciting career opportunities. We look forward to receiving your application including a cover letter, your resume, certificates as well as your salary expectations and your notice period. Become part of our Team - apply now!\nAnyone who wants to contribute to a better world with Covestro can also expect a lot.\nWe want you to feel at home at Covestro. To feel you’re treated fairly and transparently. That means financial security, a healthy work-life balance and generous benefits.\nSpecifically, it means for us: flexible working hours, the compatibility of family and work, active health promotion and the ability to convert part of your salary into long-term or retirement savings. And that's not all.\nSounds exciting? Find out more about Covestro and our benefits here:\nhttps://www.career.covestro.de/de/about-covestro/covestro-as-an-employer/employee-benefits\nContact Us\nCovestro welcomes applications from all individuals, regardless of racial or ethnic origin, skin color, nationality, religion, philosophy, gender, age, disability, appearance or sexual identity. We are committed to treating all applicants fairly and avoiding discrimination.", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 41, 41, 656713), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
