{'job_title_name': '(Senior) Manager Sustainability Portfolio & Operations', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Fresenius Medical Care', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Fresenius-Medical-Care?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad45cujkuq806&fromjk=145119b408362a44', 'city': '61352 Bad Homburg vor der Höhe', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 8, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=145119b408362a44&bb=REbZEDoxKpQuhqk7WzQBnJgEjsSL_1PxmYLTHV5H95G4WMnL7TwKldAvALnjc2jP7thllRoHyVuDcOd0QONIfMaJxxZ8HyUfg4Z49Cm6Q0M%3D&xkcb=SoCv67M3HqSBwP2Q8p0DbzkdCdPP&fccid=8de1633f2f8eae1d&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=70', 'job_description': "POSITION OVERVIEW AND\nPURPOSE :\nFresenius Medical Care, an EUR 18 billion company and largest kidney care provider in the world, is seeking a Manager Sustainability Portfolio and Operations (m/f/d) to join our Global Sustainability Team. The Manager Sustainability Portfolio and Operations (m/f/d) will be responsible for sustainability assessments, portfolio and change management.\nWe are looking for an experienced sustainability ambassador, comfortable in managing complex projects with multiple stakeholders. You have a strong interest in sustainability topics. You will work in a highly motivated, international team that is driven by the ambition to shape the sustainable future of Fresenius Medical Care.\nWHAT WE OFFER:\nWe believe: Meaningful work must also be rewarded. That's why we offer you a wide range of services and benefits, including pension plans, healthcare and career development. However, we provide much more than that for the satisfaction of our employees. For example, showing appreciation for one another as an integral part of our corporate culture. Or flexible working hours to fit with your personal life.\nPRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:\nDevelops, performs, and improves global sustainability assessments autonomously, including monitoring of sustainability risks, opportunities, and regulations/requirements as well as scenario analysis\nDevelops and monitors global sustainability targets and roadmaps proactively\nSupports and consults business units regarding sustainability initiatives as well as with their management autonomously, including requirements analysis, benchmarking, development of action plans, performance monitoring, audit readiness, trainings and other communication measures\nIndependently develops and improves global standards and processes for sustainability management and reporting according to best practices\nManages portfolio independently, including monitoring of scope, development of standards and tools to increase accuracy and efficiency, oversight of different channels, stakeholder management•\nContinuously keeps up to date in areas of expertise, proactively provides expert input to projects as well as support requests and shares expert knowledge through dedicated communication channels\nProvides transparency about the availability of resources as well as the status of projects on a regular basis• Supports the sustainability leadership team with the prioritization of projects proactively\nProactively supports with the audit management and communication activities• Proactively supports with the continued development of the global sustainability strategy • Supports with the collection, consolidation, and analysis of sustainability data, as needed\nEDUCATION:\nAcademic degree in environmental science/management/technologies or sustainability management or similar\nEXPERIENCE AND REQUIRED SKILLS:\n5+ years’ work experience in an international EHS department, experience in climate protection management, global environmental targets and circular economy or experience in an international consulting company in the area of sustainability management or similar experience in project management and product management\nExcellent interpersonal skills and strong intercultural skills\nUnderstanding of complex organizational dynamics\nStrong process-oriented, structured and conscientious working method\nExcellent analytical skills for continuous improvement\nStrong service attitude, ability to handle various tasks simultaneously, professionalism, strong team player, self-motivating\nAbility to prioritize and integrate a large number of stakeholder perspectives\nAble to work in a target-oriented mode with a mix of routine activities and new as well as changing processes\nBackground in change management beneficial\nAbility to work independently, result oriented, strong team player, strong service attitude, self-motivating\nExperience with IT tools for sustainability reporting\nKnowledge of sustainability reporting, including standards such as GRI and EU Taxonomy\nSolid presentation skills\nExcellent English language skills", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 41, 42, 675412), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
