{'job_title_name': 'Hub Supply Chain Sustaintability Leader', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Hitachi Energy', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Hitachi-Energy?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad45p42bbt000&fromjk=4aeb2605e5b62cd5', 'city': 'Bad Honnef', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 8, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=4aeb2605e5b62cd5&bb=REbZEDoxKpQuhqk7WzQBnKNnxFDP5Vpsw2q7qZhloQxNHTbs1m15EPsO5t_pGWggp5VyjufhiJCRd16f8G7y4SOWd3gmJDztv7FbgQollMA%3D&xkcb=SoDy67M3HqSBwP2Q8p0NbzkdCdPP&fccid=8774bcbf6844c59c&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=70', 'job_description': 'Working within the Transformers Business Unit Global Team, you will drive the\nHub Supply Chain Sustainability Leader\nagenda. Contribute to design and implement a sustainable and transformational changes across the SCM processes and tools. Collaborate across the value chain in order to support the customer requirements with the SCM Sustainability information. On-board and increase the maturity level of internal and external stakeholders.\nYour responsibilities\nDrive the Hub SCM sustainability agenda: Create a Hub SCM Sustainability roadmap, aligned with the BU and global SCM Sustainability strategy and in collaboration with Category managers\nInvestigate global sustainability trends in the Power Grids industry and provide inputs to SCM management, benchmark on practices form other internal and external businesses.\nLead further implementation of materials compliance processes in supply chain in support to other functions (e.g: Conflict Minerals, Cobalt, SCIP, REACH and RoHS) and adherence to those regulation.\nExecute on the deployment of the sustainability agenda related to legal requirement such as German Supply Chain Act, CBAM, etc…\nSustainable supply base management: Lead the Supplier sustainability development program expansion in PGTR including participating in critical supplier assessments and resolution of non-conformities.\nDeploy the Ecovadis assessments as a specific dedicated in order to reach the company targets. Promote low carbon circular economy practices in supply base (e.g: zero waste for suppliers, sustainable packaging introduction, recycling)\nMaterial sustainability data collection: Collect and analyze specific sustainability data such as CO2 emission levels, share of recycled materials from the production of supplier raw materials and products and influence the global sourcing strategies to achieve sustainable supply base.\nContinuous Improvement culture and Improvement Projects: Act as change agent and champion of a continuous improvement culture focused on waste elimination across the organization using ITM lean and SCM methods, such as CIPS, Dynamic Evolution, SCRM, Leader Standard Work, Practical Problem Solving, Value Stream Mapping, Kaizen.\nSuggest, and facilitate the development of Cost-out and productivity projects across the business to achieve targets. Facilitate and train team members in utilization of SCM reporting of Improvement projects. Ensure effective sustainment of results and support problem solving (Root Cause Countermeasure) as needed to close gaps to targets.\nKPI Management: Create dashboards for easy info access and multi-layers (from consolidation to adequate breakdown) reporting.\nCommunication: Structure, collect and organize the information related to the Sustainability activities and prepare report with the aim to provide information useful at execution level.,\nPeople Capability, Training and Coaching: Build continuous sustainability capability through training and implementation adequate tools and methods. Possibly contribute to update the related LOM3.0 processes and SCM tools\nYour background\nMore than 10 years of experience in an equivalent industry.\nA demonstrated leadership in an international environment together with a continuous improvement mindset.\nProject/program management skills enables you to bring value end to end from project feasibility and definition to the implementation of the measures to sustain the change.\nKnowledge of SAP Ariba, SAP4 Hana, Ecovadis is a plus.\nA collaborative, solutions-oriented approach and strong communication skills.\nBasic Info\nLocation\nBad Honnef, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany\nMonselice, Padova, Italy\nJob type\nFull time\nExperience\nExperienced\nJob function\nSupply Chain\nContract\nRegular\nPublication date\n2023-09-29\nReference number\nHQ55244191\nShare this job', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 41, 42, 978090), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
