{'job_title_name': 'LCA Sustainability Consultant (d/f/m)', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Cognizant Technology Solutions', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Cognizant-Technology-Solutions?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad49g3k6po800&fromjk=e9f127f8c7702131', 'city': 'München', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 9, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=e9f127f8c7702131&bb=F8vLymfFuqJlcCl-GlSLJT66_ekOcCzeJ3SDqXWccO-BG-ffrhKeJsl5e4wJC9QM&xkcb=SoAN67M3HqSBzeg0bD0JbzkdCdPP&fccid=2df6a1e69a70a1e7&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=80', 'job_description': "What makes Cognizant a unique place to work? The combination of rapid growth and an international and innovative environment! This is creating a lot of opportunities for people like YOU - people with an ambitious spirit who want to make a difference in this world.\nCognizant's delivery model infused with a distinct culture of high customer happiness. We consistently deliver positive relationships, cost reductions, and business results. Be one of our change-makers and join the success story: we are looking for a\nLCA Sustainability Consultant (d/f/m)\nLocation: Germany - hybrid\nThe\nOpportunity\nAre you passionate and experienced in working on challenging projects in circular economy, sustainable supply chain, low emission transportation and environment friendly industry? Do you have a personality who likes to drive transformations, leave impact and make change?\nWe are looking for an energetic advisor with a focus on quality and delivering value to our clients and leaving impact internally and externally.\nYour Key Result Areas\nDesigning strategies to automate the LCA process and enable companies to conduct LCAs on hundreds or thousands of products. Communicate results and recommendations to clients and stakeholders\nTake part of client projects in the manufacturing and logistics sector, analyzing environmental footprint of products, processes within the factory and in the upstream/downstream supply chain\nConducting LCA studies using data analytics tools and software. Supporting the development of ecodesign strategies and sustainable procurement practices. Continuously developing your knowledge and skills in the field of LCA and sustainable manufacturing.\nSetting up data management and strategy, KPI development and performance measurement process to improve sustainability metrics of products and sustainability reporting according to the new European requirements.\nJoin executive meetings and help business development and sales team in formulating the value propositions in sustainable operations and transformations.\nParticipate actively in mentoring internal team on sustainability and ESG regulations, creating reusable content and offers, thought leadership, webinars, podcasts, and creating new advisory frameworks.\nYour Qualification\nAt least a bachelor’s degree in a scientific or engineering subject with a sustainability component (e.g. industrial ecology, sustainability economy, environmental engineering, environmental science, applied physics, etc.).\nExtensive hands-on experience with LCA in manufacturing sector and product companies.\nFamiliarity with LCA standards such as ISO 14040 and Product Environmental Footprint (PEF)\nPassion for sustainability and understanding of the principles of ecodesign and sustainable procurement. First experience in management consulting and hands-on projects.\nBeing familiar with digital solutions and technologies related to LCA, software solutions such as Simapro, Gabi, OpenLCA, etc.\nStrong analytical skills and experience with data analytics tools and software\nKeen interest in digital technology and its potential to measure environmental impact\nStrong written and verbal communication skills. Fluency in German and English is a must\nWhat you can expect\nAn organization driven by technology – We have a\ntremendous technology backbone\nOpen, ‘can do’ team spirit\nAn environment\nwhere you can make your own ideas reality\nDrive your own career\nMarket conform benefits\nOur strength is built on our ability to work together. Our many backgrounds offer different perspectives and new ways of thinking. It encourages lively discussions, inspires thought leadership, and helps us build better solutions for our clients. We are looking for someone who drives in this setting and is inspired to craft significant solutions through true collaboration.\nAbout Cognizant\nCognizant is one of the world’s leading professional services companies, transforming clients’ business, operating, and technology models for the digital era. Our unique industry-based, consultative approach helps clients envision, build, and run more innovative and efficient businesses. Headquartered in the U.S., Cognizant, a member of the NASDAQ-100, is ranked 205 on the Fortune 500 and is consistently listed among the most admired companies in the world. We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company.\nEmployee Status :\nFull Time Employee\nShift :\nDay Job\nTravel :\nNo\nJob Posting :\nNov 09 2023\nAbout Cognizant\nCognizant (Nasdaq-100: CTSH) is one of the world's leading professional services companies, transforming clients' business, operating and technology models for the digital era. Our unique industry-based, consultative approach helps clients envision, build and run more innovative and efficient businesses. Headquartered in the U.S., Cognizant is ranked 185 on the Fortune 500 and is consistently listed among the most admired companies in the world. Learn how Cognizant helps clients lead with digital at www.cognizant.com or follow us @Cognizant.", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 41, 46, 990638), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
