{'job_title_name': 'Master Thesis: Development of a green reactor for wastewater treatment', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Interfacial Engineering and Biotechnology', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Fraunhofer--gesellschaft?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad4abhipai801&fromjk=6fa1e3f1852a9b57', 'city': 'Stuttgart', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 9, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=6fa1e3f1852a9b57&bb=F8vLymfFuqJhY4puAmwIHkM5bbesUt_FxleDgl73SZNAXnQVBuR39-2v6aXUc2Kp&xkcb=SoAk67M3HqSBzeg0bD0LbzkdCdPP&fccid=e5f8a07abbcb2ad4&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=80', 'job_description': "The Fraunhofer-Gesellschaft (www.fraunhofer.com) currently operates 76 institutes and research institutions throughout Germany and is the world’s leading applied research organization. Around 30 000 employees work with an annual research budget of 2.9 billion euros.\nThe Fraunhofer Institute for Interfacial Engineering and Biotechnology IGB develops and optimizes processes, technologies, and products for health, sustainable chemistry and the environment.\nFraunhofer IGB is one of 76 institutes and research units of the Fraunhofer-Gesellschaft, the world’s leading applied research organization.\nWhat you will do\nStart date: October 2022\nTo achive a sustainable circular economy, environmentally friendly wastewater treatment is a key step. A promising approach is to combine green treatment technologies to eliminate the maximum possible amount of pollutants in wastewater. In this project, the performance of a new reactor shall be demonstrated at laboratory scale to determine the target parameters of a pilot plant.\nLiterature review (state of the art and current research, working methods and efficiency determination).\nPlanning and construction of laboratory setups, design of experiment (DoE), and conduct of experiments.\nData evaluation, interpretation, comparison with literature, and presentation of results.\nWhat you bring to the table\nYou are a student of process engineering, chemical engineering, environmental engineering, chemistry, mechanical engineering, or related field.\nYou have expierience working in chemical laboratories.\nYou are confident working independently and you are a good communicator.\nYou are computer literate (MS Office).\nYou are able to lead a scientific discussion in English (or in German).\nIt is possible to conduct the work completely in English.\nYou will be encouraged to operate independently supported by our scientific and technical experts.\nWe value and promote the diversity of our employees' skills and therefore welcome all applications - regardless of age, gender, nationality, ethnic and social origin, religion, ideology, disability, sexual orientation and identity. Severely disabled persons are given preference in the event of equal suitability.\nWith its focus on developing key technologies that are vital for the future and enabling the commercial utilization of this work by business and industry, Fraunhofer plays a central role in the innovation process. As a pioneer and catalyst for groundbreaking developments and scientific excellence, Fraunhofer helps shape society now and in the future.\nInterested? Apply online now. We look forward to getting to know you!\nFor organizational or administrative questions please contact Britta Munz\nE-Mail: bewerbung@igb.fraunhofer.de\nFraunhofer Institute for Interfacial Engineering and Biotechnology IGB\nRequisition Number: 52683 Application Deadline:", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 41, 47, 819091), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
