{'job_title_name': 'Researcher - Circular Engineering (m/f/d)', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'HITACHI EUROPE S.A.S. (FRANCE)', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Hitachi-Europe-S.a.s.-(france)?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad55q1k6po800&fromjk=1802e346d1ad1b80', 'city': '40547 Düsseldorf', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 1, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=1802e346d1ad1b80&bb=MSzRphRNzJEIFv98cQRXfHjHj7pg8fnTRmSusPF6oAymD2QdxI6X-zNzAGYZ0aBSvjoHTKq5l0ffYCsh0PiNG1B4mKXfuf5tIsXAyq5kJP8%3D&xkcb=SoDH67M3HqSeG6WeNh0BbzkdCdPP&fccid=5f2d896e411ed206&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=0', 'job_description': "Description\nOur Company\nHitachi is one of the world's leading companies in Social Innovation Business striving to offer sustainable solutions to our modern society. Energy & Mobility, Connected Industries and Digital solutions are the key segments of our offering. Hitachi’s product range has significantly changed over the past years to become a climate change innovator helping to achieve a sustainable society. More than 320,000 employees work together every day to deliver products improving people’s quality of life.\nThe Corporate R&D of Hitachi in Europe, via its “Autonomy and Circularity” Laboratory with bases in Sophia Antipolis (near Nice, France) and Munich (Germany), gives the opportunity to the postholder to be involved in the Circular Economy and Smart Manufacturing areas, and related activities in academia and standardization, as well as in a variety of different other sectors (e.g. IoT Solutions, Supply Chain optimization, Green Mobility), with projects of global significance, and to become part of a cutting-edge applied-research team. The postholder will conceive and develop innovative technologies/solutions incorporating data engineering or system engineering expertise.\nYour accountability and responsibilities:\nGround-breaking research on “Product Circular Economy”, development of algorithm specifications, coding, and evaluation/validation of software functions will be carried out in collaboration with colleagues at global level.\nCreation of research proposals, also based on customer and trends requirements, and of intellectual property footprint following established methods, procedures and company conventions to a high quality in line with agreed schedules and requirements.\nTechnical management of R&D Projects, delivery of Projects results, and identification / understanding of (new) customers’ challenges and requirements, following established methods, procedures and company conventions to a high quality in line with agreed schedules and requirements.\nSupport of Hitachi events and business activities with respect to the above-mentioned topics.\nPresentation of activities and outcomes to R&D group colleagues, and possibly to stakeholders; as well as at conferences of high impact papers for journal publication.\nCollaboration with universities / research institutes, and possibly with other companies, to maximize research outcomes and expand research activity.\nYour profile:\nCandidate should have MSs or equivalent degree, preferably at Circular Engineering or other Engineering fields such as mechanical engineering, or material engineering.\nCandidate should have proven industrial experience related to circular economy or sustainable production or sustainable supply chain management.\nExperience with programming Python.\nExperience with the integration of SW and HW components in prototype environment (for example in test machineries).\nExperience with databases handling and/or data-generating sensors.\nSkills in technical writing and project management.\nKnowledge of Mechanical Engineering or Systems Dynamics Modelling (e.g. Material flow modelling) would be considered a “\nplus\n”.\nExperience in Business Analytics and Carbon accounting would be considered a “\nplus\n”.\nExperience in business analysis on Circular Economy of capital equipment products would be considered as “\nplus\n”\nExperience in statistics, artificial intelligence / machine learning, and / or computer vision would be considered a “\nplus\n”.\nA good team player, ability to build and maintain strong relationships with stakeholders, show strong skills of agility, creativity, flexibility and passion.\nPassionate about societal challenges.\nWillingness to travel within Europe, and eventually to Japan and/or to US.\nFluent in oral and written English.\nOur Values\nWe strive to create an inclusive environment for all and we are proud to say we are an equal opportunity employer.\nWith Japanese roots going back over 100 years, our culture is founded on the values of our parent company expressed as the Hitachi Spirit:\nWa - Harmony, Trust, Respect\nMakoto - Sincerity, Fairness, Honesty, Integrity\nKaitakusha-Seishin - Pioneering Spirit, Challenge", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 42, 15, 948701), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
