{'job_title_name': 'Consultant Battery Recycling (all genders)', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Accenture', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Accenture?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad5i0dk78s800&fromjk=79bd3de32e7cf699', 'city': '80807 München', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 3, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=79bd3de32e7cf699&bb=dEtWVynr6FPh3yvcM75wLJ8xXZgrfgvJAZQtMC6dKRLQvaEXnvWmYGtswvgEa-4ineWpKRrvdKQIfLqJVYBORMgwBqfK4Cf4pJy0BSgRDtM%3D&xkcb=SoDT67M3HqSebSAwoD0PbzkdCdPP&fccid=a4e4e2eaf26690c9&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=20', 'job_description': "#industry4.0 #digitaletransformation\nBecome part of our team and shape your career in process consulting as a consultant in the digital transformation of industrial manufacturing.\nYour Mission:\nYou are actively shaping the energy transition by enabling the wide adoption of energy storage technology with our clients in Germany and all over the world. You are collaborating with Accenture experts from strategy consulting to technical battery experts to conduct (market) research, develop tools and models, and offer services based on deep technical expertise in the whole field of (post) lithium-ion batteries. Through our go-to-market strategy, customized business models, market analysis, and technical expertise, you empower clients in the whole battery value chain, from raw materials to end-customer applications and recycling. You stay ahead by keeping up with technical and market advancements, acquiring new projects and clients, while enjoying an entrepreneurial environment with unlimited growth opportunities.\nWhat you can expect:\nProject work\nYou provide expert guidance to customers on battery recycling processes and define technical specifications for equipment/processes. You develop and execute go-to-market strategies, customized business models, market analyses, and supply chain strategies for the clients in battery recycling and circular economy.\nBusiness development\nDepending on level, you acquire new projects/clients in the battery value chain focusing on battery and material production and recycling. You stay up to date with the latest advancements in sustainability, battery recycling markets, and new recycling technologies.\nPortfolio development\nYou strengthen the recycling segment in the battery team while collaborating with other cross-functional groups. You conduct research and develop internal database & services around battery mass manufacturing.\nWhat we are looking forward to\nMaster or Diploma degree in process engineering, chemical engineering, chemistry/metallurgy, or related fields; doctorate is a plus.\nMinimum 2 years of experience and in-depth knowledge of battery recycling processes, metallurgy, or similar topics; experience in consulting is a plus.\nBasic understanding of sustainability and circularity principles, waste management, life cycle assessments, reverse logistics, battery recycling markets, and/or environmental regulations.\nOutstanding communication skills, strong analytical and conceptual abilities, and the flexibility to travel temporarily/work at customer site.\nBusiness fluent command in English and preferably German, additional languages are a plus.\nWhat we offer you\nCreative freedom through flat hierarchies, flexible working-time models and the option of an individual home-office hybrid model.\nCompetitive salary and an extensive company social benefit package including a company pension scheme, employee discounts, the option to participate in our employee share purchase plan and much, much more!\nA comprehensive training catalogue to optimally qualify our employees for the demands of the market and inhouse training sessions from colleagues to colleagues.\nAn unlimited supply of coffee, drinks and bugs to fix.\nYou and Accenture\nIn this role, you'll be part of Accenture Industry X.\nWe connect #engineering and #manufacturing with data and technologies. This is how we empower our clients to realign their product and value chains with digital twins, smart assets and connected manufacturing processes - for the industry of the future.\nThe Accenture culture: Here, YOU are the catalyst for change\nYour unique combination of skills, personality, and aspirations sets you apart. When distinct talents, strengths, and perspectives merge, the result is nothing short of extraordinary: ideas that propel the world forward. This is we champion diversity and personal development at Accenture. Create a working environment where you truly thrive; with responsibilities that resonate deeply; with a workload that is perfectly aligned with your capabilities; and methods that are tailored to your objectives. How you wish to connect, further your development, and personally evolve rests in your hands. This is your career. We are mere facilitators, helping you shape it exactly as you envision.\nGet in contact\nAny questions? Then contact our Recruiting Team via email at EAS-HR@accenture.com.\nWe are looking forward to receiving your application!", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 42, 28, 259196), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
