{'job_title_name': 'Global Technology Manager Fuel Cells (m/f/d)', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'BASF Environmental Catalysts and Metal Solutions', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Basf-df1bf734?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad5jaqipbb802&fromjk=8b1f1046ab230fc6', 'city': '30173 Hannover', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 4, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=8b1f1046ab230fc6&bb=Uv-lHqeCsQQIU8SlztWmU7HEiI83Ri2wr9bq_o9YOhLfwbrL5FfcWqHejfNiAPyV&xkcb=SoBK67M3HqSebqQ8LR0ObzkdCdPP&fccid=38313780e9822361&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=30', 'job_description': "Global Technology Manager Fuel Cells (m/f/d)\nHannover, DE, 30173\nLeveraging its deep expertise as the global leader in catalysis and precious metals, BASF Environmental Catalyst and Metal Solutions (ECMS) serves customers in many industries including automotive, aerospace, indoor air quality, semiconductors and hydrogen economy, and provides full loop services with its precious metals trading and recycling offering. With a focus on circular solutions and sustainability, ECMS is committed to helping our customers create a cleaner, more sustainable world. Protecting our elements of life is our purpose and this inspires us to ever-new solutions. ECMS operates globally in 15 countries with approximately 20 production sites and over 4,000 employees.\nRESPONSIBILITIES\nThe Global Technology Manager Fuel Cells has the overarching task to:\nhelp broadening BASF’s expertise and market prospects in electrocatalysts, catalyst coated membranes (CCMs) and other CCM components for hydrogen fuel cells, by connecting and coordinating hydrogen stakeholders in the relevant research and technology units at BASF and ECMS and its joint ventures, as well as external research institutions\nconvey BASF’s capabilities to existing and potential future customers/collaborators, in order to identify potential new business opportunities and make sure they are being followed through by R&D and commercial units\nto bear responsibility for intellectual property (IP) for the fuel cell segment and ensure that relevant IP is filed and monitored (point person with ECMS legal team for FTO decisions)\nDue to the extreme dynamic and complexity of the underlying, multi-sector market, effective relationship and interface management will be key. For the same reason, the market intelligence and communication aspect will be more pronounced than usual. The field’s strategic importance to ECMS also triggers an above-average level of internal communication requirements, including occasional management briefings.\nQUALIFICATIONS / REQUIREMENTS\nPhD in chemistry or a related discipline, with experience in catalysis and automotive\nA minimum of 8 years experience in the field of catalysis and automotive\nUnderstanding of the precious metals markets is preferred.\nDemonstrated strength in establishing and maintaining strong relationships with internal and/or external customers and/or suppliers\nAbility to influence decision-makers and to drive actions/decisions in a complex environment\nProblem-solving skills, with demonstrated ability to develop and implement creative solutions while working in a heterogenous, multi-functional team\nOutstanding verbal and written skills paired with high motivation, self-starter mentality and strong organizational skills\nWillingness to travel (moderate level)\nBENEFITS\nAttractive salary with additional bonus option, based on company's success and your individual performance.\nDevelopment discussions and programs so that you can reach your full potential.\nPension program and employer-funded nursing care insurance.\nSubsidies for the company fitness program at Hansefit and for childcare in a local care group.\nFlexible work arrangements whenever possible.\nWe are looking forward to your online application at careers.basf-catalystsmetals.com or via email to andreas.waldhoff@basf-catalystsmetals.com.\nPaper applications are also welcome, but please note that we do not return paper applications including folders. Address: BASF Catalysts Germany GmbH, Human Resources, Seligmannallee 1, D-30173 Hannover, Germany.\nDo you have any questions about the application process or the position? Please reach out to: Andreas Waldhoff, phone: +49(0)172 - 535 1984", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 42, 29, 662010), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
