{'job_title_name': 'Masterand (m/w/d) Batterietechnik', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'FEV Europe GmbH', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Fev-Europe?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad5jdqjkuq802&fromjk=b7e3ffa0c0cb7cfd', 'city': 'Aachen', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 4, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=b7e3ffa0c0cb7cfd&bb=Uv-lHqeCsQSBBWZ8oRkwKmUlW6Tl6K_P00aCqkW2QYLx9wEy9yUhVCBOWz5mzllC&xkcb=SoBw67M3HqSebqQ8LR0IbzkdCdPP&fccid=c5e4d44efdaf77fe&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=30', 'job_description': 'We offer a thesis (Master) in the field of battery system development and circular economy to answer the following research question: "How does the new EU directive on battery recycling influence the total cost of ownership of EVs".\nThe introduction of the battery passport with the compulsory disclosure of information for the battery reuse, the gradual increase in recycling efficiency for key raw materials as well as the introduction of recycled active materials poses challenges which potentially increase the cost of development, production, logistics and disposal of automotive batteries on one hand, on the other hand opens the possibility of exploiting circular lifecycles.\nThe proposed thesis, shall investigate these topics with help of case studies, which are technically and economically reasonable. The focus here is on the combination of technical specifications and economic considerations.\nThe open position is particularly suitable for students of electrical and mechanical engineering, especially in combination with economics. Prior experience in the following areas is useful for successful completion of the master\'s thesis:\nGeneral design of electrical powertrains.\nRequired soft skills:\nquick comprehension\nindependent way of working\nworking well in a team\ninterest in publishing researc