{'job_title_name': 'Life Cycle Assessment Consultant (m/w/d)', 'job_type': 'Festanstellung', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Mitsubishi Chemical', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Mitsubishi-Chemical?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad5v1uj30g800&fromjk=bcef294492e9feb7', 'city': 'Wiesbaden', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 2, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=bcef294492e9feb7&bb=5ZPnWC31O8Xekme-YSmbTudD4MwX6vww6bAF2bHE-qyBF9ch3RWsafzxAso0Nv1E5HB-Tq6ii2dyKJce_08C4jR9-ZD0DwuQ-gv78QWwJYk%3D&xkcb=SoCr67M3HqSebZw3lR0IbzkdCdPP&fccid=66d7603179ba5b0e&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=10', 'job_description': 'Life Cycle Assessment Consultant (m/w/d) - hybrid\nThe Mitsubishi Chemical Group is a specialty materials provider with an unwavering commitment to forging innovative solutions. We possess extensive expertise and leadership in material science within the core market segments of Mobility, Digital, Food and Healthcare. By providing advanced chemistry-based solutions our 70,000 employees enable industry transformation, develop technological advancements, and create more fruitful lives for the global population. Delivering on the core elements of our slogan - “Science. Value. Life.”\nAbout the role:\nYou will support the activities of our company in the area of environmental assessment of products to meet recent regulations and market expectations as a devoted member of the Global LCA Competence Center. This will be performed by conducting life cycle assessments and carbon footprint assessments according to ISO standards in the EMEA region. A further purpose is to advocate the business units in all LCA-related questions from procurement to sales. As part of our KAITEKI philosophy, you will support and guide our company towards a more sustainable future.\nYour Responsibilities:\nProviding guidance and supporting the implementation of LCA projects with a strong focus on energy & climate, as well as the circular economy\nCoordinating customer\'s inquiries regarding sustainability and LCA performance\nGenerating new life cycle inventories and conducting quality checks, as well as monitoring developments in the LCA field\nBuild up, validate and evaluate LCA models and evaluate them ideally in Sphera LCA for Experts software according to company\'s internal standards\nPreparation of LCA 3rd party reports and background documentation of a broad product portfolio for European business groups and headquarters in Japan\nSupporting the management of relationships between LCA service providers (suppliers), the various departments of the company, and other external stakeholders, such as suppliers and customers\nInvolvement in the organization of global KAITEKI meetings LCA-part and representing Mitsubishi Chemical at external LCA conferences, events, workshops, etc.\nYour Skills:\nUniversity degree in Chemical / Environmental engineering, Chemistry-related natural sciences\nExperience in product life cycle assessment (LCA), product carbon footprint (PCF), product environmental footprint (PEF), related standards such as ISO 14044, ISO 14067 and GHG Protocol understanding of chemical processes\nFirst related experience in softwares, such as GaBi, SimaPro or similar\nAbility to influence and communicate effectively with a variety of internal and external stakeholders\nBusiness fluency in English (German and/or French is an advantage)\nSustainability mindset, committed to guiding and supporting improvements towards a more sustainable future, as well as a cultural awareness and experience in working in an international environment\nIndependent working style and excellent communication skills\nWhat could you expect ?\nOur corporate culture is based on the values of integrity, respect, bravery, collaboration, and persistence, we call it "Our Way". With our approach, together we can shape a more sustainable, progressive and brighter version of the world.\nWe offer you a secure job position in a pleasant and collegial environment, offering engaging and responsible tasks within an international setting.\nFlat hierarchies and mutual respect are second nature. Moreover, you\'ll enjoy an appealing compensation package and comprehensive social benefits, including bonuses, a company pension plan, health offerings, employee discounts, Job bicycle leasing and some more.\nWe believe in the power of people with diverse values, viewpoints, and expertise. Our aim is the wellbeing of people and the planet – a concept we call KAITEKI. We are committed to creating an inclusive and diverse environment.\nAre you curious about this position? Become part of our team and contribute with your talents. Send us your application via our Application Portal.', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 42, 41, 706610), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
