{'job_title_name': 'Global Key Account Manager', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Stora Enso', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Stora-Enso?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad60bck6r4800&fromjk=6df2e3296009f9be', 'city': 'Düsseldorf', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 2, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=6df2e3296009f9be&bb=5ZPnWC31O8Xekme-YSmbThZWIUxGh17RDbBWS4O2Zcj_6xd7vEwKZo3LaRJHrSXAGsprw8_Xq9NkwpPQOev4_PSE17W31cvk0Ex0rQJzP2A%3D&xkcb=SoCR67M3HqSebZw3lR0ObzkdCdPP&fccid=c2e5bfabfeace5ba&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=10', 'job_description': "Global Key Account Manager\nThe Packaging Materials division is a global leader in the circular economy with our premium renewable and recyclable packaging materials based on both virgin and recycled fiber. Addressing the needs of today's eco-conscious consumers, we help customers replace fossil-based materials with low-carbon, renewable and recyclable alternatives for their food and drink, pharmaceutical or transport packaging. A wide selection of barrier coatings enables design optimization for various demanding packaging end-uses.\nCareer for a better climate. Every day.\nAs Global Key Account Manager you will drive new business opportunities and profitable growth with new and existing brand owners & retailers and identifying multiple insights for different end-use segments internationally. Also, you will drive commercialization of new solutions, concepts, and services together with the Stora Enso team. In return you will get the opportunity to truly make an impact on how we operate. The position reports to the Head of Global Accounts in the Product & Sales Business Unit Cartonboard.\nWhat do we have to offer you?\nWith our values, “Lead and Do what’s right”, we endeavor to set an example in all aspects of our business as well as in the people area. We are agile, brave and curious. We dare to leave our comport zone, we are eager to spot business opportunities and we empower people to act.\nIn this role you will\nGrow and maintain new and existing business relationships with targeted Brand Owners and Retailers including:\nDrive growth and profitability at your accounts\nRelationship development\nValue proposition development\nGrow Stora Enso brand awareness\nPromote renewable materials as an alternative to e.g. plastics\nLead the sales process end to end from first contact, first quote to multi-year contract negotiations and in the first order.\nPlan the annual sales forecast for your accounts, monitor and action its development to achieve the Stora Enso goals\nFind new opportunities and drive qualifications for Stora Enso material to be specified by brand owners/retailers\nFind project briefing and/or new business opportunities with brand owners & retailers in close collaboration with IRD, Business Lines, Sales and Product Management and other Stora Enso functions\nBe the voice of your accounts in Stora Enso and transport this market information into the Stora Enso organization. – You add the outside perspective to our business!\nWho are we looking for?\nTo succeed in this role, we see that you have approximal 5+ years relevant working experience preferably from sales in different end-use segments in folding box industry or packaging purchasing experience at brand owners/retailers with focus on fiber-based packaging. You bring a deep understanding of Customer Relations & Market dynamics with a strong commercial mindset.\nTo meet our goals and ambitions we believe that you are as passionate as we are about creating opportunities build on them and nurture these new relationships. Having a can-do attitude is key for us going forward and to succeeding in this role.\nAdditional requirements:\nRelevant university degree or an alternative qualification\nStrong strategic capability targeting market penetration\nUphold ethical standards\nHighly self-driven\nRelationship Management\nChange adaptability\nExcellent communication & presentation skills\nWillingness to travel\nAdditional Information\nPlease submit your application in English via our recruitment system latest by December 15th, 2023.\nQuestions regarding the position can be directed to hiring manager Sabine Hornischer,\nsabine.hornischer@storaenso.com\n. Any other questions can be directed to People & Culture Advisor Christian Sperling at\nChristian.Sperling@storaenso.com\n.\nGoing forward we’re implementing a hybrid work model meaning that this role can be based in any location where Stora Enso operates and/or from home office.", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 42, 43, 76255), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
