{'job_title_name': 'Environmental/ Sustainability Engineer', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Mercury Engineering', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Mercury-Engineering-7?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhad60ovikpf801&fromjk=b4d2b04f4989ba83', 'city': 'Frankfurt am Main', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 2, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=b4d2b04f4989ba83&bb=5ZPnWC31O8Xekme-YSmbTljxIptOlat0qX-56IN29BOAgE5uDZSBHzpVG8SSXnN1E4SxQqy2q21M3vepqFq_SDemMq6r6LimyfwuvMsfGFc%3D&xkcb=SoA267M3HqSebZw3lR0LbzkdCdPP&fccid=d889b09717aea6da&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circular%20Economy&l=Deutschland&filter=0&start=10', 'job_description': 'Organisational Environment:\nMercury is the European leader in construction solutions.\nWe build and manage complex engineering & construction projects for the world’s leading corporations. Our solutions help deliver technologies and life changing advancements that connect people, communities and businesses, giving them the power to achieve incredible things. Our people have the courage to be innovative. Their determination and sharp focus enable us to deliver with certainty, time and time again.\nWe deliver our clients’ visions through leading edge construction solutions across multiple sectors, including: Enterprise Data Centres, Advanced Technology & Life Sciences, Hyperscale Data Centres, Fire Protection, and Technical Support Services (TSS).\nAt Mercury, it is our duty to encourage and back our people to realise their vision of themselves. We place them at the heart of what we do, providing challenging opportunities to develop within a great team in a supportive environment that allows them to reach their full potential.\nRole Responsibilities:\nSustainable products,\nCorporate sustainability strategies,\nLife Cycle Assessments,\nWhole Life Carbon Assessment\nEnvironmental certification,\nZero carbon buildings,\nEnergy Performance modelling,\nPlanning & Compliance advice\nHandover and aftercare,\nWELL Building Standard certification,\nBREEAM certification,\nLEED certification\nKnowledge and background\nA solid understanding of building structures, envelope design, and energy efficiency.\nPrevious BIM design experience a plus\nEnvironmental/sustainability degree or qualifications a plus\nUnderstands carbon emissions, GHG emissions, embodied carbon and how they relate to the construction industry\nHas a high-level understanding of the UN SDGs and reporting frameworks like GRI\nHave a good understanding of recycling, re-use of materials and the circular economy principle\nFamiliar with / certified in LEED, LEAN methodology\nSkills and competencies\nStrong analytical skills\nExcellent business writing skills\nGood interpersonal skills\nResilient – able to maintain productivity under pressure, deadlines\nExcellent English language skills – verbal and writing\nSelf-driven and able to keep momentum on projects and agreed deliverables\nTakes pride in delivering quality outcomes – grammar, spelling and general consistency in format of documents/presentations delivered\nGood attention to detail and ability to complete compliance forms and questions in an accurate and complete way\nAble to manage several different initiatives underway within his/her span of responsibilities\nEducation:\nDegree in engineering or sustainability\n2 – 3 years of experience in sustainability or general business support\nMercury is an equal opportunities employer', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 42, 43, 494971), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_1'}
