{'job_title_name': 'Business Development Intern / Working Student (f/m/d)', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'NORNORM', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Nornorm?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhadgk6pjkuq800&fromjk=095279050dc7cdf1', 'city': 'Berlin', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 1, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=095279050dc7cdf1&bb=gn6iqSVem9CgYkU_Lbv2tCpejy2gtDKmf7ptXzoMZDpc1FuvfJpPVwm5SUmcSzXLL3-Dc1pFvwaKDUnixZ_vfCR-rJ38nTJlheC8m3Hj8gE%3D&xkcb=SoCI67M3HqR_lCw3lR0HbzkdCdPP&fccid=cd8d7d6bd1227a91&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=0', 'job_description': 'We’ve taken on a great challenge:\nTo reinvent the office furniture industry.\nOur vision:\nIntegrate circularity into the workplace of the future and demonstrate how it can benefit individuals, design, business practices, and the environment.\nHow we will achieve this:\nOur fully integrated service covers everything from initial workspace design, installation, adapting layouts, to the repair and replacement of all our "better-than-new" pieces. All this to ensure a workspace continuously maximises its impact without compromising on its benefits for people, business, or the planet.\nWho we are:\nNORNORM is an early stage start-up with backing from one of the largest players in the furnishing industry. We are developing a sustainable and subscription-based solution for furnishing future workplaces and have started rolling out our service across Europe. We have offices in Copenhagen, Amsterdam, Stockholm, and Berlin.\nWe are looking for:\nAmbitious and flexible candidates that want to grow with us and are not afraid to explore the outer edges of their capabilities. In return, we offer a fast-paced environment where initiative and willingness to take risk are encouraged and supported. Come and join our growth journey!\nThe role\nWe are looking for several interns and working students (f/m/d) to support our Business Development team in Berlin.\nYour main responsibilities include:\nIdentify prospects & contact leads: Reach out to potential customers, pitch the NORNORM concept, and understand what the customer really needs\nSupport managing our sales funnel: Support the entire sales funnel, from first contact to qualification, follow-up, and deal closing\nConduct desktop research: Help us find, approach, and win the most interesting market segments and leads\nYou bring the following qualifications:\nYou are willing to work in a fast-paced environment and use your problem-solving skills when facing challenges. You enjoy learning about prospects and customers, and find innovative ways of engaging with them to drive sales. In addition, we value the following competencies:\nA can-do mentality\nWell organized and a strong sense of ownership\nExcellent communication skills\nPersistence and a positive attitude\nAbility to work methodically and meet deadlines\nNative German speaker, fluent in English\nIdeally based in Berlin\nExperience with selling services and/or enterprise sales is a plus\nWhat we offer you:\nResponsiblity from Day 1 in an ambitious & sustainable high-growth start-up\nAccess to our modern office in the heart of Berlin (close to Berlin Central Station), work from home as needed\nAn experienced and truly diverse team (serial entrepreneurs, furnishing industry experts, sales rockstars, former management consultants)\nOccasional, need-based business trips to our international locations for training sessions and company events\nCompetitive compensation package\nFor interns, this is a full-time position for at least 12 weeks. For working students, this position requires a minimum commitment of 15-20 hours per week over a period of at least 6 months.\nIf you are driven, determined and want to grow within an exciting startup, this role is for you. Come and join us!\nDepartment\nCustomer Engagement\nLocations\nBerlin\nRemote status\nHybrid\nContact Ida Marie Hagen HR Operations Specialist – People & Finance\nBerlin', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 48, 31, 97599), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
