from experience in turnarounds and projects\nTakes the project manager role when major system changes are needed to ensure compliance to external and internal standard related to contractor safety\nMembership in the site Emergency Management Team\nQualifications\nMaster's degree in safety engineering or a comparable discipline\nAt least 3 years of work experience in projects and / or Turnarounds within the chemical or petrochemical industry\nTraining as safety officer (Sicherheitsfachkraft gemäß ArbSichG)\nKnowledge of IT Tools Impact, Investigation tools\nFluency in German and English, written and spoken\nStrong analytical thinking. Creating new and better ways for the organization to be successful. Uses lateral thinking. Questions the status quo.\nBuilding partnerships and working collaboratively with others to meet shared objectives, within and across functions.\nStrong and effective communication skills\nWhat makes us attractive – your perspectives?\nWe offer attractive salary package, company social benefits and mobile working.\nWe encourage decisions and reward results.\nWe believe in the power of many - with continuous improvement we build successful teams.\nWe want to appeal to everyone – Diversity, Equity & Inclusion\nInterested ?\nRegister your CV and apply via our online portal by clicking on the “apply” button.\nLyondellBasell\n(NYSE: LYB): As a leader in the global chemical industry, LyondellBasell strives every day to be the safest, best operated and most valued company in our industry. The company’s products, materials and technologies are advancing sustainable solutions for food safety, access to clean water, healthcare and fuel efficiency in more than 100 international markets. LyondellBasell places high priority on diversity, equity and inclusion and is Advancing Good with an emphasis on our planet, the communities where we operate and our future workforce. The company takes great pride in its world-class technology and customer focus. LyondellBasell has stepped up its circularity and climate ambitions and actions to address the global challenges of plastic waste and decarbonization. For more information, please visit www.lyondellbasell.com or follow @LyondellBasell on LinkedIn.", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 48, 32, 249462), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
