{'job_title_name': '(Senior) Data Scientist (m/f/x)', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'rebuy', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Rebuy-4?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhadgrer2cj4000&fromjk=30e3bcea6513198d', 'city': None, 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 5, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=30e3bcea6513198d&bb=J36KhxfwfwFM6CAxUjVQcFqaMLZ5p5aNlAhQA_AFwagbyYC_3V1hn0Kx9dTnkuG8&xkcb=SoBw67M3HqR_iAWQ5B0IbzkdCdPP&fccid=ff7fa90cb7b1e843&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=40', 'job_description': "About us\nReady to become part of the most important mission on this planet? We are rebuy, pioneers in the sustainable reuse of electronics and media. and we are looking for you! Our mission: to make circular living accessible to all, one transaction at a time. By giving products a second chance, we reduce resource consumption and avoid unnecessary e-waste.\nOur team of 600 comes from all corners of the world; we drive things forward collaboratively, take personal responsibility, value positive critical thinking, and persistently serve our customers and planet.\nOur Data Team\nJoin our central Data Science & Analytics team, composed of a diverse group of talented Data Scientists, Data Analysts, and Data Architects. We are actively seeking an exceptional individual to fill the role of Data Scientist or Senior Data Scientist (depends on your experience and performance in the hiring process)\nAs a crucial member of our team, you will possess the unique ability to transform massive datasets into actionable insights that drive real-world impact. Your expertise will extend beyond technical skills, encompassing critical thinking, objectivity, and pragmatic data wrangling abilities. This is a high impact role in a new working environment - you’ll be excited, rather than daunted by that. By translating your findings into compelling narratives, you will influence stakeholders and drive evidence-based decision-making.\nResponsibilities\nCollaborate closely with cross-functional teams to identify and implement data-driven solutions that drive business growth and optimization\nApply advanced statistical and machine learning techniques to extract actionable insights from complex datasets\nDevelop and deploy cutting-edge algorithms and models to solve challenging business problems, with a focus on pricing optimization, sales forecasting & process improvements, and marketing effectiveness\nTake ownership of end-to-end project execution, from data preprocessing and feature engineering to model development, validation, and deployment\nCommunicate findings and recommendations effectively to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, influencing decision-making processes\nQualifications:\nEligibility to work in Germany\nMore than 3 years of experience in Data Science or similar fields\nA degree in Statistics, Mathematics, Computer Science or another quantitative field\nExtensive experience in applying statistical modelling, machine learning, and data mining techniques to solve real-world problems\nExpertise in SQL and experience of working with large data sets\nStrong proficiency in Python, with hands-on experience in implementing machine learning algorithms.\nProven experience in deploying end-to-end machine learning pipelines, including live product deployment, monitoring, and quality assurance\nExperience working with large-scale datasets and distributed computing frameworks such as Hadoop, Spark, or AWS\nStrong problem-solving abilities, with a creative and innovative mindset to tackle complex and ambiguous challenges\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills in English\nLocation\nBerlin\nHO\nRemote within Germany\nWhat you'll receive in return\nA stimulating and innovative work environment that encourages creativity, experimentation, and professional growth\nThe opportunity to work on high-impact projects that have the potential to shape our business and industry\nCollaborative and supportive teamwork with access to mentorship from experienced Data Scientists and industry experts\nExposure to cutting-edge tools, technologies, and methodologies in the field of data science.\nCompetitive compensation package\nOur company culture, perks, and benefits\nWork with a friendly team that is passionate about circularity and wants to make the world a little more sustainable, one transaction at a time.\nFeel comfortable in an environment where independence and new ideas are welcome.\nBenefit from flat hierarchies and the greatest possible transparency so that things don't take longer than they have to and you always feel well informed.\nEnjoy our centrally located office in Berlin (Erkelenzdamm 11 - 13, 10999 Berlin).\nBenefit from our family-friendly, flexible environment and paid child sick leave.\nBring your dog to the office: we love animals and want to cuddle yours, too!\nUse employee discounts on rebuy.de, sustainable products at Futurebens, offers for sustainable micro-mobility and massages directly in our office.\nDesign your own benefits mix on our benefits portal worth EUR 50 net per month.\nHave fun at our legendary team and company events.\nUse our mental health offers as part of a cooperation with the Fürstenberg Institute.\nTake care of your work-life balance with 30 vacation days.\nAt rebuy all people are welcome and supported! We would like to talk, regardless of age, disability, national and social origin, skin color, religion, gender identity and sexual orientation. Just be who you are!", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 48, 49, 784556), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
