{'job_title_name': 'SENIOR PROGRAM MANAGER (M/W/D)', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'The DO School', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/The-Do-School?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhadh8ahk6ot801&fromjk=7957b9ab26e7799f', 'city': 'Berlin', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 5, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=7957b9ab26e7799f&bb=bravfuniWCmUWl2tPlIXT57o6ouJiNWUfS7QBzv1xB57szOzRbQxil4jj2ebMaUl&xkcb=SoBB67M3HqR_iBWQ5B0DbzkdCdPP&fccid=f7ba7751e9f5b0c1&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=40', 'job_description': 'Based in Berlin (hybrid work model), full-time\nStarting immediately\nABOUT THE ROLE\nAs a\nSenior Program Manager\n, you will lead project team(s) and will act as the main connector between The DO Catalyst and our partners with responsibility for project with a focus on ESG and circularity topics and overall stakeholder management.\nYou would\nown…\nProject leadership\nfor specific projects with a focus on ESG and circularity topics throughout the project lifecycle, accountable for quality and on-time/ in-budget execution and outcome delivery\nExternal Stakeholder management\nand act as link between The DO Catalyst team, the partner team, the wider organization and external experts, supported by a DO Catalyst Director when managing senior partner stakeholders\nProject team leadership\nincluding coordinating, leading and supporting internal project teams in an agile team set up\nSenior Content expertise\nin projects, including being an expert speaker, leading/implementing specialized work streams as part of larger projects as well as internal and external knowledge capture/training beyond projects\n… and\nsupport\nPartner development and proposals\nfor existing and new partnerships with corporate and non-corporate partners for joint programs\nData and knowledge capture\nof all stakeholder & project information as well as programmatic content, methods and tools.\nYou will\nwork closely\nwith the…\nDO Catalyst Directors\nDO Catalyst Team members on projects\nExternal business stakeholders\nProgram comms team\nThis is what you can expect…\nIn the first month\n, you will complete your onboarding, learn the nuts & bolts of The DO Catalyst program(s) that you will manage, get to know the team and establish working relationships with our external partners.\nAfter three months,\nyou will have taken over the program and stakeholder management for your program(s) and started to run the internal regular meetings. Moreover, you then have become the main contact point for team members, are in process of establishing the internal and external routines that allow you to run the project and establishing yourself as key contact for our partner.\nAfter six months,\nyou will have established a smooth workflow between stakeholders and will be in full swing designing, managing and delivering projects with guidance and in collaboration with your team and will have taken a more active role towards the partners\nAfter one year\n, you will be fully at ease in your role as program manager, Moreover, you will have taken on the primary contact role with partners and be responsible for management and delivery with strategic guidance from a DO Catalyst Director.\nABOUT YOU\nTo thrive and grow in this role,\nyou will likely be:\nBeen a\nproject or program manager\nin multi-stakeholder, complex projects and led teams\nwith responsibility for budget and a team\nExperience in change management,\norganizational development, training or innovation (topics e.g., innovation, transformation,\nESG, circularity,\nDEI, etc.)\nA people person\n, able to manage upwards and establish a productive working atmosphere and good relationships with a wide range of people. Able to inspire others, create structures and hold spaces in a fast paced environment\nStructured\nand able to pull various strands together into a coherent and efficient project plan & rollout, yet flexible to adapt to shifting circumstances and priorities\nDiligent and proactive\nabout workflow implementation, internal communication and alignment, documentation and progress, time, and budget tracking\nA clear communicator\nboth, in your day-to-day communication and in the production of written materials geared at different types of audiences. Able to communicate vision and strategy to different stakeholders and to communicate the story behind brands and organizations\nA strong facilitator and relationship builder, able to mediate and build trust one-on-one and in groups\nFluent in English and German\n(verbal and written)\n… And\nwill likely have\n:\nManaged a wide range of stakeholders, from project teams to C-level executives\nWorked in large, complex organizations and fast-paced and international environments\nFacilitated online and offline workshops and trainings\nIdeally, you might also have\nexperience in\n…\nCo-creation projects involving internal and external stakeholders\nInformal leadership and the ability to drive co-creation teams on the partners side\nDifferent methods and models of communication, coaching and design\nThis profile draws on our experience with people who have been successful in this role in the past. We warmly encourage you to apply if you feel your experience and skills equip you for this job but are not listed here!\nTHE\nDO\nAt the award-winning\nDO School\n, we unlock the potential of your people — turning teams and individuals into the drivers of your future success.\nAccelerate and sustain the change that will make your organization successful in tomorrow’s economy with\nThe DO Catalyst\n.\nThe DO is an inclusive organization\nand explicitly welcomes applicants from diverse backgrounds, whether that’s ethnicity, religion, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, disability or alternative professional paths.\nWhy join The DO?\nWe are a purposeful organization with a global reach working to make an impact, where purpose, passion and your ideas matter.\nYou will work with an entrepreneurial, creative and international team as well as a global community of purposeful DOers from over 100 countries\nWe offer a competitive salary, benefits, team-building activities, professional development opportunities and flexible and remote work modalities.\nIs this the role for you? Then please submit your application.\nApplications will be reviewed on a rolling basis.\nIf you have any questions, please email us on: career@thedo.world', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 48, 54, 654821), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
