{'job_title_name': 'SENIOR PROJECT MANAGER TEAMSPORT', 'job_type': 'Teilzeit, Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'PUMA', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Puma?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhadhenek6po800&fromjk=9ced38df62c298f7', 'city': '91074 Herzogenaurach', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 2, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=9ced38df62c298f7&bb=jcvgBJC2Fgw_f0h9z4_KE9E1YU8XcCA6PkslQ_iHU6v54tFeNYVmbjK0yUUbkckg9F163-Zck-EI6SzhhSJdmXUsoZdxLzuETxttpX0dJak%3D&xkcb=SoCo67M3HqTKTv2Q6Z0NbzkdCdPP&fccid=2f6f2e23480ffded&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=10', 'job_description': 'SPEED & SPIRIT is what we look for in our candidates, defined by some simple values that inspire us to BE DRIVEN in our performance, BE VIBRANT in our sporting legacy, BE TOGETHER in our team spirit, and BE YOU to let our individual talent and experience shine. Applying for a job at PUMA is easy. Simply click APPLY ONLINE and follow the steps to upload your application.\nYOUR TALENT\nUniversity degree in Business administration, Sports Management and/or relevant field of study\nAt least 5+ years of work experience in a relevant department such as project management, business administration, business development, market research, sustainability or brand management\nProfund experience and expertise in managing complex projects and processes across different channels and in a collaborative and international environment with various stakeholders\nStrong business acumen and excellent analytical skills\nAbility to see the bigger picture from start to finish in the commercial process\nOpen minded, flexible, open to travel and working in a multi-cultural environment\nExcellent knowledge of Microsoft Office, especially Excel and PowerPoint\nExcellent English language skills, further language skills are a plus\nExperience in the fashion, athletic/apparel industry and understanding of the product development process are a plus\nThis opportunity will be available in full time or part time\nYOUR MISSION\nLead and drive cross-functional projects of strategic focus topics for the Business Unit Teamsport such as sustainability/circularity, women’s, digitalization, social responsibility, market research and consumer insights\nBuild and inspire cross-functional project teams with passion and clear project management tools\nBuild business plans for new business opportunities in relevant and unexploited areas such as metaverse/web3\nSupport the Head of Business Development Teamsport in the process of preparing and taking strategic business decisions\nLead in depth market research and consumer insights process with external agencies, present results to relevant stakeholders and ensure consideration for strategic business decisions\nBuild strong partnerships with PUMA key markets and functions and provide support with relevant data, tools, and strategic guidance\nFurther develop agile project management principles in the Business Unit and execute them in projects with various stakeholders\nPUMA provides equal opportunities for all job applicants, regardless of race, color, religion, national origin, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, or disability. Equality for all is one of the core principles at PUMA and we do not tolerate any form of harassment or discrimination.\nPUMA supports over 16,100 employees across 120+ countries. The PUMA Group owns the brand PUMA, Cobra Golf and stichd, and is headquartered in Herzogenaurach, Germany.', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 48, 58, 248841), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
