{'job_title_name': 'Regional Tunnel Manager', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'Etex Group', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Etex-5?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhadhfodjqun800&fromjk=23e1865cb151039d', 'city': 'Ratingen', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 2, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=23e1865cb151039d&bb=jcvgBJC2Fgw_f0h9z4_KE71usUknd1-TK-nG0dqKeRdL2mPOB7ygyXcgPUKNHuC5PRXiMj-bVoQ6lvfBsIy4mwL7hBOyHUKFYMvJxYNJ6nE%3D&xkcb=SoAc67M3HqTKTv2Q6Z0MbzkdCdPP&fccid=2eb22b927a552a81&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=10', 'job_description': 'An introduction to Etex\nAt Etex, our purpose is to inspire new ways of living. By joining Etex, you won’t just be joining an international leader, you will inspire people around the world to build living spaces that are ever safer, more sustainable, smarter and beautiful. You’ll be joining a company who wants to inspire change.\nWe are committed to making a positive human impact on the world. In return, we’ll reward you by investing in your development and your personal well-being. Whilst our core values help us develop those effective and sustainable lightweight solutions we’re known for, it’s our people that matter most!\nOur diverse and inclusive workforce always strives for excellence. We have over 100 years of experience manufacturing high-performance building solutions. Etex is a company that is committed to success - and when you join us, we’ll be committed to you.\nAbout the role\nAs\nRegional Tunnel Manager\nyou will be responsible for sales of fire protection to tunnel projects in Central Eastern Europe, DACH and Nordics. The countries you are responsible is defined or redefined based on the skill levels, language advantages and primary based on the project pipe line.\nYou responsibilities will include:\nConducting thorough market research to identify potential clients, projects, and emerging trends within the tunnelling industry.\nAnalysing competitor activities and market conditions to refine sales approaches\nCultivating and maintaining strong relationships with existing clients to ensure customer satisfaction and retention.\nIdentifying and engaging new business opportunities by networking and attending industry conferences and events.\nCollaborating with cross-functional teams, including engineering, operations, and marketing, to ensure seamless project execution and customer satisfaction.\nGenerating favourable project specifications through the network of tunnel engineers\nPreparation of sales proposals, ensuring they align with client requirements and company capabilities.\nLeading negotiations to secure contracts, ensuring favourable terms and conditions for both parties\nReporting the progress and record them in One CRM.\nAbout you\nAs Regional Tunnel Manager, you will play a pivotal role in driving revenue growth and market share within your designated region. You will be responsible for establishing and nurturing relationships with key stakeholders, including contractors, engineering firms, government agencies, and other industry partners. This role requires a dynamic individual with a proven track record in sales, a deep understanding of the tunnelling industry, and excellent leadership skills.\nYou should have graduated from engineering, fire engineering, structural engineering or tunnelling studies.\nIt is essential you have an engineering and/or construction sales background.\nWe expect yoy have an experience in project sales (tunnel related or infrastructure project experience added advantage).\nYou are ready to travel extensively as the role will cover multiple countries.\nBenefits of working at Etex\nOur Social Responsibilities\nEtex has a clear commitment to help build a better, sustainable future. We work towards this vision by caring about our social and environmental impacts and working on innovative solutions for the building industry.\nOur ambition is to reduce negative effects and scale up positive impacts. We prioritise decarbonisation, including the use of renewable energy, as well as circularity, with a first focus on waste management.\nWe engage in a wide range of voluntary initiatives which offer support to local communities through partnerships and social projects. Our teammates know their local communities best, we are proud of the numerous projects and actions initiated around the world that are based on the awareness of their communities’ needs.\nCommitment to diversity\nWe’re incredibly proud of the community we’ve created at Etex. We form a global team of over 13,500 individuals from an enormous variety of backgrounds, races, faiths, and genders. Our diversity is our strength, and we are committed to ensuring that all of our teammates feel included and happy at work.\nIf you require any additional support with your application, please do not hesitate to get in touch so that we can make arrangements for you.\nGood luck with your application\nAs you have seen, our Teammates mean the world to us, they enable us to Inspire Ways of Living. If this role appeals to you, click apply now and discover how a career at Etex will help you learn, grow and lead. We look forward to hearing from you.', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 48, 59, 280534), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
