{'job_title_name': 'Intern Business Development & Communications', 'job_type': 'Vollzeit', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'numi.circular', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Numi.circular?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhadhgasjksj800&fromjk=294e426b6e26d6e4', 'city': ' München', 'remote': 'Zum Teil im Homeoffice', 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 2, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=294e426b6e26d6e4&bb=jcvgBJC2Fgw_f0h9z4_KE5OdRDYXjAP_Vgx9umHyr-IzdMak8Pp109oHXgv33fcWEdmjb0wjCazmuzSch-TmhtKpopmj26iwpr4w54NKjNQ%3D&xkcb=SoBo67M3HqTKTv2Q6Z0AbzkdCdPP&fccid=61edf65da63e8490&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=10', 'job_description': "Join the circular revolution with\nnumi.\n, an early-stage impact startup that's reshaping the future of sustainable commerce. We provide a SaaS solution empowering businesses in the consumer goods sector to effortlessly launch their own circular trade-in programs. But our software does way more than that, as it offers full transparency throughout the entire product lifecycle. By connecting with our network of recovery partners—be it resellers, refurbishers, remanufacturers, or recyclers—clients can easily track and optimise every step of the downstream value chain. Dive into a world where technology meets sustainability, and be a part of our mission.\nWe are currently\nEXIST-funded\nand are looking for a passionate team member, that is ready to drive change with us! We offer a position for an\ncompulsory internship for at least 4 months\n.\nYour Responsibilities\nAssist in product development by conducting research in the domains of circular economy, reverse logistics, and impact assessment\nHelp to improve our product by translating your insights into relevant features and data analytics\nExpand our partner network by sourcing and winning new resellers, refurbishers, remanufacturers and recyclers\nDevelop sales materials tailored to our primary target audiences\nConduct client calls alongside our Co-Founder Andrea and support in our sales process\nHelp to push our visibility by supporting content creation for our Linkedin company page and organizing further media activities (podcasts, articles)\nCoordinate our participation in various events and trade shows for the autumn/winter season, such as ISPO in November\nYour Profile\nCurrently enrolled in a bachelor's program (minimum 5th semester) or a master's program\nAcademic background or professional experience in one or more of the following areas: Economics, Business Development, Sustainability Management, Product Management\nVery good German and English language skills\nA passion for innovative solutions and good understanding of circular economy\nExperience with impact measurement and impact metrics are a plus\nA proactive, hands-on approach complemented by creative problem-solving skills\nWillingness to take responsibility and drive your own projects within the company\nWhat you’ll get\nExperience the early steps of an impact startup\nLearn first-hand about entrepreneurial challenges and the development of a tech product\nBe part of a passionate team that aims to accelerate the circular transformation\nEnjoy a flexible work environment that supports both remote work and team days in our great office in the heart of Munich\nCollaborate closely with the founders, fostering mutual learning and growth\nBenefit from our excellent network in the innovation, startup and circularity scene\nSetting\nType: Compulsory Internship (Pflichtpraktikum)\nStart: October/November 2023\nDuration: min. 4 months Full-Time\nWorking mode: Hybrid (remote, with 2 office days per week)\nHow to Apply\nApply by sending your CV along with a short yet impactful motivation text (5-6 sentences max) to Andrea at andrea.schneller@numicircular.com\nIf you have any questions, feel free to reach out to us anytime!\nFor a deeper dive into our company culture and latest updates, follow us on Linkedin https://www.linkedin.com/company/numi-circular/", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 48, 59, 785519), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
