{'job_title_name': 'Sustainability Manager Footwear (m/f/d)', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'JACK WOLFSKIN Retail GmbH', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Jack-Wolfskin?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhadhhtojkv5801&fromjk=7cb8602ce9ef6602', 'city': ' Idstein', 'remote': 'Zum Teil im Homeoffice', 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 2, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=7cb8602ce9ef6602&bb=jcvgBJC2Fgw_f0h9z4_KE0ucDFrMNIxUgdXggmLB4uqfJvH_Bpf-PAD2jt6R_Ff97X6WhfITc3gQZdtikmf8vrU8UaKumM8henKVKJyji3U%3D&xkcb=SoC767M3HqTKTv2Q6Z0JbzkdCdPP&fccid=e0fa95c985ee1704&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=10', 'job_description': 'We Live to Discover\nJack Wolfskin lives to discover and encourages people to go on new outdoor adventures, connecting with nature and rewilding themselves. Through sustainable German engineered apparel, footwear and equipment that protects and inspires, we enable everyone to experience more moments of outdoor discovery. Our success is based on a shared wanderlust and the collective input from our team of free spirits, forward thinkers and discoverers. Sharing the same values, we focus on having a positive impact through product innovations, more sustainable solutions and business practices as well as advocacy programs.\nWe encourage an open forum of ideas throughout all departments and honor collaborative discoverers who lead by introducing new paths. A career with Jack Wolfskin is anything but ordinary.\nCome on forward with us!\nWe are looking for you in our Headquarters in\nIdstei\nn\nas a\nSustainability\nManager Footwear\n(m/f/d)\n.\nThe story begins\nProject coordination and planning with the various stakeholders involved in the company e.g. Corporate Carbon Footprint, Science Based Targets, Circularity projects\nOrganisation of chemical product tests in cooperation with colleagues in Asia: Random test, USA test and if necessary, material tests\nSupport in the preparation of risk analyses of suppliers\nCommunication with suppliers on various sustainability issues in cooperation with our international teams\nYour proven path\nHigh project management and communication skills, also in an international and intercultural environment\nExperience in the sustainability field - particularly within the textile, footwear, or apparel industry, is required\nIdeally previous knowledge of certification systems in the footwear industry and in pollutant management\nIndependent, organised and structured working style\nHighly loyal, committed, flexible, and a team player\nConfident and clear communication in German and English\nWe are an outdoor gear company and we act like it\nAn international working environment and a sustainable and responsible company in all areas\nWe combine flexible working hours and hybrid working with modern workplaces and a casual dress code\nIn a sporty, familiar and continuously developing environment, success is just an important factor for us, as well as the balance offered by sports activities in our own gym and in nature, a membership in eGYM and Likeminded\nIn addition, we offer bike leasing, free coffee, tea and water, employee discounts and team events that you will remember with pleasure\nWant to join us?\nJoin us and apply online at our career portal, stating your desired salary and earliest start date.\nJob Details\nTitle\nSustainability Manager Footwear (m/f/d)\nArea of activity\nGlobal Product Development\nLocation\nIdstein (Headquarter)\nEntry level\nProfessionals\nStart date\nas soon as possible\nContract type\nUnlimited', 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 49, 1, 508174), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
