{'job_title_name': 'Process Manager (m/f/d) Spare Parts with focus on Circularity', 'job_type': '', 'shift_and_schedule': '', 'company_name': 'HILTI', 'company_indeed_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/cmp/Hilti-Group-4?campaignid=mobvjcmp&from=mobviewjob&tk=1hhadhi37jksj800&fromjk=e9a064895d1e3b58', 'city': 'Bebra', 'remote': None, 'salary': None, 'crawled_page_rank': 2, 'job_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/rc/clk?jk=e9a064895d1e3b58&bb=jcvgBJC2Fgw_f0h9z4_KEwB8CQbRLxQnvHkVsaGRewYA7NDVdMhXJ5MKv_CzX8XSz9RGv2V6kfpIH6QHqeQkRfUpM_CxHv2h122Zp69KE3Y%3D&xkcb=SoAP67M3HqTKTv2Q6Z0IbzkdCdPP&fccid=9a992a33fec815f4&vjs=3', 'listing_page_url': 'https://de.indeed.com/jobs?q=Circularity&l=Deutschland&filter=0&vjk=17f1151bb19093cb&start=10', 'job_description': "What's the role?\nAs Process Manager (m/f/d) you will assume central responsibility for the whole process development for all spare parts supply and circularity processes used for Hilti tools worldwide to deliver the Hilti sustainability strategy. This includes close contact with our tool repair service for our customers as well as handling global logistics projects in the field of aftermarket and circularity services.\nWho is Hilti?\nHilti is where innovation is improving productivity, safety and sustainability in the global construction industry, and beyond. Where strong customer relationships are creating solutions that build a better future. Where there is pride and a sense of belonging across our 120 locations, carrying right into our lives and homes. Where people are exploring possibilities, leveraging their potential, owning their personal development and growing lasting careers.\nWhat does the role involve?\nImprovement of the end-to-end supply chain for the material-management, warehouse and transport logistics along the 2 tier distribution centres to the repair/service centres\nResponsibility for all processes around our spare parts supply cross the 4 tiers form supplier/plant to the repair/service centres and back for circulatory items\nProfessional project management for spare parts supply or circulatory related projects\nPreparation, coordination and execution of SAP S/4HANA and ByD tests\nCommunication with the international service regions, global logistics and IT\nEnsure documents and processes within the IT systems conform to Hilti standards\nDefine and implement Lean standards at the global distribution centres as well as training of the relevant spare parts logistics employees onsite\nYou can build a unique network in our international and globally networked teams. We promote interdepartmental work - share your ideas!\nWhat do we offer?\nWe offer you a very thorough and transparent people and performance review process, unlike any we know of in any other business. We screen everyone in the company in a yearly career performance matching process. It means we can pair talent with opportunities - developing our people in their current roles or challenging them to work in new ways or in new places. It’s how we find the right fit and further our teams personally and professionally. People Development is even anchored in the targets of our managers.\nIn addition, we offer you innovative and personalized benefits, such as:\nFlexible working arrangements and teleworking\nEmployee share in company success\nCompany pension scheme (employer-financed)\nWhat you need is:\nTechnical or economics degree(s)\nRelevant professional experience in supply chain and logistics with commercial aspects\nExpert knowledge of multi-stream logistics and equipment service processes, in-depth knowledge of project management methods\nExperience with SAP S/4HANA, ByD and Business Warehouse in a logistics environment, material planning, transportation, warehousing and customs handling\nGood communication skills, especially being able to empathise with other cultures\nWillingness to travel worldwide\nFluent in English, further language skills are an advantage\nWhy should you apply?\nDiscover a global company where you can develop your full potential. We offer an enjoyable working environment where we embrace your commitment. Build a better future with us! For our team in Bebra we’re looking for you.\nTake up the next challenge and start your career with HILTI! We are always looking for employees for a long-term cooperation.\nDuring your job interview you will spend some time with us and get to know our company. Thus you will get a feeling for the job and our corporate culture.\nHilti stands for equal opportunities. We are looking forward to receiving applications from severely disabled persons and similarly disabled persons.\nContact: Hilti Deutschland AG | Lukas Hald | Human Resources", 'crawled_timestamp': datetime.datetime(2023, 12, 10, 18, 49, 2, 127759), 'crawler_name': 'crawler_2'}
